1
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:10,280
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

2
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:12,980
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

3
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:15,720
(Matchup for TAEYONG's Track)

4
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:16,860
(I must win.)

5
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:18,620
(We must get every single detail.)

6
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:19,820
(Team BADA and Back Koo Young)

7
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:21,490
(Because we only focused on the detail,)

8
00:00:21,490 --> 00:00:22,860
(it wasn't fun.)

9
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:24,330
(I was worried about that.)

10
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:25,900
(Meanwhile, Team NaiN and BABYZOO)

11
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,800
(It's harmonious.)

12
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,830
(Team NaiN and BABYZOO's dance is more fun.)

13
00:00:29,830 --> 00:00:31,640
(I enjoyed practicing with them more.)

14
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:33,100
(Rehearsal before filming)

15
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:34,570
(Matchup for BAILEY's Track)

16
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:36,170
(The fabric didn't rip.)

17
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:38,710
(The heels won't come off.)

18
00:00:38,710 --> 00:00:39,980
(Continuous mistakes)

19
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:41,080
(Confident of victory)

20
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:42,110
(It was full of risks.)

21
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:43,620
(They're taking off the heels too. That's funny.)

22
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:45,720
(They didn't have that before. They added it.)

23
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:46,990
(They're copying everything.)

24
00:00:46,990 --> 00:00:48,150
(Tension between the two teams continues to rise.)

25
00:00:49,590 --> 00:00:51,060
(Who did TAEYONG and BAILEY choose for their final directors?)

26
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:57,030
(Who will be the 4 choreographers on the Last Stage?)

27
00:00:57,230 --> 00:01:00,530
(You can watch their full video on "The CHOOM" and "Mnet Plus.")

28
00:01:00,530 --> 00:01:02,130
Hello, everyone. This is BADA.

29
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:04,000
Introducing my OOTD.

30
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:06,640
(Free time in Directors' Room)

31
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:07,770
What's up?

32
00:01:07,970 --> 00:01:09,110
(Way too cute)

33
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:10,310
(Spraying)

34
00:01:10,310 --> 00:01:12,410
(Cologne)

35
00:01:12,410 --> 00:01:13,810
I can't end up in the Last Stage.

36
00:01:13,810 --> 00:01:16,780
Then I won't be able to pick my family up from the airport.

37
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:17,780
(Sighing)

38
00:01:17,780 --> 00:01:19,120
(The choreographers are spending their time in their own way.)

39
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:20,390
BADA.

40
00:01:20,750 --> 00:01:22,050
(A mysterious voice echoes in the Directors' Room.)

41
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:23,560
What? What's that?

42
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:25,160
Hi, MIN JUN.

43
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:26,860
Dear Jun Hui.

44
00:01:27,130 --> 00:01:28,860
What? Who's that?

45
00:01:29,290 --> 00:01:30,660
A letter from my muse?

46
00:01:30,930 --> 00:01:32,130
- What? - What's that?

47
00:01:32,260 --> 00:01:33,500
- Hello. We're IVE. - Hello. We're IVE.

48
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:34,500
What?

49
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:35,570
(IVE out of nowhere?)

50
00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:37,600
(A video from IVE, Simeez's muse)

51
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:40,510
We met you through "I AM."

52
00:01:40,510 --> 00:01:42,410
It meant so much to us.

53
00:01:42,410 --> 00:01:44,280
We've been working together...

54
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:45,580
for many years already.

55
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:46,610
(Exclaiming)

56
00:01:46,610 --> 00:01:49,080
Your strength is...

57
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:52,880
you direct us with a lot of love.

58
00:01:53,550 --> 00:01:54,620
And...

59
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:57,390
to be honest, you're very cute.

60
00:01:57,490 --> 00:01:58,520
(Kongsuni agrees.)

61
00:01:58,690 --> 00:02:01,230
We'll look forward to seeing how cute you are...

62
00:02:01,230 --> 00:02:03,230
and how cool you are on Street World Fighter.

63
00:02:03,430 --> 00:02:04,760
Go, Simeez.

64
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:06,260
Don't come back unless you win.

65
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:07,270
- Let's say it together. - No.

66
00:02:07,270 --> 00:02:09,100
- Go, Simeez. - Let's go.

67
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:10,200
Simeez.

68
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:11,800
I'm so touched.

69
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:14,170
Oh, my gosh.

70
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:16,110
- Hello, this is TAEMIN. - It's TAEMIN.

71
00:02:16,110 --> 00:02:19,710
I often performed with Kasper,

72
00:02:19,710 --> 00:02:21,450
and he also worked on my choreography before.

73
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:24,320
I know you will inspire...

74
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:26,150
a lot of people this time.

75
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:29,220
I look forward to hearing a good result. Go, Kasper.

76
00:02:29,420 --> 00:02:30,890
Hello. I'm Young Hoon from THE BOYZ.

77
00:02:30,890 --> 00:02:32,120
I'm Hyun Jae.

78
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:35,790
When did you have them film it?

79
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:38,700
We've worked on so much with you.

80
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:40,670
Since you're not young anymore,

81
00:02:40,670 --> 00:02:42,700
you should take care of yourself.

82
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:45,100
- Watch out for your joints. - "Watch out for your joints."

83
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:46,400
- Good luck. - Good luck.

84
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:49,470
- Hello. We're izna. - Hello. We're izna.

85
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:51,240
Girls.

86
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:53,710
Our best teacher.

87
00:02:53,710 --> 00:02:55,150
- BABYZOO. - BABYZOO.

88
00:02:55,150 --> 00:02:56,310
- Good luck. - Oh, my cuties.

89
00:02:56,310 --> 00:02:57,620
- When did you film this? - I love you.

90
00:02:57,620 --> 00:02:59,220
- Oh, gosh. - Dear Jun Hui.

91
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:03,720
I know how much you've been waiting for this moment.

92
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:06,060
I know how prepared you are.

93
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:08,130
This year is yours, Jun Hui.

94
00:03:08,130 --> 00:03:09,830
It's literally all yours.

95
00:03:09,890 --> 00:03:11,400
Call me whenever you're struggling.

96
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:12,800
I love you, Jun Hui.

97
00:03:13,830 --> 00:03:16,300
(Touched)

98
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:18,140
Hey, INGYOO. You're going through a lot.

99
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:20,040
- You're going through a lot. - You're going through a lot.

100
00:03:21,140 --> 00:03:24,040
This is the level of comfort we can give to you.

101
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:26,610
- Level of comfort. - Right.

102
00:03:26,610 --> 00:03:28,750
We're out of energy because we're exhausted.

103
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:29,750
Don't misunderstand us.

104
00:03:29,750 --> 00:03:31,850
- Don't misunderstand us. - Don't misunderstand us.

105
00:03:31,850 --> 00:03:33,790
When you go to the Last Stage,

106
00:03:33,790 --> 00:03:34,890
don't look for us.

107
00:03:34,990 --> 00:03:36,120
(Laughing)

108
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:37,120
I'm sorry.

109
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:39,260
We're praying in one heart...

110
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:40,960
that you don't end up in the Last Stage.

111
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:42,990
Don't doubt yourself too much.

112
00:03:42,990 --> 00:03:44,460
Do everything you wish to do.

113
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:46,500
- Good luck, INGYOO! - Good luck!

114
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:47,930
We always...

115
00:03:47,930 --> 00:03:49,670
- root for you! - Root for you!

116
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:51,600
(Laughing)

117
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,400
- BADA! - What?

118
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,710
You're here once again.

119
00:03:54,910 --> 00:03:56,440
What?

120
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:58,640
I know you're someone...

121
00:03:58,640 --> 00:04:00,650
who can make things happen...

122
00:04:00,650 --> 00:04:01,880
wherever you are with whatever you do.

123
00:04:01,880 --> 00:04:04,150
I hope this video...

124
00:04:04,150 --> 00:04:05,650
gives you a bit of strength.

125
00:04:05,650 --> 00:04:06,780
I'm sure that you'll do well.

126
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:08,850
I'll root for you until the end, so hang in there.

127
00:04:08,850 --> 00:04:10,720
Good luck, BADA!

128
00:04:11,890 --> 00:04:13,120
- BADA! - BADA!

129
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:16,160
(The hearts of the BEBE team members)

130
00:04:18,130 --> 00:04:22,300
You must be exhausted physically and mentally.

131
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:24,200
You're someone who is more than capable.

132
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:25,740
We trust you.

133
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:27,370
You know that...

134
00:04:27,370 --> 00:04:29,540
you're the best director to us, don't you?

135
00:04:30,410 --> 00:04:33,180
We will always wait for you right here,

136
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:35,950
so make sure to come back without getting hurt.

137
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:39,150
- Let's go, BADA! - Let's go!

138
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:42,050
(Let's go, BADA!)

139
00:04:42,650 --> 00:04:44,060
That was so touching.

140
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:45,860
I directed BEBE...

141
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:48,290
and we took the trophy.

142
00:04:48,290 --> 00:04:50,460
"Could I make a name for myself as a director?"

143
00:04:50,460 --> 00:04:53,130
I felt a lot of pressure about those things.

144
00:04:53,130 --> 00:04:55,300
My babies from BEBE said,

145
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:58,400
"You're the best director to us."

146
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:00,300
(You're the best director to us, don't you?)

147
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:01,310
As soon as I heard that,

148
00:05:01,310 --> 00:05:04,540
I thought that I must've done something right as a director...

149
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:06,810
to be acknowledged by someone.

150
00:05:06,810 --> 00:05:08,510
It really gave me a lot of strength.

151
00:05:08,610 --> 00:05:10,550
- Hi, NaiN! - Hi, NaiN!

152
00:05:10,550 --> 00:05:12,220
Don't come up with these things!

153
00:05:12,220 --> 00:05:14,050
Are you doing well?

154
00:05:14,050 --> 00:05:15,920
I think she's choking up a little right now.

155
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:16,920
She's crying.

156
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:18,220
- She's going to cry now. - Is she crying?

157
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:20,060
- Her eyes are teary. - Right.

158
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:21,530
Everything else is fine.

159
00:05:21,530 --> 00:05:23,160
Please don't look down on yourself!

160
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,860
- Right! - Don't get hurt!

161
00:05:24,860 --> 00:05:26,400
You know that you're already the best, don't you?

162
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:27,470
You're already amazing.

163
00:05:27,470 --> 00:05:29,930
- I love you! - I love you so much!

164
00:05:30,870 --> 00:05:32,200
At first,

165
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:34,740
it felt like I had landed on a remote island.

166
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:36,540
It reminded me of "Street Dance Girls Fighter."

167
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:39,410
In times of difficulty, I had people to talk to.

168
00:05:39,410 --> 00:05:42,050
I had people to overcome those difficulties with.

169
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:43,050
As I was here alone,

170
00:05:43,050 --> 00:05:45,480
I kept thinking about my members.

171
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:47,450
I felt bad asking for their help.

172
00:05:47,450 --> 00:05:49,650
They had to use so much of their time...

173
00:05:49,650 --> 00:05:51,360
and had to work really hard.

174
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:55,490
But they helped me out without hesitation.

175
00:05:55,490 --> 00:05:58,300
I wondered how I could repay them.

176
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:01,730
I always feel blessed to have them by my side.

177
00:06:01,870 --> 00:06:04,300
I never have any doubts...

178
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:06,840
about you doing a good job.

179
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:08,070
Good luck, JEONG MIN JUN!

180
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:09,670
Let's do our, "Let's do this."

181
00:06:09,770 --> 00:06:12,580
- Are you ready, MIN JUN? - Are you ready?

182
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:13,580
One, two, three!

183
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:15,510
- Let's do this! - Let's do this!

184
00:06:16,650 --> 00:06:18,850
- Hi, Dad! - Hi, Dad!

185
00:06:18,950 --> 00:06:21,890
(A message from his family in Japan)

186
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:25,890
You're working hard...

187
00:06:25,890 --> 00:06:28,190
for another challenge in Korea.

188
00:06:28,190 --> 00:06:29,730
You're amazing!

189
00:06:29,730 --> 00:06:31,230
- You're amazing! - You're amazing!

190
00:06:31,530 --> 00:06:33,700
Honey, it's sad that we're not able to...

191
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:36,300
see each other often as we're far away from each other,

192
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:38,300
but I will always root for you.

193
00:06:38,300 --> 00:06:41,210
I love you, Dad!

194
00:06:41,210 --> 00:06:43,540
- I love you! - I love you!

195
00:06:43,540 --> 00:06:46,310
- I love you, Dad! - I love you!

196
00:06:46,310 --> 00:06:49,250
- I love you! - I love you!

197
00:06:49,250 --> 00:06:51,880
- Good luck, Dad! - Good luck, Dad!

198
00:06:57,090 --> 00:06:59,390
I was reminded once again...

199
00:06:59,390 --> 00:07:02,030
that putting together a great performance...

200
00:07:02,030 --> 00:07:04,030
was the way to repay my family for their support.

201
00:07:04,330 --> 00:07:06,600
(He pulls himself together with their support.)

202
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:09,400
I must work hard again.

203
00:07:09,530 --> 00:07:12,100
I'm truly blessed.

204
00:07:12,270 --> 00:07:14,440
How blessed am I...

205
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:16,140
to get this much support?

206
00:07:17,210 --> 00:07:19,010
I felt exhausted emotionally,

207
00:07:19,010 --> 00:07:21,250
and they really comforted me.

208
00:07:21,250 --> 00:07:23,380
After watching the video of support,

209
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:25,920
I think I can perform with confidence.

210
00:07:25,980 --> 00:07:27,620
I'll make it back alive...

211
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:29,190
as a strong director.

212
00:07:29,350 --> 00:07:30,390
I will claim victory!

213
00:07:30,390 --> 00:07:32,120
Thank you so much, girls!

214
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,220
My team is the best!

215
00:07:33,660 --> 00:07:35,990
(They feel energized by the support from their muses.)

216
00:07:36,230 --> 00:07:42,100
(Title sequence track: "Royalty" produced by Illmind)

217
00:08:56,770 --> 00:09:00,910
(To be continued)

218
00:09:01,010 --> 00:09:02,010
(Letting out a sigh)

219
00:09:02,380 --> 00:09:05,280
BAILEY must be mesmerized by our concept.

220
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:08,290
The main theme of the Hydra Queen...

221
00:09:08,290 --> 00:09:10,020
is that she shows more aggression with every kill.

222
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:12,860
I want them to be dressed like warriors.

223
00:09:12,860 --> 00:09:16,260
"Female warriors." I wanted an intense vibe.

224
00:09:16,260 --> 00:09:20,500
On the mood board, I went with piercings with metal bones.

225
00:09:20,500 --> 00:09:22,370
I don't want to express BAILEY as a queen.

226
00:09:22,370 --> 00:09:23,500
It's quite ugly.

227
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:25,140
It felt so cliche.

228
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:28,870
I thought of a mysterious albino snake.

229
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:31,740
This is what the outfit is like.

230
00:09:31,940 --> 00:09:34,850
We wanted a strong contrast. If BAILEY was the albino snake,

231
00:09:34,850 --> 00:09:37,320
the dancers were to put on black ink over their faces.

232
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:40,550
Creating a contrast between black and white was our goal.

233
00:09:40,750 --> 00:09:44,060
To bring the focus on BAILEY's face,

234
00:09:44,060 --> 00:09:46,120
we went with a balaclava.

235
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:49,330
We tried to avoid the focus going to something else.

236
00:09:49,330 --> 00:09:51,930
It was important for the artist to stand out.

237
00:09:51,930 --> 00:09:54,400
We went with an outfit that would stand out when moving around...

238
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:56,970
with enamel and red.

239
00:09:56,970 --> 00:09:59,840
I wanted the dancers to wear cool masks.

240
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,870
I did a lot of searching.

241
00:10:01,870 --> 00:10:03,840
Instead of coming up with something with a strategy,

242
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:06,240
we only thought about the artist.

243
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:08,510
"Let's wear Wacka Wak."

244
00:10:08,910 --> 00:10:11,250
There were many steps in the chorus part.

245
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:15,090
I wanted the lettering on the pants.

246
00:10:15,250 --> 00:10:19,220
The LED will display "Wacka Wak" like a newspaper article...

247
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:20,890
for the highlight.

248
00:10:20,890 --> 00:10:23,060
"The Wacka Wak Generation is here."

249
00:10:23,060 --> 00:10:24,730
I wanted this to be expressed in grand way.

250
00:10:24,930 --> 00:10:27,030
(The concept briefing and draft reveal ends.)

251
00:10:27,030 --> 00:10:28,230
(BAILEY is still in the meeting room.)

252
00:10:28,230 --> 00:10:30,470
I just need help, basically.

253
00:10:30,570 --> 00:10:32,270
(Who are these two who have come to help her?)

254
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:34,170
(TARZZAN and WOOCHAN of ALLDAY PROJECT)

255
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:35,910
(Reliable backup to help out with BAILEY's decision)

256
00:10:35,910 --> 00:10:37,110
(We will help you.)

257
00:10:37,310 --> 00:10:40,780
You guys know me inside out as a creative human being,

258
00:10:40,780 --> 00:10:42,680
but especially as a performance director...

259
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:43,780
and choreographer.

260
00:10:43,780 --> 00:10:47,890
So I wanted to hear your perspective on these two pieces of choreography.

261
00:10:47,890 --> 00:10:50,450
I like the MIN JUN part.

262
00:10:50,450 --> 00:10:53,560
The hand choreography he did was catchy.

263
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:56,290
I feel like I already saw that.

264
00:10:56,290 --> 00:10:58,730
It feels familiar.

265
00:10:59,060 --> 00:11:00,770
I get why they did what they did.

266
00:11:00,770 --> 00:11:02,170
- Really? - It's because...

267
00:11:02,170 --> 00:11:03,930
I worked with Kasper.

268
00:11:04,070 --> 00:11:06,200
So he knows my style. He knows my moves.

269
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:09,410
And he said, "Because this is your first solo thing,"

270
00:11:09,410 --> 00:11:11,910
"let's get that clear of who you are."

271
00:11:11,910 --> 00:11:14,780
The safe choice of what you can do well...

272
00:11:14,780 --> 00:11:16,710
is with MIN JUN and Kasper.

273
00:11:16,710 --> 00:11:17,880
But as for me,

274
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:19,880
I agree that it's of great quality.

275
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:21,750
- But from the public's perspective, - Right.

276
00:11:21,750 --> 00:11:23,620
there wasn't a part that really spoke to me.

277
00:11:23,620 --> 00:11:26,690
I wished for there to be a big impact in the chorus,

278
00:11:26,690 --> 00:11:28,060
but there wasn't anything that stood out.

279
00:11:28,060 --> 00:11:30,060
That was disappointing to me.

280
00:11:30,590 --> 00:11:31,960
But as for the one on the left,

281
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:36,000
I really liked the first concept of the red curtain.

282
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,240
- It sticks. - The material as well.

283
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:40,140
I liked how they...

284
00:11:40,140 --> 00:11:42,140
used slow-motion.

285
00:11:42,140 --> 00:11:44,740
That part was distinct.

286
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:48,080
I thought they edited it in slow motion.

287
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:49,280
- This part? - Yes.

288
00:11:49,380 --> 00:11:52,750
But in the second one, something that would worry me is...

289
00:11:52,750 --> 00:11:55,750
they want me to wear this tight outfit...

290
00:11:55,750 --> 00:11:58,560
with prickly fish-like parts.

291
00:11:58,560 --> 00:12:00,420
- These things. - Things like scales?

292
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:04,530
That ends up like a sea creature concept.

293
00:12:04,530 --> 00:12:05,530
Wearing that?

294
00:12:05,530 --> 00:12:07,230
- I don't know if that will work. - That's complicated.

295
00:12:07,230 --> 00:12:08,470
It won't be easy to look pretty or cool...

296
00:12:08,470 --> 00:12:10,270
- because she's wearing heels, too. - Right.

297
00:12:10,270 --> 00:12:12,270
- I can't pull this off then. - Right.

298
00:12:12,370 --> 00:12:14,310
Seriously. That's really important.

299
00:12:14,310 --> 00:12:16,640
A dancer's perspective? Or an artist's perspective?

300
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:18,780
These two perspectives are fighting in my mind.

301
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:22,410
My identity up until this point...

302
00:12:22,410 --> 00:12:24,880
It fits more with MIN JUN and Kasper's.

303
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:27,320
But then moving forward to now...

304
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:29,420
To where... Maybe, I'd like to take a different way.

305
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:31,690
I'd go more with Simeez and INGYOO's.

306
00:12:31,690 --> 00:12:32,890
Gosh, so hard.

307
00:12:33,490 --> 00:12:35,330
How was it for you? I'm just so curious.

308
00:12:35,330 --> 00:12:36,590
After you watched the opposing team's choreography.

309
00:12:36,590 --> 00:12:38,700
When I first watched theirs, it was just so lame.

310
00:12:38,700 --> 00:12:40,800
They added too many visual elements, and it was too much.

311
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:43,230
It was obvious that she didn't like their cocoon thing.

312
00:12:43,230 --> 00:12:44,670
I look too much like a fish.

313
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:46,700
I didn't come across as beautiful.

314
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:48,410
I was just shocked that they wanted her to do it.

315
00:12:48,570 --> 00:12:51,240
I'm like, "Why is BAILEY so torn between the two?"

316
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:52,240
(Pure curiosity)

317
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:54,980
When we compare ours to theirs, I'm sure we'll win.

318
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:58,020
Being in a cocoon versus hanging upside down.

319
00:12:58,020 --> 00:12:59,020
Hanging upside down.

320
00:12:59,020 --> 00:13:01,120
Staying in the cocoon versus getting dragged to the back.

321
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:02,150
Getting dragged to the back.

322
00:13:02,350 --> 00:13:04,490
Performing the choreography versus hatching from an egg...

323
00:13:04,490 --> 00:13:05,620
- in the pre-chorus. - That's...

324
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:06,660
(Laughing)

325
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:09,760
She looked super busy in the video.

326
00:13:09,860 --> 00:13:12,260
She's in a cocoon and breaks out from it.

327
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:13,630
She takes the microphone.

328
00:13:13,630 --> 00:13:16,170
She has to take off her heels and then throw them.

329
00:13:16,270 --> 00:13:17,270
She's too busy.

330
00:13:17,270 --> 00:13:19,600
I'm getting this feeling that BAILEY is going to hate INGYOO.

331
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:21,670
I bet she's going to have most fun when she's with us.

332
00:13:21,670 --> 00:13:23,140
It's focusing on the artistic aspect of the performance...

333
00:13:23,140 --> 00:13:24,610
versus focusing on the choreography.

334
00:13:24,710 --> 00:13:27,280
Aren't you now bored with choreography-focused performances?

335
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:29,310
When it comes to storytelling and executing the concept,

336
00:13:29,310 --> 00:13:31,220
no team on the show can beat us.

337
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:32,580
When you think of albino snakes,

338
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:34,320
you can't connect it to "can't kill me."

339
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:35,650
- Step on them, and they're dead. - Thud.

340
00:13:35,950 --> 00:13:38,590
Did you understand why the snake was hanging upside down on a tree?

341
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:42,160
Every moment of our performance was tailored to her exact taste.

342
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:43,190
That included krumping.

343
00:13:43,190 --> 00:13:44,830
Aren't you excited to watch her krump?

344
00:13:44,830 --> 00:13:46,160
It's like inviting Insooni...

345
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:47,730
and asking her to rap. Is that the right decision?

346
00:13:47,730 --> 00:13:50,030
It's like making me just nod in the choreography.

347
00:13:50,030 --> 00:13:51,340
Oh, the nodding thing?

348
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:54,210
Our choreography made BAILEY shine in the best way possible.

349
00:13:54,210 --> 00:13:57,310
They seem to be clueless about BAILEY's strengths.

350
00:13:57,310 --> 00:13:58,380
- Gosh. - We have this in the bag.

351
00:13:58,380 --> 00:13:59,640
Don't you feel confident?

352
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:00,740
(K-pop Solo Artist Direct Mission)

353
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:02,110
(The siren goes off in the Directors' Square.)

354
00:14:02,210 --> 00:14:03,410
(Hating it)

355
00:14:03,510 --> 00:14:04,620
(Used to the siren)

356
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:05,780
Let's go.

357
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:08,590
(Relaxed)

358
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:11,660
Kasper is the first one out.

359
00:14:11,660 --> 00:14:12,890
He looks so relaxed.

360
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:15,560
I can't believe that I got used to this sound.

361
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:16,560
Right?

362
00:14:16,830 --> 00:14:18,530
- How was it for you, Simeez? - What?

363
00:14:18,530 --> 00:14:19,530
How was it?

364
00:14:19,530 --> 00:14:21,800
BAILEY was incredibly good at keeping a poker face.

365
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:23,100
- Right? - She was.

366
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:25,400
- Really? - She kept a poker face.

367
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:27,400
I haven't figured her out yet.

368
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:30,310
So I'm more ambitious to do better.

369
00:14:30,310 --> 00:14:31,940
But it's not that I don't feel confident.

370
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:33,310
I wasn't nervous at all.

371
00:14:34,140 --> 00:14:35,310
(K-pop Solo Artist Direct Mission)

372
00:14:35,950 --> 00:14:38,150
(Result Announcement for Each Segment)

373
00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:39,280
(It's time.)

374
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:40,320
We're going to watch this now?

375
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:43,090
We'll watch the winning segments selected by the artist?

376
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:44,820
I wonder which team satisfied her needs.

377
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:47,320
We'll find out what she prefers through the results.

378
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:48,630
Oh, I guess they edited our videos.

379
00:14:48,630 --> 00:14:50,760
They're going to show us the draft.

380
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:52,230
Just like how it's done now.

381
00:14:52,730 --> 00:14:54,730
Each artist has compared the choreography...

382
00:14:54,730 --> 00:14:56,330
for the same segment from both teams.

383
00:14:56,900 --> 00:15:00,270
Then they selected a team with the choreography they preferred.

384
00:15:00,270 --> 00:15:02,310
Which team had...

385
00:15:02,310 --> 00:15:05,310
more of their segments chosen by the artist?

386
00:15:06,140 --> 00:15:07,950
The artist's choices will be revealed now.

387
00:15:07,950 --> 00:15:09,050
Gosh, this is going to be fun.

388
00:15:09,050 --> 00:15:10,310
Yes!

389
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:12,320
(BADA and Back Koo Young versus NaiN and BABYZOO)

390
00:15:13,020 --> 00:15:14,890
There are eight segments in the matchup for TAEYONG's track.

391
00:15:15,550 --> 00:15:17,250
As for the intro,

392
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:20,920
I thought it needed a good concept and original ideas.

393
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:23,290
We used the microphones and the lights...

394
00:15:23,290 --> 00:15:24,760
to make it look like a press conference...

395
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:25,830
which left a strong impression.

396
00:15:25,830 --> 00:15:27,930
I have no doubt that he'll pick our intro.

397
00:15:27,930 --> 00:15:29,970
I'm pretty confident that we're going to win.

398
00:15:29,970 --> 00:15:31,400
As for the intro,

399
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:34,100
we put together a series of simple, yet eye-catching movements...

400
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:35,940
and movements TAEYONG would want to try...

401
00:15:35,940 --> 00:15:37,210
and can execute well.

402
00:15:37,210 --> 00:15:39,210
That's how I can sum up our intro.

403
00:15:39,210 --> 00:15:40,810
We'll win no matter what.

404
00:15:40,810 --> 00:15:42,750
I'm definitely confident about this.

405
00:15:42,850 --> 00:15:43,850
(Section Director Back Koo Young versus Section Director BABYZOO)

406
00:15:43,850 --> 00:15:44,850
(Which intro did TAEYONG select?)

407
00:15:45,250 --> 00:15:48,220
(Choreography Video of "Wacka Wak," edited version by TAEYONG)

408
00:15:50,050 --> 00:15:51,290
(Which intro did he pick?)

409
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:55,060
(That's what I'm talking about.)

410
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:56,230
Yes.

411
00:15:56,230 --> 00:15:57,460
As soon as the intro played,

412
00:15:57,460 --> 00:15:59,000
I saw that we won the intro.

413
00:15:59,730 --> 00:16:00,860
It was unexpected.

414
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:01,970
What?

415
00:16:02,270 --> 00:16:03,500
I couldn't understand it.

416
00:16:03,500 --> 00:16:05,600
Considering the years of experience he has in this industry,

417
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:07,200
bombarding him with camera flashes...

418
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:08,770
and shoving microphones in his face...

419
00:16:08,770 --> 00:16:11,740
didn't look that appealing.

420
00:16:11,910 --> 00:16:16,410
I liked Koo Young's direction for the intro.

421
00:16:16,650 --> 00:16:19,150
It's simple, but it's full of energy.

422
00:16:19,150 --> 00:16:21,320
I appreciated starting with that energetic vibe.

423
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:24,790
I got the feeling the performance would look a bit more focused.

424
00:16:24,790 --> 00:16:26,220
I found that more interesting.

425
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:28,460
(He selected Team BADA and Koo Young for the intro.)

426
00:16:28,460 --> 00:16:30,590
(Will their segment be chosen for the intro chorus?)

427
00:16:30,590 --> 00:16:31,900
Let's keep going.

428
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,060
(Which team has won the segment for the intro chorus?)

429
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,170
(Team BADA and Koo Young wins the intro chorus as well.)

430
00:16:35,170 --> 00:16:36,170
Okay.

431
00:16:36,170 --> 00:16:38,070
(Their segments were chosen consecutively.)

432
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:40,200
I didn't expect to lose the intro chorus either.

433
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:42,410
What if we end up with zero segments of our own?

434
00:16:42,510 --> 00:16:43,740
I was nervous.

435
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:45,610
(The next segment is Verse 1.)

436
00:16:46,110 --> 00:16:48,950
(Team NaiN and BABYZOO was chosen for the 1st time for Verse 1.)

437
00:16:49,050 --> 00:16:50,110
What a relief.

438
00:16:50,110 --> 00:16:51,280
Personally,

439
00:16:51,280 --> 00:16:55,820
I prefer going all out from Verse One.

440
00:16:55,950 --> 00:16:59,120
I liked that the movements utilized my entire body.

441
00:16:59,120 --> 00:17:00,760
I thought their choreography was cool.

442
00:17:01,330 --> 00:17:03,030
(Which team has won the segment for Pre-Chorus 1?)

443
00:17:04,030 --> 00:17:06,100
(Team BADA and Koo Young wins Pre-Chorus 1 as well.)

444
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:07,100
Yes.

445
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:08,230
(Oh, yes!)

446
00:17:08,330 --> 00:17:10,070
No way. Am I seeing this right?

447
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:12,200
Is this right? Is this going to work out?

448
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:14,540
Did we take the wrong approach for this mission?

449
00:17:14,540 --> 00:17:16,770
We have to win the chorus segment.

450
00:17:16,770 --> 00:17:19,480
The chorus segment is very important because it makes the choreography...

451
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:20,880
more memorable.

452
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:24,310
The chorus segment would usually leave a strong impression.

453
00:17:24,310 --> 00:17:26,080
I was certain it would be ours 10,000 percent.

454
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:27,750
(As for the chorus segment,)

455
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:29,750
(I'd love to see it turn into a challenge.)

456
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:31,690
(Then the finger flick is the way to go.)

457
00:17:31,790 --> 00:17:32,790
(Koo Young's ambitious plan, the finger flick dance)

458
00:17:33,790 --> 00:17:36,130
Is there anyone who can't do a finger flick?

459
00:17:36,130 --> 00:17:38,160
I liked this.

460
00:17:38,430 --> 00:17:40,000
The finger flick thing was fun.

461
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:42,130
It looked like BADA was giving the backup dancers the finger flick.

462
00:17:42,130 --> 00:17:43,570
I really don't get it.

463
00:17:43,570 --> 00:17:44,940
Will the finger flick dance...

464
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:47,300
be able to take this summer by storm?

465
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:49,370
It'd look so lame if a K-pop artist does it.

466
00:17:49,370 --> 00:17:51,040
If I could vote,

467
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:53,240
I'd vote for Team NaiN and BABYZOO.

468
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:55,650
I went with swinging the hand left and right.

469
00:17:55,650 --> 00:17:57,180
I thought it was perfect for TAEYONG.

470
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:58,520
Our segment is going to win for sure.

471
00:17:58,520 --> 00:17:59,720
I'm certain about it.

472
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:02,050
(Section Director NaiN versus Section Director Koo Young)

473
00:18:02,050 --> 00:18:03,720
(Which chorus segment did the artist pick?)

474
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:05,620
(The hand swinging dance versus the finger flick dance)

475
00:18:06,790 --> 00:18:08,960
(TAEYONG chose the hand swinging dance.)

476
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:11,800
I knew it. He had to pick ours for the chorus segment.

477
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:12,930
We came up with a good one.

478
00:18:13,130 --> 00:18:14,500
I knew it.

479
00:18:14,770 --> 00:18:16,170
I found...

480
00:18:16,170 --> 00:18:18,770
NaiN's approach to the word, "wack," more interesting.

481
00:18:18,770 --> 00:18:22,670
Swinging the hand like this brought a youthful vibe in my opinion.

482
00:18:22,670 --> 00:18:24,440
I had a mental breakdown. I thought we were doomed.

483
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:26,310
We really liked our choreography,

484
00:18:26,310 --> 00:18:27,710
so we were certain ours would get picked.

485
00:18:27,710 --> 00:18:29,880
Why didn't he go with the finger flick?

486
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:31,110
I was just shocked.

487
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:33,580
Honestly, the finger flick doesn't look good.

488
00:18:33,780 --> 00:18:36,120
And my ring finger is short.

489
00:18:36,390 --> 00:18:37,750
I have a hard time doing the finger flick.

490
00:18:38,620 --> 00:18:40,060
- Two, three, four, - Hang in there.

491
00:18:40,060 --> 00:18:41,160
five, six.

492
00:18:41,590 --> 00:18:43,590
I told you, didn't I? I said I was 10,000 percent sure.

493
00:18:43,690 --> 00:18:44,800
(What about the choreography for Verse 2?)

494
00:18:45,230 --> 00:18:47,230
(He chose Team NaiN and BABYZOO for Verse 2 again.)

495
00:18:47,230 --> 00:18:48,830
We added wow factors...

496
00:18:48,830 --> 00:18:51,470
that would definitely win over TAEYONG.

497
00:18:51,470 --> 00:18:52,970
I was sure he'd like them.

498
00:18:53,070 --> 00:18:55,910
I really thought BABYZOO's composition style...

499
00:18:55,910 --> 00:18:58,310
was stylish.

500
00:18:58,310 --> 00:19:00,180
So I chose BABYZOO's segment.

501
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:02,180
(Section Director NaiN versus Section Director BADA)

502
00:19:02,180 --> 00:19:04,310
(Only Chorus 2 remains now.)

503
00:19:04,310 --> 00:19:06,720
(Here's the killing point of the choreography.)

504
00:19:06,720 --> 00:19:09,150
(When you go up and jump down,)

505
00:19:09,150 --> 00:19:11,020
(you still have this chill vibe and are having fun with it.)

506
00:19:11,020 --> 00:19:12,820
(But the dancers will keep on dancing.)

507
00:19:12,820 --> 00:19:16,190
(The contrast between you and the dancers is highlighted.)

508
00:19:16,190 --> 00:19:18,930
(The extreme contrast in the killing part)

509
00:19:19,030 --> 00:19:20,660
(In the last segment, Chorus Two,)

510
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:22,400
(you're just going to blow up.)

511
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:24,430
(You'll rock the stage.)

512
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:28,710
(The explosive energy for everyone)

513
00:19:28,810 --> 00:19:29,970
(Pondering)

514
00:19:29,970 --> 00:19:31,810
Gosh, seriously. How am I going to pick?

515
00:19:31,810 --> 00:19:33,080
(Section Director NaiN versus Section Director BADA)

516
00:19:33,080 --> 00:19:34,480
(The extreme contrast of energy and the explosive energy)

517
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:36,950
I think we can win the segment for Chorus Two.

518
00:19:36,950 --> 00:19:38,380
Our segment has to be chosen for Chorus Two.

519
00:19:38,380 --> 00:19:39,880
I was really desperate.

520
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:41,620
Our finger flick dance wasn't chosen.

521
00:19:41,620 --> 00:19:43,890
So we should win the last chorus segment.

522
00:19:43,890 --> 00:19:45,960
We couldn't win the first chorus segment.

523
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:47,890
So we must win the second chorus segment.

524
00:19:47,890 --> 00:19:49,330
(Which team won the last chorus segment?)

525
00:19:50,090 --> 00:19:52,100
(Relieved)

526
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:55,670
(He chose Team BADA and Koo Young for the last chorus segment.)

527
00:19:55,670 --> 00:19:57,030
I was a bit disappointed.

528
00:19:57,330 --> 00:19:58,600
(Disappointed)

529
00:19:58,600 --> 00:20:02,710
I liked BADA's choreography a little more.

530
00:20:02,710 --> 00:20:04,940
There's no dance break in the song. So in her version,

531
00:20:04,940 --> 00:20:07,310
she said she wanted to include a dance break.

532
00:20:07,310 --> 00:20:09,450
Her approach was more convincing.

533
00:20:09,450 --> 00:20:11,620
(Look at that.)

534
00:20:11,620 --> 00:20:12,880
(Impressed)

535
00:20:16,950 --> 00:20:19,090
(Perfectly wrapping it up)

536
00:20:19,490 --> 00:20:21,020
(Chosen Segments for TAEYONG's "Wacka Wak")

537
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:22,060
My gosh.

538
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:23,160
Yes.

539
00:20:23,590 --> 00:20:26,230
(Two teams with starkly contrasting atmospheres)

540
00:20:26,230 --> 00:20:27,560
I was really shocked to see...

541
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:29,230
that only one of my segments got chosen.

542
00:20:29,230 --> 00:20:30,770
It was embarrassing.

543
00:20:32,540 --> 00:20:34,810
What did we miss?

544
00:20:34,810 --> 00:20:36,070
Why did we end up losing?

545
00:20:36,070 --> 00:20:37,310
I couldn't stop thinking about that.

546
00:20:37,310 --> 00:20:39,280
(Team BADA and Koo Young won more segments.)

547
00:20:39,310 --> 00:20:40,740
Gosh, this is hard.

548
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:42,180
What's your take on this?

549
00:20:42,180 --> 00:20:44,680
Let me say this with caution then. I'd go with...

550
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:46,920
My gosh, Il Hyeong. Our opinions are different.

551
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,690
(They have conflicting opinions.)

552
00:20:48,790 --> 00:20:50,090
I...

553
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:53,090
(Choreography chosen by Artist TAEYONG)

554
00:20:53,090 --> 00:20:54,390
It's old generation versus new generation.

555
00:20:54,390 --> 00:20:56,690
I think TAEYONG will like Team NaiN and BABYZOO's choreography.

556
00:20:56,690 --> 00:20:59,200
He would stand out more with Team Koo Young's choreography.

557
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:01,670
Their overall performance stands out more.

558
00:21:01,970 --> 00:21:03,730
(Nervous)

559
00:21:03,730 --> 00:21:06,670
I hope he picks my team.

560
00:21:06,670 --> 00:21:07,970
And he will.

561
00:21:07,970 --> 00:21:09,440
(Exchanging eye contact)

562
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:10,510
I was confident.

563
00:21:11,040 --> 00:21:13,310
(Which team was chosen by the artist?)

564
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:16,650
(NaiN and BABYZOO)

565
00:21:16,750 --> 00:21:17,780
(Surprised)

566
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:19,420
The result didn't match.

567
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:21,920
(Despite fewer winning segments, their choreography was chosen.)

568
00:21:22,220 --> 00:21:23,950
Actually, I'd go with the first team.

569
00:21:23,950 --> 00:21:27,990
I thought there was a lot more stuff I could try with the first one.

570
00:21:27,990 --> 00:21:29,960
I'd go with the first team.

571
00:21:30,430 --> 00:21:32,230
(Choreography chosen by TAEYONG: NaiN and BABYZOO)

572
00:21:32,230 --> 00:21:35,330
He chose our choreography.

573
00:21:35,330 --> 00:21:36,600
But we won't just settle for it.

574
00:21:36,600 --> 00:21:38,570
We need to be a bit more ambitious...

575
00:21:38,570 --> 00:21:41,510
if we want to guarantee a win.

576
00:21:41,510 --> 00:21:43,010
I wasn't all that happy.

577
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:45,940
I'll keep looking for ways to revise so that we can maximize...

578
00:21:45,940 --> 00:21:47,140
our performance...

579
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:48,550
or ways to develop our choreography.

580
00:21:48,550 --> 00:21:50,050
This is just the first draft.

581
00:21:50,050 --> 00:21:52,150
The final performance will change.

582
00:21:52,150 --> 00:21:54,180
We'll do our best and pull all-nighters...

583
00:21:54,180 --> 00:21:56,720
to make our choreography the best it can be.

584
00:21:56,720 --> 00:21:58,160
Koo Young and I will make that happen.

585
00:21:58,160 --> 00:21:59,620
I was very disappointed.

586
00:21:59,620 --> 00:22:02,530
We'll be changing the choreography considering the fact that...

587
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:03,730
it'll be his official choreography.

588
00:22:03,730 --> 00:22:06,760
We need to give it our all, so it becomes the choreography...

589
00:22:06,760 --> 00:22:08,400
he can execute well.

590
00:22:08,900 --> 00:22:11,200
(Which team will be named as the final directors?)

591
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:14,240
(It's quiet in the Directors' Room.)

592
00:22:14,540 --> 00:22:15,940
Our choreography was chosen at the end.

593
00:22:15,940 --> 00:22:17,110
But...

594
00:22:17,110 --> 00:22:18,680
we didn't win a lot of the segments.

595
00:22:19,610 --> 00:22:21,080
(Segment Win-Loss Results, 5: 4)

596
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:23,580
Only four of our segments were chosen.

597
00:22:23,580 --> 00:22:27,020
I thought, "At this rate, we might end up losing."

598
00:22:27,080 --> 00:22:29,120
Things are getting serious.

599
00:22:29,120 --> 00:22:30,520
I wasn't all that happy.

600
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:33,020
What did we miss?

601
00:22:33,020 --> 00:22:34,360
Why did we end up losing?

602
00:22:36,260 --> 00:22:38,630
I really think the intro with microphones is so lame.

603
00:22:38,960 --> 00:22:41,060
Will his fans like this?

604
00:22:41,830 --> 00:22:43,200
Actually,

605
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:44,670
I was quite shocked.

606
00:22:44,670 --> 00:22:45,740
I even suspected this.

607
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:47,040
Maybe, he chose their intro...

608
00:22:47,040 --> 00:22:49,010
because he wanted to simplify the choreography.

609
00:22:49,010 --> 00:22:51,940
Their intro practically has no choreography.

610
00:22:52,040 --> 00:22:55,010
We need to think about the intro.

611
00:22:55,010 --> 00:22:56,880
I'm sure we can change our intro...

612
00:22:56,880 --> 00:22:59,050
and incorporate more wow factors.

613
00:22:59,050 --> 00:23:00,050
Let's ask him tomorrow...

614
00:23:00,050 --> 00:23:02,820
what part of our intro he wants to change.

615
00:23:02,820 --> 00:23:04,020
That's great.

616
00:23:04,020 --> 00:23:05,490
Even if his explanation is abstract,

617
00:23:05,490 --> 00:23:07,120
we'll be fine as long as we figure out his intention.

618
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:09,560
We're going to be...

619
00:23:09,560 --> 00:23:11,090
a lot more detailed with this mission.

620
00:23:11,090 --> 00:23:14,000
"He seemed to like it and chose our choreography."

621
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:15,070
Despite everything,

622
00:23:15,070 --> 00:23:17,100
I'll keep looking for ways to revise so that we can maximize...

623
00:23:17,100 --> 00:23:18,470
our performance...

624
00:23:18,470 --> 00:23:19,940
or ways to develop...

625
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:21,300
our choreography.

626
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:22,310
I want more than just a win.

627
00:23:22,310 --> 00:23:23,410
I want to win by a landslide.

628
00:23:23,410 --> 00:23:24,470
(First practice with the artist)

629
00:23:24,470 --> 00:23:26,040
I'm a bit nervous.

630
00:23:26,040 --> 00:23:27,880
- Hello. - Hello.

631
00:23:27,880 --> 00:23:28,910
What should we do?

632
00:23:28,910 --> 00:23:30,910
We have some questions for you.

633
00:23:30,910 --> 00:23:31,920
You too?

634
00:23:32,180 --> 00:23:34,120
I guess they also asked you a lot of questions.

635
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:36,450
There's something we'd like to talk to you about.

636
00:23:36,490 --> 00:23:38,760
It's going to be a hit this summer and fall.

637
00:23:38,760 --> 00:23:40,260
- What was that? - The finger flick dance?

638
00:23:40,260 --> 00:23:43,330
(Chorus 1 was their secret weapon, but wasn't chosen.)

639
00:23:43,330 --> 00:23:45,130
(They asked the artist for his opinion.)

640
00:23:45,200 --> 00:23:46,360
We were wondering...

641
00:23:46,360 --> 00:23:49,530
if you had a specific direction in mind for revising the intro.

642
00:23:50,100 --> 00:23:51,330
By the way,

643
00:23:51,330 --> 00:23:53,070
I'm fine with everything else.

644
00:23:53,070 --> 00:23:56,040
But it bothers me the most that our intro wasn't chosen.

645
00:23:56,040 --> 00:23:57,370
I think it will play a major role.

646
00:23:57,370 --> 00:23:58,710
It's the start of the performance.

647
00:23:58,840 --> 00:24:00,610
NaiN's intro is slightly similar...

648
00:24:00,610 --> 00:24:02,050
to "WYLD."

649
00:24:02,050 --> 00:24:04,450
With this move and all... Yes.

650
00:24:04,450 --> 00:24:06,080
It's the shape.

651
00:24:06,250 --> 00:24:07,780
At the end of the intro in "WYLD,"

652
00:24:07,780 --> 00:24:09,650
two dancers are positioned away from him like this.

653
00:24:09,650 --> 00:24:10,820
I kept pivoting...

654
00:24:10,820 --> 00:24:13,490
for every single segment, so it wouldn't remind him...

655
00:24:13,490 --> 00:24:15,030
of his recent works.

656
00:24:15,490 --> 00:24:17,760
But I'm a bit careful about swinging our arms...

657
00:24:17,760 --> 00:24:19,500
because it'd look very similar to "WYLD."

658
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:21,730
I want to give him something fresh.

659
00:24:21,930 --> 00:24:23,570
What should I go with?

660
00:24:23,630 --> 00:24:25,400
(Thinking hard)

661
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:26,440
What could I do?

662
00:24:26,440 --> 00:24:28,670
If the movements looked familiar,

663
00:24:28,670 --> 00:24:30,210
I tried to come up with something different.

664
00:24:30,210 --> 00:24:32,640
But he caught that with the intro.

665
00:24:32,640 --> 00:24:34,780
He has many years of experience in this industry.

666
00:24:34,780 --> 00:24:37,710
And I could feel that he wanted a specific direction with this.

667
00:24:37,710 --> 00:24:39,520
We wanted to revise the choreography...

668
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:42,520
based on what he wanted, so we asked him in person.

669
00:24:42,620 --> 00:24:44,860
How should I put it? As for the intro,

670
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:47,060
I want to start with a bang.

671
00:24:47,060 --> 00:24:50,560
It'd be nice to leave an impression on the audience that I'm rapping.

672
00:24:50,560 --> 00:24:51,760
- Or... - Yes?

673
00:24:51,760 --> 00:24:55,900
it'd also be nice if I come across as a bigger lunatic.

674
00:24:55,900 --> 00:24:57,070
(Accepting the feedback)

675
00:24:57,070 --> 00:24:58,940
I like the rest of the choreography.

676
00:24:58,970 --> 00:25:02,710
I thought we had to accept his feedback if we wanted to win.

677
00:25:02,710 --> 00:25:04,270
We're definitely going to revise it.

678
00:25:04,270 --> 00:25:05,580
I'll look for more moments...

679
00:25:05,580 --> 00:25:07,310
where he could show a different side of him.

680
00:25:08,980 --> 00:25:10,310
Hey, guys.

681
00:25:10,310 --> 00:25:13,120
We received some feedback from TAEYONG.

682
00:25:13,180 --> 00:25:15,520
We need to change it around, so it doesn't remind him of "WYLD."

683
00:25:15,520 --> 00:25:18,050
I think that's our key assignment for this mission.

684
00:25:18,050 --> 00:25:23,030
(The two of them decided to come up with a new intro.)

685
00:25:23,190 --> 00:25:25,130
Here's what I have...

686
00:25:25,130 --> 00:25:27,030
so far.

687
00:25:27,030 --> 00:25:29,630
I want to highlight the contrast in roles...

688
00:25:29,630 --> 00:25:31,430
between the dancers and TAEYONG.

689
00:25:31,430 --> 00:25:34,270
Intuitively speaking,

690
00:25:34,270 --> 00:25:36,740
TAEYONG will be surrounded...

691
00:25:36,740 --> 00:25:38,980
by dancers like this.

692
00:25:39,080 --> 00:25:41,310
They're going to spread out...

693
00:25:41,310 --> 00:25:44,650
for the reverse V formation while dancing.

694
00:25:44,650 --> 00:25:48,390
That's the revised version. I really hope he likes it.

695
00:25:48,390 --> 00:25:49,720
I really hope he does.

696
00:25:49,720 --> 00:25:51,250
No, he'll like it.

697
00:25:51,390 --> 00:25:54,220
Before we start, we want to tell you that we revised the intro.

698
00:25:54,220 --> 00:25:56,190
- Let's work on that together. - Should I learn it as we go?

699
00:25:56,190 --> 00:25:57,260
- Yes. - Yes.

700
00:25:57,260 --> 00:25:58,700
The intro will start off...

701
00:25:58,700 --> 00:26:01,300
with two male dancers bending over like this.

702
00:26:01,300 --> 00:26:03,570
You're going to start on top of them.

703
00:26:03,900 --> 00:26:05,270
- You want me to go on top? - Yes.

704
00:26:05,370 --> 00:26:06,870
Yes, you'll start on top of them.

705
00:26:06,870 --> 00:26:10,570
Actually, we weren't even thinking about our opponents.

706
00:26:10,570 --> 00:26:13,510
They're going to use a podium as their prop.

707
00:26:13,580 --> 00:26:17,510
But we revised the composition and incorporated the dancers.

708
00:26:17,750 --> 00:26:20,380
I think it will definitely look different.

709
00:26:20,580 --> 00:26:22,390
(They continue with the revised intro chorus.)

710
00:26:22,590 --> 00:26:24,120
Before the revision,

711
00:26:24,120 --> 00:26:26,260
it was between acting and dancing.

712
00:26:26,620 --> 00:26:28,690
If they dance in an expanding formation...

713
00:26:28,690 --> 00:26:30,160
while adding some rhythm to it,

714
00:26:30,160 --> 00:26:31,730
it might bring out more depth to the performance.

715
00:26:31,730 --> 00:26:33,700
His energy might come across better with this.

716
00:26:33,700 --> 00:26:35,330
(The revised version focuses more on delivering his energy.)

717
00:26:35,570 --> 00:26:36,600
(Cheering)

718
00:26:37,230 --> 00:26:38,600
You look amazing.

719
00:26:38,740 --> 00:26:39,770
This is it.

720
00:26:39,770 --> 00:26:42,210
They came up with compositions I would have never put together.

721
00:26:42,210 --> 00:26:44,370
And they made the choreography fun. I really appreciated that.

722
00:26:44,370 --> 00:26:45,840
It became the trendiest choreography.

723
00:26:45,840 --> 00:26:46,910
It's perfect.

724
00:26:46,910 --> 00:26:48,040
It's great.

725
00:26:48,040 --> 00:26:49,280
I couldn't be more satisfied.

726
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:51,510
He pulled off the revised choreography well,

727
00:26:51,510 --> 00:26:52,520
so I was happy.

728
00:26:52,520 --> 00:26:55,190
I got the feeling that he really liked it.

729
00:26:55,250 --> 00:26:57,720
We were very happy with the final choreography.

730
00:26:57,720 --> 00:26:59,820
I don't want to lose now...

731
00:26:59,820 --> 00:27:01,190
more than ever.

732
00:27:01,260 --> 00:27:02,460
- Let's try it. - Okay.

733
00:27:02,460 --> 00:27:04,260
- Let's do the whole thing. - Sounds good.

734
00:27:04,660 --> 00:27:06,330
This was our team's strategy.

735
00:27:06,330 --> 00:27:09,600
Instead of demanding him to focus on precision,

736
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:11,840
we observed the movements...

737
00:27:11,840 --> 00:27:13,900
from TAEYONG.

738
00:27:13,970 --> 00:27:16,310
Our strategy was to bring out...

739
00:27:16,310 --> 00:27:17,710
natural movements...

740
00:27:17,710 --> 00:27:18,880
from him.

741
00:27:18,940 --> 00:27:20,510
(Their practice is going smoothly thanks to their effort.)

742
00:27:21,480 --> 00:27:23,750
- Wack, you are... Yes, that's it. - That's it.

743
00:27:23,750 --> 00:27:24,750
Let's go with that.

744
00:27:25,020 --> 00:27:26,420
(I like that.)

745
00:27:26,420 --> 00:27:28,320
I think it's more fun when I shake my head around.

746
00:27:28,320 --> 00:27:29,990
- That's right. You got it. - Yes.

747
00:27:30,550 --> 00:27:31,760
(Feeling proud)

748
00:27:31,820 --> 00:27:33,090
Slide down.

749
00:27:33,090 --> 00:27:34,860
It's more comfortable when you sit on your bottom first.

750
00:27:34,860 --> 00:27:35,890
(Giggling)

751
00:27:35,890 --> 00:27:36,890
I got it.

752
00:27:36,890 --> 00:27:38,630
But you can freestyle it.

753
00:27:39,100 --> 00:27:40,830
(Sliding down like slime)

754
00:27:40,830 --> 00:27:42,100
Yes. That's great.

755
00:27:42,170 --> 00:27:44,070
- Let me test out the cushions. - You can sit...

756
00:27:44,400 --> 00:27:45,500
This is nice.

757
00:27:46,140 --> 00:27:47,240
(Plopping down)

758
00:27:47,570 --> 00:27:48,870
The landing wasn't so soft.

759
00:27:48,970 --> 00:27:50,110
(Laughing)

760
00:27:52,280 --> 00:27:54,110
(Getting playful)

761
00:27:54,110 --> 00:27:55,980
(A fun and relaxed atmosphere for their practice session)

762
00:27:55,980 --> 00:27:57,080
Right.

763
00:27:57,110 --> 00:27:59,880
They let me have a lot of freedom during practice.

764
00:28:00,050 --> 00:28:01,180
That was fun.

765
00:28:01,550 --> 00:28:02,550
That's great.

766
00:28:02,550 --> 00:28:04,220
It wasn't too hard.

767
00:28:04,420 --> 00:28:05,460
That's fun.

768
00:28:05,460 --> 00:28:07,690
When TAEYONG said he liked it,

769
00:28:07,690 --> 00:28:09,790
it felt so rewarding.

770
00:28:09,790 --> 00:28:11,830
(The practice session is going smoothly.)

771
00:28:11,830 --> 00:28:14,000
(Glancing)

772
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:15,770
- Right here... Wait. - Seven...

773
00:28:15,770 --> 00:28:19,100
(BABYZOO is rushing somewhere.)

774
00:28:19,100 --> 00:28:20,670
(What's going on?)

775
00:28:20,670 --> 00:28:22,070
- TAEYONG. - Yes?

776
00:28:22,070 --> 00:28:23,110
If you don't mind,

777
00:28:23,110 --> 00:28:24,140
- could you put this on? - Sure.

778
00:28:25,180 --> 00:28:26,640
There was something I really wanted to try.

779
00:28:26,640 --> 00:28:28,180
- Gosh. Sounds good. - Yes.

780
00:28:28,680 --> 00:28:29,780
- This? - That's perfect.

781
00:28:29,780 --> 00:28:31,250
- Like this. - Exactly.

782
00:28:31,680 --> 00:28:33,220
His fans are going to love this.

783
00:28:33,220 --> 00:28:34,520
I'm sure of it.

784
00:28:34,520 --> 00:28:37,620
We thought about ways to captivate his fans.

785
00:28:37,620 --> 00:28:39,490
As for BABYZOO,

786
00:28:39,490 --> 00:28:41,930
he has a knack for creating visually impressive moments...

787
00:28:41,930 --> 00:28:42,930
on stage.

788
00:28:43,190 --> 00:28:46,000
(Drilling new details nonstop)

789
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:47,760
(Bite it like this.)

790
00:28:47,760 --> 00:28:48,900
Can you try this? Like this.

791
00:28:48,900 --> 00:28:49,930
(Like this?)

792
00:28:50,830 --> 00:28:52,840
(Can you pull this off too?)

793
00:28:53,400 --> 00:28:54,400
Like this?

794
00:28:54,400 --> 00:28:56,210
(Flawlessly executing it)

795
00:28:56,210 --> 00:28:57,770
(This is crazy.)

