1060
00:39:48,220 --> 00:39:50,330
Is my finger flick dance that bad?

1061
00:39:52,160 --> 00:39:53,460
Abandon the finger flick dance.

1062
00:39:54,330 --> 00:39:56,570
- We have to discard the flick. - Yes.

1063
00:39:57,100 --> 00:39:58,600
- It's a bad sign, right? - Yes.

1064
00:39:59,030 --> 00:40:01,600
Rather than persuading him, let's just remove it.

1065
00:40:02,170 --> 00:40:03,810
I need to talk to BADA...

1066
00:40:03,940 --> 00:40:06,110
and think about removing it.

1067
00:40:07,240 --> 00:40:08,610
(That night)

1068
00:40:08,810 --> 00:40:10,180
- Chorus one? - Yes.

1069
00:40:10,180 --> 00:40:11,480
(BADA and Back Koo Young begin changing the choreography.)

1070
00:40:11,810 --> 00:40:13,650
The finger flick is such a bummer.

1071
00:40:16,850 --> 00:40:18,420
(Abandon the finger flick dance.)

1072
00:40:19,820 --> 00:40:21,460
Although I said that,

1073
00:40:21,460 --> 00:40:23,260
that's not what I wanted.

1074
00:40:24,460 --> 00:40:26,100
Is my finger flick dance that bad?

1075
00:40:28,230 --> 00:40:30,270
(Choi Young Jun from 1MILLION)

1076
00:40:30,270 --> 00:40:32,500
(Watching the finger flick dance)

1077
00:40:32,770 --> 00:40:35,540
It is catchy,

1078
00:40:35,770 --> 00:40:37,470
but what TAEYONG wants is to dance.

1079
00:40:38,640 --> 00:40:40,680
(NOH WON from AMAZON)

1080
00:40:40,980 --> 00:40:42,080
I love it.

1081
00:40:42,310 --> 00:40:43,910
It's easy for people to follow.

1082
00:40:44,150 --> 00:40:46,320
Yet it's danceable.

1083
00:40:46,450 --> 00:40:47,920
It's very impactful.

1084
00:40:48,750 --> 00:40:52,020
Honestly, I didn't want to give up on the finger flick dance.

1085
00:40:52,450 --> 00:40:54,220
It kept ringing...

1086
00:40:54,220 --> 00:40:56,630
- in my head. - Flick.

1087
00:40:57,990 --> 00:40:59,230
- Flick. - Is there a way...

1088
00:40:59,230 --> 00:41:01,530
to talk him into it?

1089
00:41:02,870 --> 00:41:04,670
It's not that he doesn't like...

1090
00:41:04,670 --> 00:41:06,600
the contrast between him and the dancers.

1091
00:41:06,840 --> 00:41:08,740
BADA and I came up with a strategy.

1092
00:41:09,210 --> 00:41:11,070
We decided to come up...

1093
00:41:11,070 --> 00:41:13,640
with four different versions of the finger flick dance...

1094
00:41:13,640 --> 00:41:17,050
and let TAEYONG choose.

1095
00:41:17,210 --> 00:41:19,580
(An example of the finger flick dance)

1096
00:41:19,580 --> 00:41:21,820
It'll look more like a dance.

1097
00:41:22,150 --> 00:41:23,790
We should be prepared.

1098
00:41:24,020 --> 00:41:26,820
I want to push the finger flick dance.

1099
00:41:26,990 --> 00:41:29,790
But the artist might have a different opinion.

1100
00:41:29,860 --> 00:41:31,690
He'd be like, "A finger flick in this song?"

1101
00:41:31,860 --> 00:41:34,500
- A flick. - I don't know what he's like.

1102
00:41:34,660 --> 00:41:36,130
Will it just be abandoned?

1103
00:41:36,130 --> 00:41:39,030
Or he didn't choose it,

1104
00:41:39,100 --> 00:41:42,570
but people are doing it after this show airs.

1105
00:41:42,570 --> 00:41:43,670
That's one possibility.

1106
00:41:44,210 --> 00:41:45,640
(The choreography TAEYONG chose by section)

1107
00:41:45,640 --> 00:41:47,940
(People are actually sad that the finger flick dance is gone.)

1108
00:41:48,110 --> 00:41:49,910
- Flick. - I'm also curious.

1109
00:41:50,910 --> 00:41:52,580
Hello.

1110
00:41:53,020 --> 00:41:54,280
You have to memorize it.

1111
00:41:54,280 --> 00:41:55,480
- Let's give it a try first. - Okay.

1112
00:41:55,480 --> 00:41:56,790
(BADA and Back Koo Young begin practicing the choreography.)

1113
00:41:58,350 --> 00:41:59,420
First,

1114
00:41:59,420 --> 00:42:02,460
we didn't start with the finger flick dance on purpose.

1115
00:42:02,460 --> 00:42:05,590
We assumed he didn't like it.

1116
00:42:05,830 --> 00:42:06,930
So...

1117
00:42:07,300 --> 00:42:08,330
You got it!

1118
00:42:08,560 --> 00:42:12,070
We taught him exciting and trendy moves first.

1119
00:42:13,040 --> 00:42:15,400
We taught them first, and when he was somewhat warmed up...

1120
00:42:16,070 --> 00:42:17,110
- Anyway... - The chorus?

1121
00:42:17,110 --> 00:42:18,410
The chorus? Okay.

1122
00:42:18,410 --> 00:42:19,880
Actually,

1123
00:42:19,880 --> 00:42:22,180
we prepared four different versions for the chorus.

1124
00:42:22,480 --> 00:42:24,950
TAEYONG, let's talk before we continue with practice.

1125
00:42:25,310 --> 00:42:28,320
There's something I want to talk to you about.

1126
00:42:28,680 --> 00:42:29,850
That is...

1127
00:42:29,850 --> 00:42:31,350
The finger flick dance?

1128
00:42:31,350 --> 00:42:32,820
(Busted)

1129
00:42:33,160 --> 00:42:35,020
There are many options.

1130
00:42:35,020 --> 00:42:36,030
Okay.

1131
00:42:36,030 --> 00:42:38,490
(Option 1, dancing instead of the finger flick dance)

1132
00:42:38,660 --> 00:42:39,860
That's very energetic.

1133
00:42:40,030 --> 00:42:42,360
But if we were to add the finger flick dance,

1134
00:42:42,360 --> 00:42:43,800
this is what happens.

1135
00:42:44,200 --> 00:42:47,100
(Option 2, finger flick dance)

1136
00:42:48,170 --> 00:42:49,940
(Something like that)

1137
00:42:50,410 --> 00:42:51,470
I see.

1138
00:42:52,040 --> 00:42:53,180
That's the flow.

1139
00:42:53,180 --> 00:42:54,710
What do you think?

1140
00:42:54,710 --> 00:42:56,310
Do I have to choose now?

1141
00:42:56,810 --> 00:42:58,710
- I was pretty nervous. - The flick.

1142
00:42:58,710 --> 00:43:00,650
(What's going to happen to his finger flick dance?)

1143
00:43:00,650 --> 00:43:02,520
(What will TAEYONG say?)

1144
00:43:02,520 --> 00:43:04,490
I...

1145
00:43:05,090 --> 00:43:06,990
I want to keep the finger flick dance.

1146
00:43:08,120 --> 00:43:11,260
I like this more.

1147
00:43:11,260 --> 00:43:12,800
After the four finger flicks...

1148
00:43:13,130 --> 00:43:14,800
(During the concept briefing)

1149
00:43:14,800 --> 00:43:16,330
(Unsure about the finger flick)

1150
00:43:16,330 --> 00:43:18,370
(Flick)

1151
00:43:19,000 --> 00:43:20,400
(They can adjust it to four times.)

1152
00:43:20,400 --> 00:43:22,570
(4 finger flicks)

1153
00:43:22,570 --> 00:43:24,240
(Then dance)

1154
00:43:24,440 --> 00:43:26,180
In the end,

1155
00:43:26,180 --> 00:43:27,410
TAEYONG chose it.

1156
00:43:27,410 --> 00:43:30,480
It's not exactly my opinion.

1157
00:43:30,480 --> 00:43:34,720
I said it because you kept pushing it.

1158
00:43:34,720 --> 00:43:36,290
I believe it's part of an artist's ability...

1159
00:43:36,290 --> 00:43:38,690
to trust the director.

1160
00:43:38,850 --> 00:43:40,090
Thank you.

1161
00:43:40,620 --> 00:43:42,360
This summer and fall.

1162
00:43:42,360 --> 00:43:44,290
- It'll hit big. - You sound like...

1163
00:43:44,290 --> 00:43:45,290
As soon as TAEYONG said it,

1164
00:43:45,290 --> 00:43:47,060
Koo Young smiled.

1165
00:43:47,060 --> 00:43:48,060
When Chuseok comes,

1166
00:43:48,060 --> 00:43:50,030
right after bowing...

1167
00:43:50,030 --> 00:43:51,900
- Flick? - Flick.

1168
00:43:51,900 --> 00:43:53,800
This will air just before Chuseok.

1169
00:43:54,100 --> 00:43:56,170
It doesn't need to be done in a fixed position.

1170
00:43:56,170 --> 00:43:57,310
(BADA and Back Koo Young begin developing the finger flick dance.)

1171
00:43:58,240 --> 00:44:00,540
(TAEYONG's version of the finger flick dance)

1172
00:44:00,540 --> 00:44:03,750
I wouldn't try it if he was someone...

1173
00:44:03,750 --> 00:44:04,810
who couldn't pull it off.

1174
00:44:04,810 --> 00:44:07,980
But he's good at pulling off the gestures.

1175
00:44:07,980 --> 00:44:09,590
This is how I taught him,

1176
00:44:09,590 --> 00:44:11,450
but he knows how to alter it.

1177
00:44:11,450 --> 00:44:13,590
It's fun to watch artists doing that.

1178
00:44:13,590 --> 00:44:14,590
(The next practice)

1179
00:44:15,620 --> 00:44:18,590
I think the finger flick dance got upgraded.

1180
00:44:18,590 --> 00:44:19,730
I love this part.

1181
00:44:19,730 --> 00:44:21,700
(A gesture added to the finger flick dance)

1182
00:44:21,700 --> 00:44:23,700
- I love this. - This?

1183
00:44:23,700 --> 00:44:25,130
I love being funny...

1184
00:44:25,130 --> 00:44:27,970
on stage.

1185
00:44:27,970 --> 00:44:31,410
I liked how I could be funny with style.

1186
00:44:31,410 --> 00:44:33,380
In that sense,

1187
00:44:33,380 --> 00:44:35,180
it created good synergy.

1188
00:44:35,180 --> 00:44:36,510
We created a performance choreography...

1189
00:44:36,510 --> 00:44:38,850
that TAEYONG will like.

1190
00:44:38,850 --> 00:44:40,950
There will be 13 more dancers.

1191
00:44:40,950 --> 00:44:42,020
That's 22 in total.

1192
00:44:42,020 --> 00:44:44,490
It's big in scale, and it involves a lot of people.

1193
00:44:44,490 --> 00:44:47,190
You don't just come up with a structure...

1194
00:44:47,190 --> 00:44:49,560
for 22 people in your head like that.

1195
00:44:49,560 --> 00:44:52,230
But when I open the app,

1196
00:44:52,230 --> 00:44:55,330
I can see the V structure and all at a glance.

1197
00:44:55,600 --> 00:44:57,900
Like this. Okay?

1198
00:44:57,900 --> 00:44:59,200
Let's try it.

1199
00:44:59,270 --> 00:45:00,770
When I show the dancers using the app,

1200
00:45:00,770 --> 00:45:03,210
they understand when to move easily and accurately.

1201
00:45:03,210 --> 00:45:05,370
I've always wanted to make something like this.

1202
00:45:05,370 --> 00:45:07,280
I knew I could do it.

1203
00:45:07,280 --> 00:45:08,280
- Hi. - Hello.

1204
00:45:08,280 --> 00:45:09,780
Hello.

1205
00:45:10,250 --> 00:45:11,950
We worked on the details.

1206
00:45:11,950 --> 00:45:13,220
I'll explain it to you later.

1207
00:45:13,220 --> 00:45:14,320
Okay.

1208
00:45:14,320 --> 00:45:16,450
TAEYONG often makes gestures.

1209
00:45:16,450 --> 00:45:18,450
So we'll make the gestures clear and then start dancing.

1210
00:45:18,450 --> 00:45:19,920
If we organize that first,

1211
00:45:19,920 --> 00:45:21,890
he'd pull off the performance even more.

1212
00:45:21,890 --> 00:45:23,960
We added details here.

1213
00:45:24,090 --> 00:45:26,430
Three, four, and that's when you shake your hand.

1214
00:45:26,430 --> 00:45:27,430
After shaking...

1215
00:45:27,430 --> 00:45:28,660
(A pause)

1216
00:45:28,660 --> 00:45:30,630
- You have to pause slightly. - Okay.

1217
00:45:30,630 --> 00:45:33,570
BADA is stricter than I am when she directs.

1218
00:45:33,570 --> 00:45:35,570
You have to use your hand.

1219
00:45:35,570 --> 00:45:36,710
(Adding gestures)

1220
00:45:36,970 --> 00:45:39,070
BADA tends to...

1221
00:45:39,070 --> 00:45:41,380
teaches her style strictly.

1222
00:45:41,380 --> 00:45:43,310
As if you're hitting the ceiling.

1223
00:45:43,310 --> 00:45:44,750
After this...

1224
00:45:44,750 --> 00:45:46,250
Your left foot comes forward first.

1225
00:45:46,250 --> 00:45:47,320
- Okay. - Yes.

1226
00:45:47,580 --> 00:45:50,220
We worked on every little detail.

1227
00:45:50,220 --> 00:45:51,290
TAEYONG.

1228
00:45:51,290 --> 00:45:52,960
Don't go this way, but forward.

1229
00:45:52,960 --> 00:45:54,420
- Forward? Okay. - Yes.

1230
00:45:54,420 --> 00:45:57,190
We practiced the angle and the speed.

1231
00:45:57,190 --> 00:45:59,130
The timing of some of the direction was off.

1232
00:45:59,130 --> 00:46:00,260
We fixed every single thing.

1233
00:46:00,260 --> 00:46:02,360
We must get every single detail.

1234
00:46:03,630 --> 00:46:05,570
I tend...

1235
00:46:05,570 --> 00:46:07,740
not to force artists...

1236
00:46:07,740 --> 00:46:10,370
to get every single detail right.

1237
00:46:10,370 --> 00:46:11,370
Because...

1238
00:46:11,370 --> 00:46:13,280
TAEYONG already has enough stage experience as it is.

1239
00:46:13,280 --> 00:46:15,080
He's an artist with ten years of experience...

1240
00:46:15,080 --> 00:46:16,450
who's good enough to see the whole picture.

1241
00:46:16,450 --> 00:46:18,280
If I teach him one,

1242
00:46:18,280 --> 00:46:20,620
he can do 5 or even 10.

1243
00:46:20,620 --> 00:46:23,020
New details were added every day.

1244
00:46:23,290 --> 00:46:24,720
The gesture here changed.

1245
00:46:24,720 --> 00:46:27,920
(The gesture changed again in the next practice.)

1246
00:46:28,220 --> 00:46:29,730
I knew TAEYONG would feel...

1247
00:46:29,730 --> 00:46:33,100
pressured.

1248
00:46:33,100 --> 00:46:34,630
Even if I were him,

1249
00:46:34,630 --> 00:46:36,870
it's got to be tiring...

1250
00:46:36,870 --> 00:46:38,430
to learn different choreographies for the same song.

1251
00:46:38,430 --> 00:46:40,040
Can we practice this part?

1252
00:46:40,200 --> 00:46:41,740
TAEYONG, when you do this...

1253
00:46:43,740 --> 00:46:45,140
(Confused)

1254
00:46:45,470 --> 00:46:46,780
In terms of directing style,

1255
00:46:46,780 --> 00:46:49,180
BADA and Koo Young...

1256
00:46:49,180 --> 00:46:52,380
focus too much...

1257
00:46:52,380 --> 00:46:53,420
on gestures and details.

1258
00:46:53,420 --> 00:46:55,850
I'm not sure...

1259
00:46:55,850 --> 00:46:57,450
if I can pull everything off.

1260
00:46:57,450 --> 00:46:58,920
Honestly, when I was dancing,

1261
00:46:58,920 --> 00:47:00,220
I was too worried about the detail...

1262
00:47:00,220 --> 00:47:01,590
that I didn't enjoy it.

1263
00:47:01,790 --> 00:47:03,030
- Do it right away? - Okay.

1264
00:47:03,030 --> 00:47:04,360
I think it's better that way.

1265
00:47:04,360 --> 00:47:05,730
I think...

1266
00:47:05,730 --> 00:47:07,330
there are too many.

1267
00:47:09,260 --> 00:47:13,240
It was exactly what I was worried about.

1268
00:47:14,640 --> 00:47:17,610
(BADA and Back Koo Young have an urgent meeting.)

1269
00:47:17,770 --> 00:47:19,840
You added more details today.

1270
00:47:19,840 --> 00:47:21,710
(More details were added just a day before filming.)

1271
00:47:21,710 --> 00:47:23,550
You're being too strict.

1272
00:47:23,750 --> 00:47:24,850
We need to loosen it.

1273
00:47:24,850 --> 00:47:27,320
- Is that how you see it? - If this weren't for the mission,

1274
00:47:27,320 --> 00:47:29,650
but just our job,

1275
00:47:29,650 --> 00:47:31,390
we wouldn't be doing this.

1276
00:47:31,620 --> 00:47:32,990
I'm the opposite.

1277
00:47:32,990 --> 00:47:35,090
I would've been more strict about the details.

1278
00:47:35,090 --> 00:47:36,090
Triple times harder.

1279
00:47:36,090 --> 00:47:38,230
When I'm strict, I'm ten times stricter.

1280
00:47:38,230 --> 00:47:40,600
If it's a first-year artist, I'd do the same.

1281
00:47:41,100 --> 00:47:42,800
But not for TAEYONG with ten years of experience.

1282
00:47:43,100 --> 00:47:45,500
The hours of time I put into teaching and the way I teach EXO...

1283
00:47:45,500 --> 00:47:46,500
in their first year...

1284
00:47:46,500 --> 00:47:48,600
and now...

1285
00:47:48,600 --> 00:47:50,140
are different.

1286
00:47:50,370 --> 00:47:52,410
You're treating him like he's a rookie.

1287
00:47:52,540 --> 00:47:54,840
We set everything for rookies.

1288
00:47:55,240 --> 00:47:58,310
I think we made a mistake from that perspective.

1289
00:47:58,450 --> 00:48:00,480
From a choreographer's perspective,

1290
00:48:00,480 --> 00:48:02,320
I shouldn't just think the artist would be happy...

1291
00:48:02,320 --> 00:48:05,820
when I raise the quality of the performance,

1292
00:48:05,820 --> 00:48:07,590
but I realized I should worry...

1293
00:48:07,590 --> 00:48:10,830
about the pressure, risk, and stress the artist will have...

1294
00:48:10,830 --> 00:48:13,960
as a director.

1295
00:48:15,330 --> 00:48:17,530
- Koo Young, I'm sorry. - About what?

1296
00:48:17,530 --> 00:48:20,870
About being too strict about the details.

1297
00:48:20,870 --> 00:48:23,640
I thought leaving everything to him...

1298
00:48:23,640 --> 00:48:25,740
- He'd think you're being insincere? - Yes.

1299
00:48:25,740 --> 00:48:27,380
I didn't want him to feel that way.

1300
00:48:27,380 --> 00:48:29,680
Although TAEYONG says that,

1301
00:48:29,680 --> 00:48:31,610
I know he'll pull it off on stage.

1302
00:48:31,610 --> 00:48:34,180
I guess it bothered BADA so much.

1303
00:48:34,180 --> 00:48:35,750
She apologized to me.

1304
00:48:35,750 --> 00:48:37,650
It broke my heart.

1305
00:48:37,820 --> 00:48:39,660
She was worried about it,

1306
00:48:39,660 --> 00:48:41,690
so she came to talk to me.

1307
00:48:41,690 --> 00:48:43,790
But even if I were to go back in time,

1308
00:48:43,790 --> 00:48:45,160
I wouldn't stop her.

1309
00:48:45,160 --> 00:48:47,100
I respect her directing skills...

1310
00:48:47,100 --> 00:48:49,260
and her way of teaching.

1311
00:48:49,260 --> 00:48:50,300
What if it was the opposite?

1312
00:48:50,300 --> 00:48:52,830
If I forced BADA...

1313
00:48:52,830 --> 00:48:55,870
to push the finger flick dance,

1314
00:48:56,040 --> 00:48:58,240
she might not have been sure about it.

1315
00:48:58,240 --> 00:48:59,240
But she was kind enough...

1316
00:48:59,240 --> 00:49:00,840
to give it a try.

1317
00:49:00,840 --> 00:49:03,980
In a collaborative project, we need to respect each other.

1318
00:49:04,050 --> 00:49:06,280
In the end, we made it.

1319
00:49:06,420 --> 00:49:08,680
Even if we lose tomorrow,

1320
00:49:08,680 --> 00:49:11,250
as long as people say, "Good job. That's cool."

1321
00:49:11,250 --> 00:49:13,160
That's all that matters.

1322
00:49:13,390 --> 00:49:16,930
I was facing TAEYONG...

1323
00:49:16,930 --> 00:49:19,590
whose presence has grown as a solo artist.

1324
00:49:19,590 --> 00:49:21,100
I had to study a lot.

1325
00:49:21,100 --> 00:49:23,000
I learned a lot from Koo Young.

1326
00:49:23,000 --> 00:49:25,330
I hope...

1327
00:49:25,330 --> 00:49:27,770
TAEYONG feels...

1328
00:49:27,770 --> 00:49:29,370
that we created a performance...

1329
00:49:29,370 --> 00:49:32,070
where he can express the impact.

1330
00:49:32,070 --> 00:49:33,410
That's all I want.

1331
00:49:33,410 --> 00:49:35,980
It's only morning. So don't put any pressure on him.

1332
00:49:35,980 --> 00:49:38,250
- Let's loosen him up. - Sure.

1333
00:49:39,150 --> 00:49:41,150
Let's do our best.

1334
00:49:41,750 --> 00:49:43,250
When TAEYONG gets here later,

1335
00:49:43,250 --> 00:49:44,720
we'll have to cheer him up.

1336
00:49:44,720 --> 00:49:45,890
We have to support him.

1337
00:49:45,890 --> 00:49:48,220
That's all we can do.

1338
00:49:48,560 --> 00:49:51,830
Helping the artist feel less pressured is most important.

1339
00:49:51,830 --> 00:49:53,800
We're going to cover the details...

1340
00:49:53,800 --> 00:49:56,130
for TAEYONG to enjoy.

1341
00:49:56,700 --> 00:49:58,030
Let's go.

1342
00:49:58,030 --> 00:49:59,840
(BADA and Back Koo Young go on stage to rehearse.)

1343
00:49:59,970 --> 00:50:02,000
Can you turn on the high-powered fan?

1344
00:50:02,270 --> 00:50:03,470
(The high-powered fan?)

1345
00:50:03,670 --> 00:50:07,110
I want the high-powered fan to make it look more like a concert.

1346
00:50:07,110 --> 00:50:09,640
So his hair or clothes will fly and give that vibe.

1347
00:50:09,710 --> 00:50:12,680
What's the point of using the high-powered fan...

1348
00:50:12,680 --> 00:50:14,520
- when TAEYONG has short hair? - Exactly.

1349
00:50:14,520 --> 00:50:16,490
They don't realize it's more dancers.

1350
00:50:16,790 --> 00:50:18,920
This mission is for artists.

1351
00:50:18,920 --> 00:50:21,190
This isn't a stage for dancers.

1352
00:50:21,320 --> 00:50:23,560
- BADA's in the center of it. - I know.

1353
00:50:23,560 --> 00:50:26,800
- Only her hair is flying. - Can you put it on the side?

1354
00:50:26,800 --> 00:50:30,000
I think the artist should shine.

1355
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:32,630
It got me thinking, "Will the artist like it?"

1356
00:50:32,800 --> 00:50:34,540
If we just play the song and dance on stage,

1357
00:50:34,540 --> 00:50:37,210
it's not fun.

1358
00:50:37,210 --> 00:50:40,140
The audience is TAEYONG's fans.

1359
00:50:40,140 --> 00:50:42,080
I want to give them endorphins like in a concert.

1360
00:50:42,080 --> 00:50:43,080
(During the concept briefing)

1361
00:50:43,080 --> 00:50:45,380
(Strategy 1, made for a large-scale concert)

1362
00:50:45,380 --> 00:50:46,520
(The audience is on the side.)

1363
00:50:46,520 --> 00:50:48,180
(Exclaiming)

1364
00:50:48,180 --> 00:50:49,180
(Intrigued)

1365
00:50:49,180 --> 00:50:52,520
(Strategy 2, communication with the audience)

1366
00:50:52,650 --> 00:50:53,660
There's a finger flick dance.

1367
00:50:53,660 --> 00:50:54,990
There's also headbanging at the end.

1368
00:50:54,990 --> 00:50:56,890
It'll excite the audience.

1369
00:50:56,890 --> 00:50:59,960
"We can share this emotion along with the performance."

1370
00:50:59,960 --> 00:51:01,560
The audience is going to love it.

1371
00:51:01,900 --> 00:51:03,400
Hello.

1372
00:51:03,400 --> 00:51:04,870
I haven't been to Ilsan for so long.

1373
00:51:04,970 --> 00:51:06,170
Hello.

1374
00:51:06,170 --> 00:51:08,440
Hello.

1375
00:51:08,440 --> 00:51:11,710
Do we have the confetti ready?

1376
00:51:11,710 --> 00:51:12,710
(Confetti?)

1377
00:51:12,710 --> 00:51:14,580
I noticed the fans keep them.

1378
00:51:14,580 --> 00:51:16,850
For the fans to take it home,

1379
00:51:16,850 --> 00:51:18,280
and remember it,

1380
00:51:18,280 --> 00:51:20,550
I wanted to create them.

1381
00:51:20,550 --> 00:51:22,980
We're going to fly these later.

1382
00:51:22,980 --> 00:51:24,720
Did you make them yourself?

1383
00:51:24,820 --> 00:51:26,390
We're still making them.

1384
00:51:26,390 --> 00:51:28,220
We're making them in the green room.

1385
00:51:29,090 --> 00:51:31,490
I said I ran a factory.

1386
00:51:31,490 --> 00:51:34,000
And I literally did. I stamped them one by one.

1387
00:51:34,460 --> 00:51:35,960
(The confetti factory kept running until the very last minute.)

1388
00:51:35,960 --> 00:51:38,400
When the other teams are practicing dancing...

1389
00:51:38,400 --> 00:51:40,670
(We're stamping.)

1390
00:51:40,900 --> 00:51:41,900
There are three types.

1391
00:51:41,900 --> 00:51:43,910
"Wacka Wak." "Written by TAEYONG."

1392
00:51:43,910 --> 00:51:45,970
"Choreography by BADA and Back Koo Young."

1393
00:51:45,970 --> 00:51:48,280
We created them,

1394
00:51:48,280 --> 00:51:49,780
so they'd fly high...

1395
00:51:49,780 --> 00:51:50,980
and reach his fans.

1396
00:51:51,180 --> 00:51:53,880
I want TAEYONG to feel the same way about it.

1397
00:51:54,150 --> 00:51:56,020
I thought that was cute.

1398
00:51:56,180 --> 00:51:59,220
That's what the high-powered fan was for.

1399
00:51:59,220 --> 00:52:01,420
They're handmade confetti.

1400
00:52:01,420 --> 00:52:03,830
The fans are going to like it.

1401
00:52:03,830 --> 00:52:05,090
It made me anxious.

1402
00:52:05,360 --> 00:52:06,430
I placed them in the sections...

1403
00:52:06,430 --> 00:52:08,660
I wanted to highlight.

1404
00:52:08,660 --> 00:52:13,030
Please pan the camera to catch the left LED screen together here.

1405
00:52:13,340 --> 00:52:15,370
For the next part, frame it with the right LED screen.

1406
00:52:15,370 --> 00:52:16,510
The lyrics will display on the screen.

1407
00:52:16,940 --> 00:52:18,310
Since TAEYONG's fans are coming as the audience,

1408
00:52:18,310 --> 00:52:19,770
we decided to project...

1409
00:52:19,770 --> 00:52:21,210
what TAEYONG wants to convey onto the LED screens.

1410
00:52:21,210 --> 00:52:23,510
That's how we ended up putting the lyrics up on the LED.

1411
00:52:23,510 --> 00:52:25,410
(The gimbal rehearsal is proceeding...)

1412
00:52:25,410 --> 00:52:27,320
(according to BADA and Back Koo Young's directing)

1413
00:52:27,420 --> 00:52:29,420
It feels quite distracting because of the LED screen.

1414
00:52:29,420 --> 00:52:32,020
The focus got drawn to the text that I thought...

1415
00:52:32,020 --> 00:52:33,960
they might have missed the actual focal point.

1416
00:52:33,960 --> 00:52:36,320
I thought it could feel overwhelming.

1417
00:52:36,320 --> 00:52:38,290
It might look a bit chaotic.

1418
00:52:38,630 --> 00:52:39,630
This is...

1419
00:52:41,830 --> 00:52:42,830
fun.

1420
00:52:43,330 --> 00:52:45,500
(BADA and Koo Young's faces brighten at a word from TAEYONG.)

1421
00:52:45,830 --> 00:52:48,240
I felt so relieved.

1422
00:52:48,570 --> 00:52:50,170
The directors really hype me up.

1423
00:52:50,270 --> 00:52:51,910
Seeing them expend their own energy...

1424
00:52:51,910 --> 00:52:54,680
to hype me up even when they're exhausted...

1425
00:52:54,680 --> 00:52:56,510
makes me feel even more attached to this choreography.

1426
00:52:56,610 --> 00:52:58,450
Having TAEYONG tell us that it was fun...

1427
00:52:58,450 --> 00:53:00,020
even in such a grueling situation...

1428
00:53:00,020 --> 00:53:01,420
gave us a lot of strength.

1429
00:53:01,780 --> 00:53:02,780
Okay.

1430
00:53:03,950 --> 00:53:06,090
- Thank you. - Thank you.

1431
00:53:06,090 --> 00:53:07,220
Thank you. Great work.

1432
00:53:07,220 --> 00:53:08,220
(BADA and Back Koo Young's rehearsal is over.)

1433
00:53:08,620 --> 00:53:10,330
- Good work. - I'll see you later.

1434
00:53:10,590 --> 00:53:11,590
Thank you.

1435
00:53:11,590 --> 00:53:13,500
Having the fans enjoy that performance.

1436
00:53:13,600 --> 00:53:15,530
I believe that is the ultimate weapon...

1437
00:53:15,530 --> 00:53:16,770
to capture an artist's heart.

1438
00:53:16,770 --> 00:53:18,200
The directors of this performance...

1439
00:53:18,430 --> 00:53:20,100
are BADA and Back Koo Young.

1440
00:53:21,840 --> 00:53:25,870
(Make some noise!)

1441
00:53:25,870 --> 00:53:28,880
(Screaming)

1442
00:53:28,880 --> 00:53:31,450
The crowd reaction feels way louder than during our turn.

1443
00:53:31,450 --> 00:53:33,050
Let us greet everyone first.

1444
00:53:33,050 --> 00:53:34,620
To the world, this is...

1445
00:53:34,720 --> 00:53:37,820
- Street World Fighter! - Make some noise!

1446
00:53:38,490 --> 00:53:40,220
You all know it, right?

1447
00:53:40,560 --> 00:53:42,620
And now, let's welcome...

1448
00:53:42,620 --> 00:53:43,960
the one and only...

1449
00:53:43,960 --> 00:53:47,060
- TAEYONG! - TAEYONG!

1450
00:53:47,060 --> 00:53:49,630
TY!

1451
00:53:53,670 --> 00:53:56,300
(Cheering)

1452
00:53:56,300 --> 00:53:59,310
The two directors here paid great attention to many details...

1453
00:53:59,310 --> 00:54:02,580
such as makeup, costume, hair, and everything in between.

1454
00:54:02,580 --> 00:54:04,150
How I look right now...

1455
00:54:04,150 --> 00:54:07,080
is what these two directors wanted to bring to life.

1456
00:54:08,250 --> 00:54:10,220
We'll show you my performance right away.

1457
00:54:10,750 --> 00:54:12,520
"Wacka Wak."

1458
00:54:12,520 --> 00:54:15,020
(Filled with anticipation)

1459
00:54:15,020 --> 00:54:16,890
We are fully prepared...

1460
00:54:16,890 --> 00:54:19,430
to captivate the audience here today.

1461
00:54:19,430 --> 00:54:22,700
We plan to go all-in with our own solidity,

1462
00:54:22,700 --> 00:54:25,070
so I think it'll stand apart from BABYZOO and NaiN's piece.

1463
00:54:29,040 --> 00:54:31,440
Wak, Wak, Wak!

1464
00:54:31,440 --> 00:54:34,940
(To be continued)

1465
00:54:36,040 --> 00:54:38,250
Wak, Wak, Wak!

1466
00:54:39,080 --> 00:54:41,250
We wanted to create a performance where the energy of TAEYONG...

1467
00:54:41,250 --> 00:54:42,980
and the fans become one.

1468
00:54:42,980 --> 00:54:45,620
We'll deliver a performance that feels like a real concert.

1469
00:54:45,820 --> 00:54:48,620
(Cheering)

1470
00:54:48,620 --> 00:54:50,230
The fans are loving this so much.

1471
00:54:50,230 --> 00:54:52,530
The vibe is definitely different from ours.

1472
00:54:54,900 --> 00:54:56,730
(Overall Concept: Emphasized expressions like "Wacka Wak...")

1473
00:54:56,730 --> 00:54:58,370
(and "You're Wack" from the title and lyrics)

1474
00:54:58,370 --> 00:55:01,970
("Wacka Wak" by TAEYONG)

1475
00:55:07,140 --> 00:55:09,740
I could definitely feel a lot more energy coming through.

1476
00:55:11,580 --> 00:55:14,150
This kind of staging definitely looks great on stage.

1477
00:55:15,020 --> 00:55:16,450
This is nice.

1478
00:55:22,090 --> 00:55:24,660
The reaction from the fans was definitely great.

1479
00:55:30,730 --> 00:55:32,800
The choreography hits harder here.

1480
00:55:35,240 --> 00:55:36,240
The outfit looks stunning.

1481
00:55:37,740 --> 00:55:38,740
I like this one.

1482
00:55:39,340 --> 00:55:42,110
This seems to showcase TAEYONG as an individual better.

1483
00:55:43,550 --> 00:55:45,010
His face is clearly visible,

1484
00:55:45,550 --> 00:55:46,980
and he looks much more like a true artist.

1485
00:55:52,320 --> 00:55:53,490
This is more crowd-pleasing.

1486
00:55:57,660 --> 00:55:58,760
This is fun.

1487
00:56:05,800 --> 00:56:07,440
TAEYONG is so good.

1488
00:56:15,380 --> 00:56:17,510
I could just feel a massive amount of pure energy.

1489
00:56:20,880 --> 00:56:23,320
The VJ graphics are definitely sleeker here.

1490
00:56:27,390 --> 00:56:28,720
The finger flick dance is coming.

1491
00:56:28,720 --> 00:56:29,760
The finger flick dance is here.

1492
00:56:30,290 --> 00:56:31,430
I love stuff like this.

1493
00:56:32,390 --> 00:56:34,730
Is there anyone in this country who doesn't know how to flick?

1494
00:56:34,830 --> 00:56:36,900
TAEYONG pulled that off so well.

1495
00:56:38,800 --> 00:56:40,170
The finger flick dance is totally hitting.

1496
00:56:43,100 --> 00:56:45,240
The choreography is way more memorable here.

1497
00:56:45,240 --> 00:56:48,040
It has the impact from repeating the exact same movement.

1498
00:56:55,750 --> 00:56:57,090
The performance is clear.

1499
00:56:57,320 --> 00:56:59,550
It's a performance that's easy for the public to read.

1500
00:57:04,160 --> 00:57:06,430
Koo Young is the main dancer here.

1501
00:57:06,430 --> 00:57:08,500
I don't think the fans loved that.

1502
00:57:09,000 --> 00:57:10,830
Koo Young coming right up front and doing that part.

1503
00:57:21,210 --> 00:57:23,180
They did a solid job channeling the spotlight into the part...

1504
00:57:23,180 --> 00:57:24,310
where the artist becomes the star.

1505
00:57:32,850 --> 00:57:34,020
This is so cool.

1506
00:57:34,020 --> 00:57:36,560
"My goodness. What is this? This is insane."

1507
00:57:36,560 --> 00:57:38,190
I wanted the fans to feel like this.

1508
00:57:38,190 --> 00:57:40,160
We need to go wild on stage.

1509
00:57:40,260 --> 00:57:42,860
Only when we go crazy can we get the crowd even crazier,

1510
00:57:42,860 --> 00:57:44,770
and get the artist to go completely wild, too.

1511
00:57:44,870 --> 00:57:47,370
Headbanging right in front of the fans...

1512
00:57:47,370 --> 00:57:49,300
must've made it more thrilling for them.

1513
00:57:49,300 --> 00:57:50,910
The fans are definitely loving it.

1514
00:57:53,610 --> 00:57:55,310
The performance felt like a pure rush of dopamine.

1515
00:57:55,310 --> 00:57:58,250
It was like, "This is what TAEYONG's new track should be like!"

1516
00:58:06,550 --> 00:58:09,960
(Listen to "Wacka Wak" by TAEYONG on all streaming platforms.)

1517
00:58:09,960 --> 00:58:11,160
(BADA, Back Koo Young, Ha Ram, MINSANG, MIA, Tita, Gyurian,)

1518
00:58:11,160 --> 00:58:12,290
(NOH WON, Tatter, Sowon, Bae Cho Hee, SJEAN, Jeong Ye Won...)

1519
00:58:12,330 --> 00:58:14,230
(Confetti)

1520
00:58:14,230 --> 00:58:16,560
The fans loved it so much.

1521
00:58:17,500 --> 00:58:19,600
They were going, "Blast it over this way!"

1522
00:58:19,600 --> 00:58:21,140
The reaction was incredible.

1523
00:58:21,140 --> 00:58:23,200
Spending hours stamping these by hand...

1524
00:58:23,200 --> 00:58:26,170
was actually worth it.

1525
00:58:26,270 --> 00:58:27,410
If they catch a piece of confetti...

1526
00:58:27,410 --> 00:58:29,310
and see BADA and Back Koo Young's names on it,

1527
00:58:30,080 --> 00:58:31,180
they'll just blow it away.

1528
00:58:31,280 --> 00:58:32,610
The vibe between the two teams is totally different.

1529
00:58:32,710 --> 00:58:34,880
In terms of artist appeal, this team highlights it well,

1530
00:58:34,880 --> 00:58:36,720
while NaiN and BABYZOO's team brings out the dance factor.

1531
00:58:36,720 --> 00:58:39,320
The choice will split depending on...

1532
00:58:39,320 --> 00:58:40,590
what TAEYONG is looking for.

1533
00:58:40,590 --> 00:58:41,920
If he wanted point choreography that sticks in your head,

1534
00:58:41,920 --> 00:58:43,190
it's BADA and Back Koo Young.

1535
00:58:43,190 --> 00:58:44,860
If he wants pure performance power,

1536
00:58:44,860 --> 00:58:47,530
BABYZOO and NaiN's team seems like the better option.

1537
00:58:47,530 --> 00:58:49,460
It's like choosing between sweet potato or potato.

1538
00:58:49,560 --> 00:58:52,000
If you prefer something cleaner and savory, it's potato.

1539
00:58:52,000 --> 00:58:54,400
If you want something sweeter, it's sweet potato.

1540
00:58:54,700 --> 00:58:57,170
I don't think I could watch him promote with that choreography.

1541
00:58:57,170 --> 00:58:58,670
I'd probably burst into tears.

1542
00:58:58,670 --> 00:59:01,340
BABYZOO and NaiN joined forces for a reason.

1543
00:59:01,340 --> 00:59:04,450
I have no doubt TAEYONG felt that.

1544
00:59:04,450 --> 00:59:07,250
I think our piece matched the song's energy much better...

1545
00:59:07,250 --> 00:59:09,050
and carried more impact.

1546
00:59:09,050 --> 00:59:10,180
We must win.

1547
00:59:10,180 --> 00:59:12,150
I think we have way more raw energy.

1548
00:59:12,150 --> 00:59:13,320
I'm expecting a good result.

1549
00:59:13,320 --> 00:59:14,760
(The dream artist who will make the directors' vision come true)

1550
00:59:14,760 --> 00:59:16,520
(BAILEY of ALLDAY PROJECT)

1551
00:59:16,520 --> 00:59:17,990
(Simeez and INGYOO's piece feels very cinematic.)

1552
00:59:17,990 --> 00:59:20,360
(It feels like watching something bigger than a dance performance.)

1553
00:59:20,360 --> 00:59:22,230
(But I think there's a lot we need to try.)

1554
00:59:22,230 --> 00:59:23,830
(The fabric, the shoes)

1555
00:59:23,830 --> 00:59:26,070
(And the whole thing, top to bottom)

1556
00:59:26,170 --> 00:59:27,300
(It was just riddled with risks.)

1557
00:59:27,300 --> 00:59:29,200
(Is the keyword "risk?")

1558
00:59:29,200 --> 00:59:30,470
(With Kasper and MIN JUN,)

1559
00:59:30,470 --> 00:59:31,910
(I definitely feel comfortable.)

1560
00:59:31,910 --> 00:59:32,910
(What a cordial atmosphere.)

1561
00:59:32,910 --> 00:59:33,940
(They must have no risks.)

1562
00:59:33,940 --> 00:59:35,010
(BAILEY looks so comfortable.)

1563
00:59:35,010 --> 00:59:36,840
(I don't think she'd want to repeat what she's already done before.)

1564
00:59:36,840 --> 00:59:38,010
(Being so comfortable...)

1565
00:59:38,110 --> 00:59:39,810
(could be both strength and weakness.)

1566
00:59:39,810 --> 00:59:40,820
(Is that enough?)

1567
00:59:40,820 --> 00:59:42,250
(The unchosen team...)

1568
00:59:42,320 --> 00:59:44,320
(will head straight to the Last Stage.)

1569
00:59:44,320 --> 00:59:47,420
(Which team will be chosen by the artists?)

1570
00:59:47,420 --> 00:59:48,820
(The on-site crowd reaction...)

1571
00:59:48,820 --> 00:59:49,920
(was no joke.)

1572
00:59:49,920 --> 00:59:51,260
(My mind was wavering so much.)

1573
00:59:51,260 --> 00:59:52,330
(I'm not lying.)

1574
00:59:52,330 --> 00:59:53,330
(I have no idea.)

1575
00:59:53,330 --> 00:59:56,560
(Which choreographers will be heading to the Last Stage?)

1576
00:59:57,230 --> 00:59:59,670
- BADA! - What? Hey!

1577
00:59:59,670 --> 01:00:00,670
(MC Sung Hanbin is dropping in to visit BADA during her break.)

1578
01:00:00,670 --> 01:00:04,240
I hear you've been working hard prepping for the mission,

1579
01:00:04,340 --> 01:00:05,440
so I came by to cheer you on.

1580
01:00:05,870 --> 01:00:08,810
Thank you! Thanks for coming.

1581
01:00:08,810 --> 01:00:09,880
How's the preparation going?

1582
01:00:09,880 --> 01:00:11,550
I'm just working hard.

1583
01:00:11,680 --> 01:00:13,850
This is something I've been using a lot lately.

1584
01:00:14,280 --> 01:00:15,620
You sweat a lot during practice, right?

1585
01:00:15,620 --> 01:00:16,850
They say this is great when it gets hot.

1586
01:00:17,720 --> 01:00:19,220
This is what we need now.

1587
01:00:19,220 --> 01:00:20,250
- I know, right? - Yes.

1588
01:00:20,250 --> 01:00:22,220
You can use it with the other choreographers.

1589
01:00:22,820 --> 01:00:24,830
Totally. I should share it with them.

1590
01:00:24,830 --> 01:00:26,930
- Thank you. - Make good use of it.

1591
01:00:27,030 --> 01:00:29,000
Thank you. I will.

1592
01:00:29,000 --> 01:00:30,160
(Simeez is practicing choreography on her own.)

1593
01:00:30,160 --> 01:00:32,600
- Simeez. - BADA!

1594
01:00:32,600 --> 01:00:33,900
How have you been?

1595
01:00:34,870 --> 01:00:36,170
Is the mission prep going well?

1596
01:00:36,270 --> 01:00:37,940
It's going well. We're almost done.

1597
01:00:37,940 --> 01:00:40,040
- Can you take a look at mine? - Sure.

1598
01:00:40,040 --> 01:00:41,040
At first...

1599
01:00:41,040 --> 01:00:43,810
(Watch me.)

1600
01:00:44,680 --> 01:00:46,250
- Is it okay? - It's a total killer.

1601
01:00:46,680 --> 01:00:47,680
This is so cool.

1602
01:00:47,680 --> 01:00:49,480
My face is flushing a bit with heat now.

1603
01:00:49,480 --> 01:00:50,820
You must be feeling hot.

1604
01:00:50,820 --> 01:00:51,920
Do you want to give this a try?

1605
01:00:51,920 --> 01:00:53,860
It's a stick-on serum sheet for your face.

1606
01:00:53,860 --> 01:00:55,160
It's good when your skin heats up.

1607
01:00:55,160 --> 01:00:56,860
A stick-on serum? I've never used one before.

1608
01:00:56,860 --> 01:00:59,560
Open the cap and twist the bottom like this.

1609
01:00:59,960 --> 01:01:01,760
You can pull them out sheet by sheet,

1610
01:01:01,760 --> 01:01:03,000
so it's hygienic.

1611
01:01:03,000 --> 01:01:04,230
Apply this right under your eyes.

1612
01:01:04,230 --> 01:01:05,600
- Really? Nice. - Yes.

1613
01:01:05,600 --> 01:01:08,300
I think it would be amazing to put this on after practice...

1614
01:01:08,300 --> 01:01:09,370
when you're heating up.

1615
01:01:09,370 --> 01:01:11,340
- It's cold. - It feels so cool.

1616
01:01:11,340 --> 01:01:14,510
It feels like your pores are tightening up too.

1617
01:01:14,680 --> 01:01:17,410
The sheet sticks so well to the face...

1618
01:01:17,410 --> 01:01:18,850
that I could just practice like this.

1619
01:01:18,950 --> 01:01:20,050
This is nice.

1620
01:01:20,050 --> 01:01:23,250
(Dancing all of a sudden)

1621
01:01:23,820 --> 01:01:25,090
This isn't falling off.

1622
01:01:25,190 --> 01:01:26,550
It's totally locked onto my face.

1623
01:01:26,550 --> 01:01:27,860
I think it's all absorbed.

1624
01:01:28,190 --> 01:01:29,790
- This is so hydrating. - Right.

1625
01:01:29,790 --> 01:01:32,260
It feels like the heat has cooled down.

1626
01:01:32,260 --> 01:01:33,490
Now let's head back...

1627
01:01:33,490 --> 01:01:35,030
- to practice. - Okay.

1628
01:01:35,130 --> 01:01:36,500
Let's crush this mission.

1629
01:01:36,830 --> 01:01:37,830
Hi.

1630
01:01:37,830 --> 01:01:39,600
- Hi. - Hi.

1631
01:01:39,600 --> 01:01:40,770
(Simeez and INGYOO welcome BAILEY with an extravagant red carpet.)

1632
01:01:40,770 --> 01:01:43,070
Hello.

1633
01:01:43,070 --> 01:01:46,210
- Welcome to the Red World. - The Red World.

1634
01:01:46,270 --> 01:01:47,410
This is crazy.

1635
01:01:48,040 --> 01:01:50,010
We're going to wrap you inside the fabric today.

1636
01:01:50,010 --> 01:01:51,510
Oh, my goodness.

1637
01:01:51,580 --> 01:01:52,810
Look, BAILEY.

1638
01:01:52,810 --> 01:01:56,120
I picked out some heels that are comfortable to dance in.

1639
01:01:56,320 --> 01:01:57,850
Try them on,

1640
01:01:57,850 --> 01:01:59,520
pick whichever feels the most comfortable.

1641
01:01:59,690 --> 01:02:01,690
- Black does look nice. - It's pretty.

1642
01:02:01,820 --> 01:02:03,160
During the practice...

1643
01:02:03,160 --> 01:02:05,130
Do you want this one? BAILEY's choice.

1644
01:02:05,190 --> 01:02:06,560
And INGYOO...

1645
01:02:06,760 --> 01:02:09,200
- Hey, I have a present for you. - What is this?

1646
01:02:09,200 --> 01:02:10,630
I made these pants.

1647
01:02:10,630 --> 01:02:11,670
- This is kind of like... - No way.

1648
01:02:11,670 --> 01:02:13,870
- track-ish, but... - Yes.

1649
01:02:13,870 --> 01:02:14,970
You guys are cool.

1650
01:02:15,240 --> 01:02:17,040
(The welcome gift mission is successful.)

1651
01:02:17,040 --> 01:02:18,340
BAILEY, you should work with us.

1652
01:02:18,340 --> 01:02:20,440
We've got your back, right?

1653
01:02:20,440 --> 01:02:22,180
- We're acting as your stylists. - We're your stylists.

1654
01:02:22,180 --> 01:02:23,210
(They gaslight her into thinking they're even handling her style.)

1655
01:02:23,210 --> 01:02:25,180
- Are you ready to be reborn? - Yes.

1656
01:02:25,180 --> 01:02:27,450
Since our "main dish" just got approved,

1657
01:02:27,450 --> 01:02:28,720
our minds are at ease.

1658
01:02:28,820 --> 01:02:30,250
(Section-by-section results announcement)

1659
01:02:30,920 --> 01:02:32,690
In any case, the killer parts...

1660
01:02:32,690 --> 01:02:34,260
were the intro and the chorus.

1661
01:02:34,260 --> 01:02:37,060
The intro is literally stepping foot into that world.

1662
01:02:37,090 --> 01:02:39,990
Does it really have enough merit...

1663
01:02:39,990 --> 01:02:41,700
to sacrifice her own face for it?

1664
01:02:41,700 --> 01:02:43,060
I don't think so.

1665
01:02:43,060 --> 01:02:44,830
(Which intro section did BAILEY choose?)

1666
01:02:45,000 --> 01:02:46,830
(Intro: Simeez and INGYOO)

1667
01:02:46,930 --> 01:02:49,840
It's just that the color sticks so well.

1668
01:02:49,840 --> 01:02:52,070
It's very memorable. The audience would feel like,

1669
01:02:52,070 --> 01:02:54,240
"Gosh, it feels so theatrical."

1670
01:02:54,240 --> 01:02:56,010
So the concept is locked in.

1671
01:02:56,010 --> 01:02:57,480
The chorus is a part...

1672
01:02:57,480 --> 01:02:58,950
that instantly comes to mind when you hear the song.

1673
01:02:59,010 --> 01:03:01,320
Not having your chorus chosen is the worst-case scenario.

1674
01:03:01,420 --> 01:03:02,780
For the chorus...

1675
01:03:02,920 --> 01:03:04,990
It has so many crazy details.

1676
01:03:04,990 --> 01:03:06,390
I think I can pull it off.

1677
01:03:06,390 --> 01:03:08,090
But somehow it lacks a real impact.

1678
01:03:08,090 --> 01:03:09,290
Because the part was so long,

1679
01:03:09,290 --> 01:03:11,230
it was bound to have some gaps.

1680
01:03:11,230 --> 01:03:14,200
The use of red in the back is just so memorable.

1681
01:03:14,330 --> 01:03:18,470
Using these certain pictures is so clean in my brain.

1682
01:03:18,700 --> 01:03:20,600
(Which chorus section did BAILEY choose?)

1683
01:03:20,740 --> 01:03:22,670
(Chorus 1: Simeez and INGYOO)

1684
01:03:23,070 --> 01:03:24,170
This is it.

1685
01:03:24,170 --> 01:03:26,140
It's really nice that we got the chorus part.

1686
01:03:26,140 --> 01:03:27,880
The direction we had in mind was right after all.

1687
01:03:28,310 --> 01:03:29,840
Okay. The main dish is confirmed.

1688
01:03:30,140 --> 01:03:31,750
She chose our concept for the intro, the two chorus parts,

1689
01:03:31,750 --> 01:03:32,980
and the core backbone.

1690
01:03:33,050 --> 01:03:35,750
She picked ours for the intro,

1691
01:03:35,750 --> 01:03:37,390
the two chorus parts, and the bridge.

1692
01:03:37,390 --> 01:03:39,590
That gave us more conviction about our overall concept.

1693
01:03:39,690 --> 01:03:41,090
It's like salted pollack roe.

1694
01:03:41,720 --> 01:03:42,860
It goes like this.

1695
01:03:42,860 --> 01:03:43,930
(Simeez demonstrates it first.)

1696
01:03:43,930 --> 01:03:45,060
So you drop down like this.

1697
01:03:47,160 --> 01:03:48,160
(Chuckling)

1698
01:03:48,160 --> 01:03:49,200
(The fish is feeling awkward.)

1699
01:03:49,200 --> 01:03:51,000
Get over it! Get over it!

1700
01:03:51,000 --> 01:03:52,200
- Get over it! - Then you do this.

1701
01:03:52,570 --> 01:03:53,770
You get up like this...

1702
01:03:53,770 --> 01:03:55,740
and tear through the fabric.

1703
01:03:56,470 --> 01:03:57,810
You're expressing hardships and adversity.

1704
01:03:57,870 --> 01:03:59,870
The harder it gets, the cooler you look.

1705
01:03:59,870 --> 01:04:01,340
Just like a cocoon.

1706
01:04:01,340 --> 01:04:03,010
- It does look cool, honestly. - It does.

1707
01:04:03,010 --> 01:04:04,280
It feels like a Margiela show.

1708
01:04:05,380 --> 01:04:06,550
It's reversed...

1709
01:04:06,550 --> 01:04:08,180
(The flopping-backwards show)

1710
01:04:09,280 --> 01:04:10,280
Knees to the head.

1711
01:04:10,280 --> 01:04:12,820
The team with INGYOO and Simeez...

1712
01:04:12,950 --> 01:04:14,890
It is really fun. It is fun to do.

1713
01:04:14,890 --> 01:04:16,620
But I definitely can feel...

1714
01:04:16,620 --> 01:04:18,190
Gosh, this is tricky. Okay.

1715
01:04:18,190 --> 01:04:19,290
Controlling the fabric is so tough.

1716
01:04:20,030 --> 01:04:22,330
There's the whole fabric around me,

1717
01:04:22,330 --> 01:04:24,330
so I can easily get lost in that.

1718
01:04:24,330 --> 01:04:26,130
There are visual things that can go wrong.

1719
01:04:26,130 --> 01:04:27,470
There's definitely more risk.

1720
01:04:28,000 --> 01:04:29,840
- Standing on my territory - Standing on my territory

1721
01:04:29,840 --> 01:04:31,770
Then you'll tear through the fabric.

1722
01:04:31,870 --> 01:04:33,040
(Section-by-section results announcement)

1723
01:04:33,040 --> 01:04:34,610
It transitioned straight into Verse One.

1724
01:04:34,840 --> 01:04:36,380
Looking at the pre-chorus,

1725
01:04:36,380 --> 01:04:38,210
I realized she wanted to dance full-out...

1726
01:04:38,210 --> 01:04:39,950
instead of just coasting on concept and visual staging.

1727
01:04:39,950 --> 01:04:42,820
I took it as, "I want to break out of the fabric fast."

1728
01:04:42,820 --> 01:04:43,920
Okay. Got it.

1729
01:04:43,990 --> 01:04:45,120
For Option One,

1730
01:04:45,120 --> 01:04:49,260
I did consider getting rid of the fabric quickly.

1731
01:04:49,620 --> 01:04:50,860
(Initial draft, final version)

1732
01:04:50,860 --> 01:04:52,030
So while keeping the concept,

1733
01:04:52,030 --> 01:04:54,160
we modified the routine so BAILEY could break out earlier.

1734
01:04:54,830 --> 01:04:57,000
And we packed the pre-chorus with more actual dance.

1735
01:04:57,000 --> 01:04:58,570
(Initial draft, final version)

1736
01:04:58,600 --> 01:05:01,100
The outro was originally a krump freestyle,

1737
01:05:01,100 --> 01:05:03,070
but if having that krump theme feels like too much,

1738
01:05:03,070 --> 01:05:04,910
I'll structure it like a dance break.

1739
01:05:04,970 --> 01:05:06,670
I don't want to use krump twice.

1740
01:05:06,740 --> 01:05:08,410
At the end, it should still showcase her own identity.

1741
01:05:08,410 --> 01:05:09,810
I want to finish it off clean,

1742
01:05:09,810 --> 01:05:11,610
bringing out that distinct texture in the movement.

1743
01:05:11,610 --> 01:05:12,680
(Modifying the outro with clean, texture-defining moves)

1744
01:05:12,680 --> 01:05:13,810
(Oh, yes!)

1745
01:05:13,810 --> 01:05:14,880
Sorry.

1746
01:05:14,880 --> 01:05:15,950
(You startled me.)

1747
01:05:15,950 --> 01:05:17,320
That was so cool.

1748
01:05:18,120 --> 01:05:19,320
I was impressed.

1749
01:05:19,790 --> 01:05:21,860
- This is great. - How do you feel, BAILEY?

1750
01:05:22,460 --> 01:05:24,860
- I feel... - You feel...

1751
01:05:24,860 --> 01:05:26,660
I wonder what BAILEY is thinking.

1752
01:05:26,730 --> 01:05:28,700
(Feeling nervous)

1753
01:05:28,860 --> 01:05:31,000
Like way more than an artist than a dancer now.

1754
01:05:31,530 --> 01:05:32,700
It's really interesting.

1755
01:05:32,730 --> 01:05:33,770
That's nice.

1756
01:05:33,770 --> 01:05:35,240
So whom are you going to pick?

1757
01:05:36,170 --> 01:05:39,040
- Don't push her. - I don't speak Korean well.

1758
01:05:39,040 --> 01:05:41,180
I don't know what you're saying. I don't know anything.

1759
01:05:41,310 --> 01:05:43,810
We're working really hard.

1760
01:05:44,510 --> 01:05:46,210
Actually, I'm confident.

1761
01:05:46,210 --> 01:05:48,180
But my concern is...

1762
01:05:48,180 --> 01:05:49,250
the heels.

1763
01:05:49,250 --> 01:05:52,550
It's kind of the key point of the whole performance.

1764
01:05:52,550 --> 01:05:54,920
I feel like it's more than choreo.

1765
01:05:55,260 --> 01:05:57,160
I'm more concerned about...

1766
01:05:57,160 --> 01:05:58,430
taking the heels off.

1767
01:05:59,130 --> 01:06:00,830
If I can't get the heels off,

1768
01:06:01,230 --> 01:06:02,430
there will be no answer, really.

1769
01:06:02,430 --> 01:06:03,500
Okay.

1770
01:06:04,100 --> 01:06:07,440
(The heels are not coming off fast enough on cue.)

1771
01:06:07,440 --> 01:06:09,270
The heels even have zippers on them.

1772
01:06:09,300 --> 01:06:10,570
Are there way too many tasks?

1773
01:06:10,640 --> 01:06:12,670
Taking off the heels is something I'm worried about.

1774
01:06:12,710 --> 01:06:14,840
Should we apply baby powder to the heels of the feet?

1775
01:06:14,840 --> 01:06:17,140
Once the sweat builds up in here...

1776
01:06:17,140 --> 01:06:18,810
BAILEY was going through the same risk...

1777
01:06:18,810 --> 01:06:20,510
I ran into during the demo run.

1778
01:06:20,850 --> 01:06:23,320
(Simeez had the same issue with heels that wouldn't slip off.)

1779
01:06:23,320 --> 01:06:26,320
My feet are sweating so much now that they won't come off.

1780
01:06:27,020 --> 01:06:28,490
Every single obstacle I run into...

1781
01:06:28,490 --> 01:06:30,860
could impact the artist,

1782
01:06:30,860 --> 01:06:32,060
so I was worried.

1783
01:06:32,560 --> 01:06:34,360
Or let's just ask the stylist...

1784
01:06:34,430 --> 01:06:35,830
to attach Velcro instead.

1785
01:06:35,900 --> 01:06:38,500
Zippers are hard to find in a split second,

1786
01:06:38,500 --> 01:06:39,900
so we decided to add Velcro...

1787
01:06:39,900 --> 01:06:42,740
and let the heels slip off in a single motion.

1788
01:06:42,740 --> 01:06:44,070
I think placing it right here would be good.

1789
01:06:44,070 --> 01:06:45,240
- Here? - Yes, around here.

1790
01:06:45,240 --> 01:06:48,810
Right below the part that covers the back of the heel.

1791
01:06:48,810 --> 01:06:51,480
So we will rip this open in the middle of the performance.

1792
01:06:51,480 --> 01:06:55,950
If you have socks and tape on, it won't stick as much.

1793
01:06:56,480 --> 01:06:58,490
Is this all right? Nice.

1794
01:06:58,690 --> 01:07:00,020
- This is Option One for now. - Nice.

1795
01:07:01,520 --> 01:07:03,720
(Even with taping, the heels still refuse to come off smoothly.)

1796
01:07:03,720 --> 01:07:05,830
Do you feel like the taping actually helps?

1797
01:07:05,830 --> 01:07:06,960
What do you think, BAILEY?

1798
01:07:07,030 --> 01:07:08,200
I don't know.

1799
01:07:08,300 --> 01:07:09,630
Actually, it doesn't help.

1800
01:07:09,630 --> 01:07:11,230
I don't know. I can't tell.

1801
01:07:12,230 --> 01:07:13,500
I'll think about other options.

1802
01:07:13,670 --> 01:07:15,900
Just throwing out ideas and taking risks isn't the end of it.

1803
01:07:15,900 --> 01:07:17,910
Finding the actual solution is part of the assignment.

1804
01:07:17,970 --> 01:07:22,240
She's going to understand female artists' personalities and colors.

1805
01:07:22,610 --> 01:07:23,840
If it works,

1806
01:07:23,840 --> 01:07:26,110
I think it can really change the performance.

1807
01:07:26,310 --> 01:07:28,280
I bought both of these.

1808
01:07:28,280 --> 01:07:29,380
(Simeez brought something to the practice room.)

1809
01:07:29,380 --> 01:07:30,750
They are toe socks.

1810
01:07:30,850 --> 01:07:32,620
She's supposed to be the "Hydra Queen," and now...

1811
01:07:32,620 --> 01:07:33,950
You won't be able to tell on stage. I'm serious.

1812
01:07:33,950 --> 01:07:35,060
No one will notice it.

1813
01:07:35,060 --> 01:07:36,690
- So is it like sports taping? - Yes.

1814
01:07:36,790 --> 01:07:38,930
I've danced barefoot before, you know?

1815
01:07:38,930 --> 01:07:42,000
You can't really go full power with bare feet.

1816
01:07:42,060 --> 01:07:44,730
That's why I wore these during the first mission.

1817
01:07:44,730 --> 01:07:45,970
Originally, I was planning to go barefoot.

1818
01:07:46,170 --> 01:07:48,770
And you know that part where she drops hard from the lift?

1819
01:07:48,770 --> 01:07:50,670
- Is it slippery? - The impact goes to your feet.

1820
01:07:50,770 --> 01:07:52,870
We definitely need these for her own safety.

1821
01:07:53,810 --> 01:07:55,540
(The Velcro-modded heels...)

1822
01:07:55,540 --> 01:07:57,550
(and the toe socks are ready.)

1823
01:07:57,680 --> 01:08:01,120
The artist should never feel like there are too many risks.

1824
01:08:01,120 --> 01:08:03,550
So I kept testing it out in heels over and over.

1825
01:08:04,520 --> 01:08:05,650
(Slipping them on...)

1826
01:08:05,650 --> 01:08:06,850
(over and over again)

1827
01:08:07,190 --> 01:08:10,660
(Testing out multiple options, running it again on bare feet.)

1828
01:08:10,830 --> 01:08:12,030
Does it feel much more comfortable wearing the socks?

1829
01:08:12,030 --> 01:08:14,300
I keep alternating between the two options.

1830
01:08:15,060 --> 01:08:17,630
As far as I can see, she must wear the socks.

1831
01:08:18,100 --> 01:08:19,670
I put my foot in wrong.

1832
01:08:20,570 --> 01:08:23,240
(Gradually wearing down...)

1833
01:08:23,240 --> 01:08:27,440
(from the non-stop rehearsal in heels)

1834
01:08:27,440 --> 01:08:29,240
- Listen, Simeez. - Yes?

1835
01:08:29,240 --> 01:08:31,610
We need to review the footage during tomorrow's rehearsal,

1836
01:08:31,610 --> 01:08:33,480
so I think you need to practice the outro choreo a bit.

1837
01:08:33,480 --> 01:08:35,620
- Me? - Yes. Maybe you should.

1838
01:08:35,620 --> 01:08:37,690
Wouldn't it be easier to gauge the full picture that way?

1839
01:08:37,790 --> 01:08:39,450
Aren't I just supposed to be her double?

1840
01:08:39,450 --> 01:08:40,450
I'll just stand in as her double.

1841
01:08:40,450 --> 01:08:42,620
Let's not just phone it in. You don't have to go all out.

1842
01:08:42,620 --> 01:08:43,720
Okay.

1843
01:08:43,720 --> 01:08:45,060
Executing the moves shows...

1844
01:08:45,060 --> 01:08:46,460
the overall picture better than faking it.

1845
01:08:46,490 --> 01:08:47,830
Sloppy moves draw attention.

1846
01:08:48,730 --> 01:08:50,430
(Simeez ran through practice without executing the outro moves,)

1847
01:08:50,430 --> 01:08:52,230
(just to monitor the overall picture.)

1848
01:08:52,300 --> 01:08:54,200
I want you to practice your parts if you can't pull them off.

1849
01:08:54,200 --> 01:08:55,970
I don't want to lose our momentum at the end.

1850
01:08:55,970 --> 01:08:57,740
I don't want to slack off until the very end.

1851
01:08:57,740 --> 01:09:00,140
I want to tie things up as solidly as possible.

1852
01:09:00,140 --> 01:09:02,980
I just said that because I wanted the monitoring to be flawless.

1853
01:09:03,180 --> 01:09:04,250
This is frustrating.

1854
01:09:04,250 --> 01:09:06,250
I had to stand in for BAILEY...

1855
01:09:06,250 --> 01:09:08,280
and double-check that potential risks for the artist...

1856
01:09:08,280 --> 01:09:09,780
went off without a hitch.

1857
01:09:09,780 --> 01:09:12,020
I also had to watch all the performers as a director.

1858
01:09:12,020 --> 01:09:16,260
It felt like I got another lower-priority task to handle.

1859
01:09:16,260 --> 01:09:18,230
I found it overwhelming.

1860
01:09:19,490 --> 01:09:21,400
(Silence is settling between the two after the practice wraps up.)

1861
01:09:21,400 --> 01:09:23,230
Honestly, my entire focus was on BAILEY...

1862
01:09:23,230 --> 01:09:24,700
up until yesterday, too.

1863
01:09:24,700 --> 01:09:25,730
I'm aware of that.

1864
01:09:25,730 --> 01:09:27,900
But when you suddenly asked me to flawlessly execute...

1865
01:09:27,900 --> 01:09:29,100
what BAILEY had practiced...

1866
01:09:29,100 --> 01:09:30,140
for three days,

1867
01:09:30,140 --> 01:09:31,310
I did feel the pressure.

1868
01:09:31,310 --> 01:09:32,570
I just had to bring it up.

1869
01:09:32,640 --> 01:09:34,680
This is the artist's practice video,

1870
01:09:34,680 --> 01:09:36,910
and BAILEY is such a detailed artist,

1871
01:09:36,910 --> 01:09:38,480
so rather than phoning it in like that...

1872
01:09:38,480 --> 01:09:40,610
But I want to focus more on the overall picture too.

1873
01:09:40,610 --> 01:09:41,880
It's stressful for me...

1874
01:09:41,880 --> 01:09:43,150
not being able to watch it, playing the artist.

1875
01:09:43,220 --> 01:09:45,150
I want to step out and monitor it comfortably, too.

1876
01:09:45,150 --> 01:09:46,190
I understand.

1877
01:09:46,190 --> 01:09:47,390
But when you asked me for more,

1878
01:09:47,390 --> 01:09:48,990
I think I felt...

1879
01:09:48,990 --> 01:09:50,320
a little overwhelmed by pressure.

1880
01:09:50,320 --> 01:09:53,060
But I couldn't just say nothing about the outro.

1881
01:09:53,060 --> 01:09:55,100
If you'd just asked, "How about we at least run through the outro?"

1882
01:09:55,100 --> 01:09:56,300
it would've been fine,

1883
01:09:56,300 --> 01:09:58,000
but you're always so aggressive toward me.

1884
01:09:58,000 --> 01:09:59,770
You've never been cautious when talking to me.

1885
01:09:59,770 --> 01:10:01,140
From the demo stages until now.

1886
01:10:01,140 --> 01:10:03,200
That's not true.

1887
01:10:03,200 --> 01:10:05,810
Things like that really hit me hard.

1888
01:10:05,810 --> 01:10:06,840
It puts so much pressure on me.

1889
01:10:06,840 --> 01:10:08,780
It'd be nice if I could soften my words, but that's not easy.

1890
01:10:08,780 --> 01:10:12,250
I think I was overwhelmed trying to direct the big picture...

1891
01:10:14,010 --> 01:10:16,120
and playing the performer at the same time.

1892
01:10:16,120 --> 01:10:17,890
I guess that's why I asked if I could just phone it in.

1893
01:10:18,090 --> 01:10:20,420
Then you can just focus on dancing your part.

1894
01:10:20,420 --> 01:10:23,190
But my own fate is on the line with this piece, too.

1895
01:10:23,220 --> 01:10:24,930
I'm just doing what I need to do.

1896
01:10:25,030 --> 01:10:26,990
It's not like I can put on heels myself.

1897
01:10:27,160 --> 01:10:29,030
We're just covering the blind spots that the other person can't handle.

1898
01:10:29,030 --> 01:10:31,800
I knew how exhausted you were, so I waited until the very end.

1899
01:10:32,500 --> 01:10:33,730
Okay. I'm sorry.

1900
01:10:33,800 --> 01:10:35,840
Because there are parts where I can't help you.

1901
01:10:36,170 --> 01:10:38,310
It's not like I didn't know she was struggling,

1902
01:10:38,310 --> 01:10:41,240
but it made me reflect on the dedication...

1903
01:10:41,240 --> 01:10:42,580
she was pouring into this.

1904
01:10:42,810 --> 01:10:44,850
We will win, no matter what! Let's go!

1905
01:10:44,850 --> 01:10:46,780
Ours will be the absolute coolest performance...

1906
01:10:46,780 --> 01:10:48,620
out of all four teams'.

1907
01:10:48,950 --> 01:10:50,850
(Simeez has mastered the outro despite the ticking clock.)

1908
01:10:50,850 --> 01:10:52,190
I gritted my teeth and pushed through it.

1909
01:10:54,620 --> 01:10:56,290
I was so grateful. Thanks to her,

1910
01:10:56,290 --> 01:10:58,030
we could generate synergy in a professional way.

1911
01:10:58,330 --> 01:11:00,930
We love this performance so much.

1912
01:11:00,930 --> 01:11:03,900
I think it was possible because I did it with INGYOO.

1913
01:11:03,900 --> 01:11:05,670
- There's no way we can lose now. - We did a great job.

1914
01:11:05,670 --> 01:11:07,230
Our routine is so locked in and stable now...

1915
01:11:07,230 --> 01:11:08,300
that there are no risks left now.

1916
01:11:08,370 --> 01:11:11,270
Should I give Kasper's team something to worry about tomorrow?

1917
01:11:11,770 --> 01:11:12,970
How would you do that?

1918
01:11:12,970 --> 01:11:14,280
(Reassured)

1919
01:11:14,280 --> 01:11:15,880
(MIN JUN and Kasper check the results for each section)

1920
01:11:15,880 --> 01:11:16,880
That's how it turned out?

1921
01:11:16,880 --> 01:11:19,780
INGYOO and Simeez took both choruses too.

1922
01:11:20,210 --> 01:11:21,550
Honestly, I don't get it.

1923
01:11:21,720 --> 01:11:23,980
We won way more sections overall,

1924
01:11:24,080 --> 01:11:25,920
but losing the chorus really hurts.

1925
01:11:26,450 --> 01:11:28,520
The chorus went to Simeez and INGYOO.

1926
01:11:28,620 --> 01:11:29,860
That was a huge shock.

1927
01:11:29,990 --> 01:11:32,190
I thought it might turn into another "Whiplash."

1928
01:11:32,360 --> 01:11:35,060
The chorus is what really makes the choreography stick.

1929
01:11:35,200 --> 01:11:37,030
It's the most important part.

1930
01:11:37,030 --> 01:11:40,130
So I wondered if winning more sections even mattered.

1931
01:11:40,130 --> 01:11:41,440
That's what I was thinking.

1932
01:11:41,540 --> 01:11:43,200
Chorus 1, Chorus 2.

1933
01:11:43,370 --> 01:11:45,210
BAILEY hasn't tried anything like that before,

1934
01:11:45,510 --> 01:11:47,740
so I think she wants to try it.

1935
01:11:47,910 --> 01:11:48,980
(Agreeing)

1936
01:11:49,110 --> 01:11:51,250
Like I said... "Let's try something new."

1937
01:11:51,250 --> 01:11:52,450
I think that's what this is.

1938
01:11:52,550 --> 01:11:55,580
It's true that nothing new comes out if you never take a chance.

1939
01:11:55,780 --> 01:11:57,690
But this is a risk.

1940
01:11:57,790 --> 01:12:00,390
I feel like once BAILEY learns it, it'll change right away.

1941
01:12:00,690 --> 01:12:01,960
We shouldn't...

1942
01:12:02,160 --> 01:12:04,290
rush into changing things.

1943
01:12:04,290 --> 01:12:06,190
Right. I have no plans to change it.

1944
01:12:06,690 --> 01:12:08,860
We'll stick with the direction we started with...

1945
01:12:09,100 --> 01:12:10,530
and keep pushing ahead.

1946
01:12:10,530 --> 01:12:12,400
I have zero intention of following INGYOO and Simeez...

1947
01:12:12,400 --> 01:12:14,600
or changing ours to match theirs.

1948
01:12:14,740 --> 01:12:16,770
Our challenge this time is to convince BAILEY.

1949
01:12:17,070 --> 01:12:19,240
- Hello. - Hello.

1950
01:12:19,240 --> 01:12:20,240
Hello.

1951
01:12:20,240 --> 01:12:24,380
Was there anything you felt was lacking in yesterday's video?

1952
01:12:24,810 --> 01:12:26,250
(Oh!)

1953
01:12:26,250 --> 01:12:29,050
What do you think about Chorus Two?

1954
01:12:29,320 --> 01:12:30,850
If I just look at the choreography,

1955
01:12:30,850 --> 01:12:33,020
even when I saw it the first time, I really liked the choreography.

1956
01:12:33,020 --> 01:12:34,320
(Satisfied)

1957
01:12:34,320 --> 01:12:36,490
Then if I look at it from more of a...

1958
01:12:37,730 --> 01:12:41,100
Do you think it's better to repeat choreography and have one chorus?

1959
01:12:41,300 --> 01:12:45,030
(Different choreography for choruses 1 and 2)

1960
01:12:45,030 --> 01:12:47,070
From a viewer... Just like so much information.

1961
01:12:47,170 --> 01:12:50,070
If another girl group or solo artist were doing this,

1962
01:12:50,070 --> 01:12:51,410
we'd combine verses 1 and 2,

1963
01:12:51,410 --> 01:12:53,010
- and make verse three different. - Right.

1964
01:12:53,010 --> 01:12:54,110
That's the usual formula.

1965
01:12:54,110 --> 01:12:58,310
But I wanted to move away from that.

1966
01:12:59,080 --> 01:13:01,780
I think the reason I wanted to show this side of you is...

1967
01:13:01,920 --> 01:13:03,750
This is your first time as a soloist.

1968
01:13:03,750 --> 01:13:06,220
And I think that first step is really important.

1969
01:13:06,220 --> 01:13:08,490
People know BAILEY can dance.

1970
01:13:08,490 --> 01:13:11,990
But some may not realize just how good you are.

1971
01:13:12,530 --> 01:13:13,530
Right.

1972
01:13:13,530 --> 01:13:14,730
I also wanted to show that...

1973
01:13:14,730 --> 01:13:18,670
your talent alone is enough to carry a performance.

1974
01:13:18,800 --> 01:13:21,870
I wanted to show the K-pop world what you can do.

1975
01:13:22,270 --> 01:13:25,370
I can tell they intentionally put that hat on...

1976
01:13:25,710 --> 01:13:28,040
to make it, which I think is a really big strength.

1977
01:13:28,140 --> 01:13:29,640
I mean, I haven't danced...

1978
01:13:29,640 --> 01:13:31,610
I haven't really danced in a long time.

1979
01:13:31,610 --> 01:13:33,310
Then come along with us.

1980
01:13:33,850 --> 01:13:34,920
(Bailey is sold.)

1981
01:13:34,920 --> 01:13:35,980
- Let's go. - I'll...

1982
01:13:36,180 --> 01:13:37,990
My job is to make her feel like she can do it.

1983
01:13:37,990 --> 01:13:39,120
So I pushed for it.

1984
01:13:39,220 --> 01:13:41,290
- Shall we try it? - Yes.

1985
01:13:41,760 --> 01:13:45,460
(A difficult intro move hanging upside down)

1986
01:13:45,660 --> 01:13:46,830
Hold her feet.

1987
01:13:46,830 --> 01:13:49,000
(BAILEY tries it right away.)

1988
01:13:50,260 --> 01:13:51,730
Yes.

1989
01:13:51,930 --> 01:13:53,230
Now lower her.

1990
01:13:53,870 --> 01:13:56,800
This leg first. Yes, and if you drop forward like that...

1991
01:13:56,800 --> 01:13:58,040
(She lands perfectly with a cartwheel.)

1992
01:13:58,040 --> 01:13:59,240
- That's it. - Was that right?

1993
01:13:59,240 --> 01:14:00,240
Yes.

1994
01:14:00,340 --> 01:14:01,780
Want to try it with the music?

1995
01:14:01,780 --> 01:14:02,980
I know you can do it.

1996
01:14:03,480 --> 01:14:04,480
Okay.

1997
01:14:07,950 --> 01:14:09,950
(She nails it right away.)

1998
01:14:10,120 --> 01:14:11,250
That was amazing.

1999
01:14:11,290 --> 01:14:13,220
She's on another level.

2000
01:14:13,220 --> 01:14:16,090
She nailed the intro on her first try.

2001
01:14:16,460 --> 01:14:18,960
I feel that thrill of working with people at this level...

2002
01:14:18,960 --> 01:14:20,860
every moment of rehearsal.

2003
01:14:21,030 --> 01:14:22,930
BAILEY memorizes it so quickly...

2004
01:14:22,930 --> 01:14:24,800
and picks things up so fast.

2005
01:14:24,800 --> 01:14:26,130
It makes me so happy.

2006
01:14:26,500 --> 01:14:27,940
It's such a relief.

2007
01:14:28,040 --> 01:14:29,300
This is BAILEY.

2008
01:14:29,440 --> 01:14:30,940
I made a suit just for her.

2009
01:14:30,940 --> 01:14:32,540
She only had to put it on.

2010
01:14:32,640 --> 01:14:34,140
I was also feeling like that.

2011
01:14:34,140 --> 01:14:36,280
I just feel really comfortable in it. It feels like me.

2012
01:14:36,280 --> 01:14:39,750
And I think that was a really smart direction too.

2013
01:14:39,880 --> 01:14:41,480
Seeing it made me even more sure.

2014
01:14:41,480 --> 01:14:43,280
I showed it to MIN JUN and said, "Look at this."

2015
01:14:43,620 --> 01:14:45,220
And that gave him a real boost of confidence.

2016
01:14:45,220 --> 01:14:46,550
That's the biggest problem.

2017
01:14:46,650 --> 01:14:49,960
We were trying to revise the outro together,

2018
01:14:50,090 --> 01:14:51,990
but he kept doing it his way.

2019
01:14:52,690 --> 01:14:53,730
Of course I did.

2020
01:14:53,730 --> 01:14:55,660
The outro choreography BAILEY chose...

2021
01:14:55,660 --> 01:14:56,930
I made that, didn't I?

2022
01:14:56,930 --> 01:14:58,600
Well, yes. He did.

2023
01:14:58,730 --> 01:15:01,070
But we were going to revise it whether it got picked or not.

2024
01:15:01,070 --> 01:15:03,340
Actually, I'm less happy with the part of mine she chose.

2025
01:15:03,570 --> 01:15:04,570
The outro feels a little...

2026
01:15:04,570 --> 01:15:06,270
The scale, for one thing.

2027
01:15:06,470 --> 01:15:08,740
We'd discussed it separately too.

2028
01:15:08,740 --> 01:15:11,080
We revised the outro 4 or 5 times.

2029
01:15:11,080 --> 01:15:13,450
It's hard to call it K-pop.

2030
01:15:13,550 --> 01:15:15,920
In K-pop, there's a formula...

2031
01:15:15,980 --> 01:15:17,420
for an outro.

2032
01:15:17,420 --> 01:15:19,220
A typical outro has a lot of big beats.

2033
01:15:19,650 --> 01:15:20,950
The moves should be bigger...

2034
01:15:20,950 --> 01:15:23,420
with more scale and energy.

2035
01:15:24,090 --> 01:15:26,490
But MIN JUN keeps the movement too contained.

2036
01:15:27,530 --> 01:15:29,060
The outro needs a jump...

2037
01:15:29,060 --> 01:15:30,960
or some kind of change in scene.

2038
01:15:30,960 --> 01:15:32,500
It needs to hit harder.

2039
01:15:32,600 --> 01:15:34,370
I agree it needs more scale.

2040
01:15:34,370 --> 01:15:36,570
But this is BAILEY.

2041
01:15:36,570 --> 01:15:38,270
She uses a lot of hand movements...

2042
01:15:38,270 --> 01:15:39,640
and knows exactly when to blend...

2043
01:15:39,640 --> 01:15:42,140
control and rhythm.

2044
01:15:42,240 --> 01:15:43,810
We already have so much detail.

2045
01:15:43,940 --> 01:15:45,980
There's the hand movement in the verse intro.

2046
01:15:46,250 --> 01:15:47,780
In the bridge,

2047
01:15:48,050 --> 01:15:49,620
and even in the pre-chorus too.

2048
01:15:49,880 --> 01:15:52,090
If we keep adding detail after detail...

2049
01:15:52,290 --> 01:15:53,590
That's one drawback on top of another.

2050
01:15:53,590 --> 01:15:54,590
I completely disagree.

2051
01:15:54,590 --> 01:15:56,790
A mega crew formation makes it look bigger.

2052
01:15:56,890 --> 01:15:58,890
But if the moves are big too,

2053
01:15:58,890 --> 01:16:00,890
and we don't keep it clean,

2054
01:16:00,890 --> 01:16:03,100
we lose that crew synergy.

2055
01:16:03,100 --> 01:16:04,930
The outro choreography BAILEY chose...

2056
01:16:04,930 --> 01:16:06,830
It was chosen because she thought this choreography...

2057
01:16:06,830 --> 01:16:08,770
would look great with a mega crew.

2058
01:16:08,940 --> 01:16:09,940
This is a problem.

2059
01:16:09,940 --> 01:16:11,340
He must have thought this was...

2060
01:16:11,340 --> 01:16:12,940
a BAILEY K-pop mega crew mission.

2061
01:16:13,170 --> 01:16:14,440
K-pop was my specialty,

2062
01:16:14,440 --> 01:16:15,910
so I could've told MIN JUN...

2063
01:16:15,910 --> 01:16:18,280
to stay out of it too.

2064
01:16:18,480 --> 01:16:19,880
But I didn't because...

2065
01:16:20,110 --> 01:16:22,150
I wanted MIN JUN to learn the K-pop style,

2066
01:16:22,150 --> 01:16:25,150
not just competition style. I kept giving him feedback,

2067
01:16:25,320 --> 01:16:27,320
but it was hard to get him to budge.

2068
01:16:27,520 --> 01:16:29,020
So I thought I'd have to let it go.

2069
01:16:29,220 --> 01:16:30,590
I could be wrong.

2070
01:16:30,590 --> 01:16:32,260
Let's do it your way, MIN JUN.

2071
01:16:32,530 --> 01:16:34,160
Seven, eight, and...

2072
01:16:34,160 --> 01:16:35,900
One, two, two.

2073
01:16:36,860 --> 01:16:38,330
(Where is BAILEY?)

2074
01:16:38,330 --> 01:16:39,370
Left, right, kick, kick, kick.

2075
01:16:39,370 --> 01:16:40,430
And left, right.

2076
01:16:40,430 --> 01:16:41,670
(BAILEY rehearses off to the side.)

2077
01:16:42,000 --> 01:16:43,840
What's going on? Why is he doing this all of a sudden?

2078
01:16:43,940 --> 01:16:45,610
I figured he had a reason,

2079
01:16:45,610 --> 01:16:47,210
so I watched for the time being.

2080
01:16:47,510 --> 01:16:48,510
On shoulders.

2081
01:16:48,510 --> 01:16:50,510
(The rehearsal continues with BAILEY off to the side.)

2082
01:16:50,810 --> 01:16:51,810
Okay.

2083
01:16:53,010 --> 01:16:54,450
MIN JUN must be out of his mind.

2084
01:16:54,510 --> 01:16:57,080
When you're teaching, BAILEY should come first,

2085
01:16:57,320 --> 01:17:00,650
and the dancers should learn afterward.

2086
01:17:00,650 --> 01:17:02,590
Leaving the artist off to the side?

2087
01:17:02,590 --> 01:17:04,060
That makes no sense to me.

2088
01:17:05,260 --> 01:17:07,090
I went straight over to take care of BAILEY.

2089
01:17:07,760 --> 01:17:08,960
- Over here. - Okay.

2090
01:17:09,530 --> 01:17:10,800
- The center. - I was taken care of...

2091
01:17:10,800 --> 01:17:12,270
as an artist thanks to KASPER.

2092
01:17:12,270 --> 01:17:13,500
I deliberately didn't do that.

2093
01:17:13,500 --> 01:17:14,670
I had my reasons.

2094
01:17:14,670 --> 01:17:16,170
Getting the dancers perfectly in sync...

2095
01:17:16,170 --> 01:17:19,210
for such a detail-heavy performance was important,

2096
01:17:19,210 --> 01:17:20,640
so I focused on the dancers.

2097
01:17:20,810 --> 01:17:23,740
BAILEY had no trouble memorizing it.

2098
01:17:23,810 --> 01:17:25,050
She picked it up so well.

2099
01:17:25,250 --> 01:17:27,680
I couldn't really understand him.

2100
01:17:28,220 --> 01:17:29,750
Let's mark it through once.

2101
01:17:29,750 --> 01:17:31,420
- Sounds good. - Let's mark it through.

2102
01:17:31,420 --> 01:17:33,990
Dancers, about your exact positions and the other details,

2103
01:17:33,990 --> 01:17:35,620
I'll go over them with you again...

2104
01:17:35,620 --> 01:17:37,860
after this rehearsal.

2105
01:17:37,860 --> 01:17:38,860
- Okay. - Okay.

2106
01:17:38,860 --> 01:17:41,700
We don't get much time to rehearse with the artist,

2107
01:17:41,730 --> 01:17:45,070
so when she's here, the focus should be on her.

2108
01:17:45,070 --> 01:17:46,870
He needs to run it with her, see how it looks,

2109
01:17:46,870 --> 01:17:49,970
make changes and solve problems. That's part of the director's job.

2110
01:17:49,970 --> 01:17:53,070
MIN JUN doesn't have much experience with that.

2111
01:17:53,170 --> 01:17:56,110
From that point on, I felt like he didn't really...

2112
01:17:56,210 --> 01:17:58,180
see me as a director on the same level as him.

2113
01:17:58,310 --> 01:18:00,710
Could you lean back as you move this way?

2114
01:18:00,710 --> 01:18:02,780
Let's fix it later and move on.

2115
01:18:02,920 --> 01:18:04,990
Like this, bam, bam, bam. They get up 1 by 1...

2116
01:18:04,990 --> 01:18:06,950
We'll do verse one first...

2117
01:18:07,150 --> 01:18:08,760
Then go straight to the outro and call it a day?

2118
01:18:09,020 --> 01:18:10,260
We got through a lot today.

2119
01:18:10,260 --> 01:18:11,390
(Awkward)

2120
01:18:11,390 --> 01:18:13,530
Am I being sidelined here?

2121
01:18:13,730 --> 01:18:15,260
I can see why he'd feel that way.

2122
01:18:15,260 --> 01:18:18,370
Either way, we have very little time.

2123
01:18:18,430 --> 01:18:20,100
We need to pick what to focus on,

2124
01:18:20,100 --> 01:18:23,040
but we keep going over things again and again.

2125
01:18:23,200 --> 01:18:25,810
K-pop is a race against time, with the artist at its center.

2126
01:18:25,970 --> 01:18:27,670
I wanted MIN JUN to know that.

2127
01:18:27,910 --> 01:18:30,780
So I took over the rehearsal.

2128
01:18:32,010 --> 01:18:33,110
Let's go for the rehearsal!

2129
01:18:33,250 --> 01:18:35,150
Let's see what they've prepared.

2130
01:18:35,150 --> 01:18:36,550
Who are we strangling?

2131
01:18:36,550 --> 01:18:38,390
Team Kasper and MIN JUN.

2132
01:18:38,450 --> 01:18:40,690
It's time for your rehearsal. Please come on in.

2133
01:18:40,690 --> 01:18:41,690
You got this!

2134
01:18:41,690 --> 01:18:43,190
(With the other team watching)

2135
01:18:43,420 --> 01:18:44,990
Come on up. Everybody, come on up.

2136
01:18:45,290 --> 01:18:48,700
For starters, we'd won on costumes.

2137
01:18:49,130 --> 01:18:51,800
The dancers' outfits were kind of confusing too.

2138
01:18:52,030 --> 01:18:53,730
The male dancers wore leather pants...

2139
01:18:53,870 --> 01:18:56,600
with these shoulder accents,

2140
01:18:56,600 --> 01:18:58,770
but I couldn't tell what went with what.

2141
01:18:58,770 --> 01:19:01,880
The female dancers wore full-body suits,

2142
01:19:01,880 --> 01:19:03,280
and it all felt a little busy.

2143
01:19:05,380 --> 01:19:06,380
What's up!

2144
01:19:06,750 --> 01:19:08,720
BAILEY is coming in.

2145
01:19:08,720 --> 01:19:09,780
Hello.

2146
01:19:10,120 --> 01:19:11,120
She's finally here.

2147
01:19:11,120 --> 01:19:12,790
I wanted to see what she'd do.

2148
01:19:13,250 --> 01:19:15,190
Let's run the rehearsal.

2149
01:19:21,560 --> 01:19:24,000
That was insane! That's exactly what we wanted.

2150
01:19:24,330 --> 01:19:26,770
She added a little BAILEY flavor,

2151
01:19:26,770 --> 01:19:28,940
and it looked great. I was really happy with it.

2152
01:19:31,000 --> 01:19:32,110
Wait, what?

2153
01:19:32,370 --> 01:19:34,240
Now it looks just like ours.

2154
01:19:34,940 --> 01:19:36,810
There are a lot of similarities.

2155
01:19:37,010 --> 01:19:39,250
A lot of similarities.

2156
01:19:39,810 --> 01:19:41,310
They changed the outro a lot too.

2157
01:19:41,650 --> 01:19:42,680
To look like ours.

2158
01:19:43,250 --> 01:19:45,050
After the interim choreography evaluation,

2159
01:19:45,050 --> 01:19:46,390
it didn't feel like they'd built on their idea.

2160
01:19:46,390 --> 01:19:49,260
It felt more like they'd changed its shape to match ours.

2161
01:19:49,320 --> 01:19:50,520
In pre-chorus one,

2162
01:19:50,520 --> 01:19:52,890
I don't remember that being their original formation.

2163
01:19:53,260 --> 01:19:54,590
(In their concept video,)

2164
01:19:54,590 --> 01:19:57,360
(BAILEY broke through the fabric alone.)

2165
01:19:58,030 --> 01:20:00,130
They'd changed it to a triangle formation.

2166
01:20:00,130 --> 01:20:01,330
(Changed to the same triangle formation as his team)

2167
01:20:01,430 --> 01:20:04,700
And in verse two, they suddenly had a diagonal formation.

2168
01:20:04,700 --> 01:20:05,870
Just like ours.

2169
01:20:05,910 --> 01:20:10,240
(The original choreography used a circular formation.)

2170
01:20:10,240 --> 01:20:11,850
(But it was changed to the same diagonal formation.)

2171
01:20:11,850 --> 01:20:13,310
(Team Simeez and INGYOO's rehearsal)

2172
01:20:13,510 --> 01:20:16,050
And everyone dying at the end of the outro...

2173
01:20:16,180 --> 01:20:18,950
They didn't do that before. Now they drop on the big hit.

2174
01:20:19,290 --> 01:20:21,560
It felt like they'd copied our team's guidelines exactly.

2175
01:20:21,690 --> 01:20:22,990
It got so boring.

2176
01:20:22,990 --> 01:20:25,560
It wasn't fun to compete anymore.

2177
01:20:25,560 --> 01:20:26,690
I was really disappointed.

2178
01:20:26,830 --> 01:20:28,400
(The rehearsal continues as they check the stage and choreography.)

2179
01:20:28,400 --> 01:20:29,700
(But then...)

2180
01:20:30,030 --> 01:20:31,970
(BAILEY misses her cue to take off her heels.)

2181
01:20:32,070 --> 01:20:33,330
(Flustered)

2182
01:20:34,030 --> 01:20:35,600
I really don't like that.

2183
01:20:35,800 --> 01:20:37,170
The way she takes off her heels.

2184
01:20:37,670 --> 01:20:38,740
(The lift section follows.)

2185
01:20:38,740 --> 01:20:40,210
(Slip)

2186
01:20:40,210 --> 01:20:41,540
Oh, she slipped!

2187
01:20:42,410 --> 01:20:43,980
We won. We've got this.

2188
01:20:44,640 --> 01:20:46,380
There were quite a few mishaps onstage.

2189
01:20:46,380 --> 01:20:48,520
With so many risky build-ups,

2190
01:20:48,520 --> 01:20:50,720
I didn't think it would come together well.

2191
01:20:50,750 --> 01:20:53,790
I kept thinking we might win.

2192
01:20:54,020 --> 01:20:55,560
I can't say I didn't expect it.

2193
01:20:55,690 --> 01:20:58,260
That section had me worried.

2194
01:20:58,530 --> 01:21:00,890
But taking those kinds of risks...

2195
01:21:00,890 --> 01:21:02,800
can take a performance to the next level.

2196
01:21:02,800 --> 01:21:04,360
It was a bold choice.

2197
01:21:04,760 --> 01:21:07,000
Wait, that's not BAILEY, right?

2198
01:21:07,070 --> 01:21:08,100
Look at her.

2199
01:21:08,100 --> 01:21:09,470
She looks uncomfortable.

2200
01:21:09,470 --> 01:21:11,740
The person onstage can feel it...

2201
01:21:11,740 --> 01:21:12,970
how they're coming across.

2202
01:21:12,970 --> 01:21:14,370
One thing we can't forget is...

2203
01:21:14,370 --> 01:21:15,680
that she's a female artist.

2204
01:21:15,680 --> 01:21:18,750
She's grimacing onstage...

2205
01:21:19,080 --> 01:21:21,010
when they have far less choreography than we do.

2206
01:21:21,010 --> 01:21:22,950
She has way too much to worry about.

2207
01:21:22,950 --> 01:21:24,380
It was full of risks.

2208
01:21:24,380 --> 01:21:26,920
I thought, "Is 'risk' their theme?"

2209
01:21:27,190 --> 01:21:28,960
(Annoyed)

2210
01:21:29,460 --> 01:21:32,830
Let's begin Team JEONG MIN JUN and Kasper's rehearsal.

2211
01:21:33,030 --> 01:21:34,360
- Hello. - Hello.

2212
01:21:34,360 --> 01:21:36,060
- Hello. - Hello.

2213
01:21:36,060 --> 01:21:37,460
How are you feeling?

2214
01:21:37,530 --> 01:21:38,530
Did you get any sleep?

2215
01:21:38,530 --> 01:21:41,870
About 3 or 4 hours? Not bad.

2216
01:21:41,870 --> 01:21:44,240
I felt bad watching you earlier.

2217
01:21:44,240 --> 01:21:45,370
Really?

2218
01:21:45,670 --> 01:21:47,310
- Why? - I really felt bad for you.

2219
01:21:48,310 --> 01:21:50,510
(Just then!)

2220
01:21:50,740 --> 01:21:52,050
I felt bad watching you earlier.

2221
01:21:52,050 --> 01:21:55,120
(INGYOO happens to overhear Kasper.)

2222
01:21:55,950 --> 01:21:57,820
What? Why would he say that?

2223
01:21:57,820 --> 01:21:59,120
It made me angry.

2224
01:21:59,550 --> 01:22:01,590
They're all chummy over there.

2225
01:22:01,720 --> 01:22:03,790
(Simeez watches Team JEONG MIN JUN and Kasper.)

2226
01:22:04,220 --> 01:22:06,790
Kasper said it hurt to watch ours.

2227
01:22:07,230 --> 01:22:08,660
- Why? - I don't know.

2228
01:22:09,000 --> 01:22:10,160
Because we had so much trouble?

2229
01:22:10,160 --> 01:22:11,160
Did he say that to you?

2230
01:22:11,160 --> 01:22:12,300
To BAILEY.

2231
01:22:13,230 --> 01:22:14,230
I...

2232
01:22:14,400 --> 01:22:15,940
But why would he be upset?

2233
01:22:15,940 --> 01:22:17,600
It's true their routine is risky.

2234
01:22:17,600 --> 01:22:19,370
I didn't make anything up.

2235
01:22:19,370 --> 01:22:21,570
If they heard me, that's fine. I said it out in the open.

2236
01:22:21,570 --> 01:22:22,980
I wasn't talking behind their backs.

2237
01:22:22,980 --> 01:22:24,210
Look at that forked tongue.

2238
01:22:24,210 --> 01:22:26,010
So he's the albino snake.

2239
01:22:26,010 --> 01:22:28,520
The albino snake has forbidden fruit in his mouth,

2240
01:22:28,520 --> 01:22:30,280
and he's flicking his tongue.

2241
01:22:30,880 --> 01:22:31,890
That's really sly.

2242
01:22:31,890 --> 01:22:34,790
At least we didn't compare ours to their routine.

2243
01:22:34,790 --> 01:22:35,790
It rubbed me the wrong way.

2244
01:22:35,790 --> 01:22:37,060
Is he that confident?

2245
01:22:37,790 --> 01:22:39,560
Can we do all the tech checks now?

2246
01:22:39,560 --> 01:22:40,960
Okay, let's see how good they are.

2247
01:22:41,190 --> 01:22:43,360
We were pretty much ready.

2248
01:22:43,360 --> 01:22:46,230
Checking the lighting cues was the main priority.

2249
01:22:51,200 --> 01:22:55,040
Director, can we cut all the decorative lights in verses 1 and 2?

2250
01:22:55,240 --> 01:22:58,240
They set the mood onstage,

2251
01:22:58,410 --> 01:22:59,710
and they can look flashy,

2252
01:22:59,710 --> 01:23:01,310
but I didn't think they suited this song.

2253
01:23:01,310 --> 01:23:04,020
Using every light doesn't make a performance better.

2254
01:23:04,020 --> 01:23:06,590
You need to know when to use them and when to leave them out.

2255
01:23:06,690 --> 01:23:07,820
(Decorative lights off)

2256
01:23:07,820 --> 01:23:10,660
Their lighting design is seriously top-notch.

2257
01:23:10,660 --> 01:23:11,990
Kasper's the best here.

2258
01:23:12,390 --> 01:23:13,930
That lighting looks great.

2259
01:23:13,930 --> 01:23:16,060
I like that. A single-color laser.

2260
01:23:16,060 --> 01:23:18,060
They've killed all the other lights and gone with just that.

2261
01:23:18,060 --> 01:23:19,430
Could we use that somewhere too?

2262
01:23:19,430 --> 01:23:20,570
Let's use it right away.

2263
01:23:21,530 --> 01:23:23,400
And when you throw the shoe,

2264
01:23:23,400 --> 01:23:26,610
I think if you just toss it from here,

2265
01:23:26,610 --> 01:23:27,870
it'll land about there.

2266
01:23:27,870 --> 01:23:29,110
- Can I try it? - Sure.

2267
01:23:30,740 --> 01:23:31,980
Looks like she's taking the heel off too.

2268
01:23:32,210 --> 01:23:34,250
Hey, she's taking her shoe off too. That's funny.

2269
01:23:36,580 --> 01:23:37,850
(She even throws it at the same point.)

2270
01:23:37,850 --> 01:23:38,990
You don't have to throw it as hard.

2271
01:23:38,990 --> 01:23:41,250
Taking off and throwing her heel? That wasn't there before.

2272
01:23:42,060 --> 01:23:44,990
(She takes off the heel she's wearing and hurls it.)

2273
01:23:44,990 --> 01:23:47,860
(That was also in the concept video of Simeez and INGYOO.)

2274
01:23:48,130 --> 01:23:49,830
- They saw ours. - Yes.

2275
01:23:49,830 --> 01:23:51,660
They're copying everything?

2276
01:23:51,660 --> 01:23:52,800
I hate this.

2277
01:23:53,200 --> 01:23:54,800
No, we had that from the start.

2278
01:23:54,800 --> 01:23:55,870
From the start.

2279
01:23:56,300 --> 01:23:58,510
The first thing I thought was...

2280
01:23:58,510 --> 01:24:00,970
There's a bridge, then there's an outro.

2281
01:24:00,970 --> 01:24:05,250
I wanted a scene change somewhere in this part.

2282
01:24:05,250 --> 01:24:06,950
She starts off in heels, then takes them off,

2283
01:24:06,950 --> 01:24:09,680
and goes into a section where she's in total control.

2284
01:24:09,680 --> 01:24:11,990
That will be a whole different section.

2285
01:24:11,990 --> 01:24:15,290
That should be a clear shift into a new scene.

2286
01:24:15,520 --> 01:24:17,860
We'd planned for her to take off her shoes all along.

2287
01:24:17,860 --> 01:24:21,160
I'd even planned out the camera work.

2288
01:24:21,160 --> 01:24:24,060
We deliberately left it out of the concept video.

2289
01:24:24,060 --> 01:24:25,400
We didn't want to show it yet.

2290
01:24:25,400 --> 01:24:27,230
I'd have to want to copy them.

2291
01:24:27,230 --> 01:24:29,300
There's nothing worth copying, so how could I?

2292
01:24:29,300 --> 01:24:31,340
Are you kidding me? This is fun. Keep going.

2293
01:24:31,340 --> 01:24:33,140
What was hardest about performing with Team Simeez and INGYOO?

2294
01:24:33,370 --> 01:24:35,680
Just... There are a lot of things.

2295
01:24:35,880 --> 01:24:37,540
The shoes, for one.

2296
01:24:37,540 --> 01:24:39,180
It's all so hectic.

2297
01:24:39,180 --> 01:24:40,280
It looks that way.

2298
01:24:40,280 --> 01:24:41,710
It's nerve-racking to watch too.

2299
01:24:41,920 --> 01:24:44,120
It felt like we were in for a showdown today.

2300
01:24:44,120 --> 01:24:46,090
They must've been really focused on us.

2301
01:24:46,090 --> 01:24:48,390
They kept bringing us up to BAILEY.

2302
01:24:48,460 --> 01:24:49,760
We just have to give it our all.

2303
01:24:49,760 --> 01:24:51,320
We can't lose to them now, can we?

2304
01:24:51,420 --> 01:24:52,590
What do you think?

2305
01:24:52,590 --> 01:24:53,890
- Looks cool. - The shoes.

2306
01:24:53,890 --> 01:24:54,960
No, seriously.

2307
01:24:54,960 --> 01:24:57,860
I was on edge the whole time I was watching you.

2308
01:24:57,860 --> 01:24:59,200
(Team Simeez and INGYOO's rehearsal)

2309
01:24:59,200 --> 01:25:00,870
They just missed the lift,

2310
01:25:01,230 --> 01:25:02,800
and BAILEY says their choreography is harder for her to do.

2311
01:25:02,800 --> 01:25:04,340
It doesn't suit the way she moves.

2312
01:25:04,340 --> 01:25:05,870
Look at her face right now.

2313
01:25:06,070 --> 01:25:07,740
She looks uncomfortable.

2314
01:25:07,740 --> 01:25:09,310
Be honest, that wasn't fun, was it?

2315
01:25:09,480 --> 01:25:11,180
(Awkward)

2316
01:25:11,410 --> 01:25:12,880
From the artist's perspective,

2317
01:25:12,880 --> 01:25:16,520
comments like that could make her feel uneasy.

2318
01:25:16,520 --> 01:25:20,690
I thought we should help BAILEY feel more at ease.

2319
01:25:20,890 --> 01:25:22,290
- Come on, let's go. - Let's go.

2320
01:25:24,060 --> 01:25:25,430
But this is fun. It really is.

2321
01:25:25,430 --> 01:25:26,430
Really?

2322
01:25:26,430 --> 01:25:27,790
Anyway, that's good.

2323
01:25:28,330 --> 01:25:29,430
(Simeez and INGYOO wait for BAILEY.)

2324
01:25:29,430 --> 01:25:30,500
Oh, there's BAILEY.

2325
01:25:30,500 --> 01:25:32,500
- BAILEY, aren't you tired? - Hello.

2326
01:25:32,500 --> 01:25:35,440
I know you're standing on the edge.

2327
01:25:35,770 --> 01:25:37,640
(A little!)

2328
01:25:37,640 --> 01:25:39,370
- That's crazy. - How do you feel?

2329
01:25:39,640 --> 01:25:42,410
Me? It feels kind of weird.

2330
01:25:42,940 --> 01:25:44,740
Like somebody's cheating on me.

2331
01:25:44,740 --> 01:25:46,310
I feel like I'm cheating right now.

2332
01:25:46,880 --> 01:25:48,110
Seriously.

2333
01:25:48,110 --> 01:25:49,920
It feels kind of awkward, but...

2334
01:25:49,920 --> 01:25:51,180
I pretend it looks good.

2335
01:25:51,450 --> 01:25:52,950
The artist can sense all of that.

2336
01:25:52,950 --> 01:25:55,020
She'd know it was a dig at the other team.

2337
01:25:55,020 --> 01:25:58,320
And with BAILEY, comments like that would make her uncomfortable.

2338
01:25:58,320 --> 01:26:00,030
Let's not compare ourselves to the other team.

2339
01:26:00,030 --> 01:26:02,130
Let's not bring that up with her.

2340
01:26:02,530 --> 01:26:03,800
- Are you having fun? - Yes.

2341
01:26:04,160 --> 01:26:05,400
I'm glad.

2342
01:26:06,570 --> 01:26:08,740
It's been years since you've had a challenge like this, right?

2343
01:26:09,170 --> 01:26:11,470
A real challenge, it is.

2344
01:26:11,470 --> 01:26:14,140
Props, heels, barefoot krumping.

2345
01:26:14,140 --> 01:26:17,910
A performance with so many things to pull off...

2346
01:26:17,910 --> 01:26:20,850
might be a first in K-pop history.

2347
01:26:20,850 --> 01:26:24,120
The whole concept only worked because it was BAILEY.

2348
01:26:24,120 --> 01:26:27,090
After putting this much into it,

2349
01:26:27,250 --> 01:26:28,320
we have to win.

2350
01:26:28,420 --> 01:26:30,260
We won't let our guard down.

2351
01:26:30,490 --> 01:26:32,790
We'll shoot the Ronin footage first. The Ronin footage.

2352
01:26:33,430 --> 01:26:35,960
The fabric, the heels, all those risky moments,

2353
01:26:35,960 --> 01:26:39,770
