2619
01:39:21,790 --> 01:39:24,200
I knew that ending would suit her well.

2620
01:39:24,200 --> 01:39:27,300
To me and NaiN, it looks like the choreo was made by BAILEY.

2621
01:39:27,300 --> 01:39:30,740
I'm watching with myself completely surrendered.

2622
01:39:30,740 --> 01:39:32,740
Firstly, it was much better...

2623
01:39:32,740 --> 01:39:34,510
- than the draft. - Yes.

2624
01:39:34,510 --> 01:39:36,680
It means it suited her dancing style well.

2625
01:39:36,680 --> 01:39:38,910
What I personally found more impactful...

2626
01:39:38,910 --> 01:39:40,280
was Team Kasper and MIN JUN.

2627
01:39:40,280 --> 01:39:43,480
It depends on what BAILEY focuses on.

2628
01:39:43,480 --> 01:39:45,280
One, I want to show...

2629
01:39:45,280 --> 01:39:46,950
what I'm good at.

2630
01:39:46,950 --> 01:39:50,760
Or two, I want to break away from my image as a dancer...

2631
01:39:50,760 --> 01:39:52,090
and show people something new.

2632
01:39:52,090 --> 01:39:54,390
I'm not sure which she'd focus on more.

2633
01:39:54,390 --> 01:39:55,430
(What will BAILEY choose?)

2634
01:39:55,430 --> 01:39:56,700
(K-pop Solo Artist Direct Mission ends.)

2635
01:39:56,700 --> 01:39:58,600
- Good job. - Good job.

2636
01:39:58,600 --> 01:40:00,570
- Good job. - Good job.

2637
01:40:01,100 --> 01:40:02,230
What will I do if I lose?

2638
01:40:02,230 --> 01:40:03,800
I suddenly got so scared.

2639
01:40:03,800 --> 01:40:06,070
Everyone at my company has high expectations.

2640
01:40:06,070 --> 01:40:07,710
I'm shaking as if I'm sick.

2641
01:40:07,710 --> 01:40:09,510
No way I'd lose, right?

2642
01:40:09,510 --> 01:40:11,580
I know a lot about her.

2643
01:40:11,580 --> 01:40:13,280
I know what her strengths are.

2644
01:40:13,280 --> 01:40:15,210
Her biggest strength is her musicality.

2645
01:40:15,210 --> 01:40:16,580
And her expression of texture.

2646
01:40:16,580 --> 01:40:18,150
I showed those well.

2647
01:40:18,150 --> 01:40:20,820
INGYOO and Simeez wanted to try something new.

2648
01:40:20,820 --> 01:40:23,320
BAILEY doesn't do krump,

2649
01:40:23,320 --> 01:40:24,690
but make her do krump barefoot?

2650
01:40:24,690 --> 01:40:26,090
If you're someone with skills,

2651
01:40:26,090 --> 01:40:27,930
isn't high-risk, high-return more fun?

2652
01:40:27,930 --> 01:40:29,800
She wouldn't want to do something she's always done.

2653
01:40:29,800 --> 01:40:32,030
She's an artist now, not a dancer.

2654
01:40:32,030 --> 01:40:35,630
Please, I...

2655
01:40:36,030 --> 01:40:38,500
Please let me win this time.

2656
01:40:38,670 --> 01:40:40,770
TAEYONG told me directly...

2657
01:40:40,770 --> 01:40:41,870
that ours was fun.

2658
01:40:41,870 --> 01:40:45,440
And I heard him saying the other team's was tough.

2659
01:40:45,640 --> 01:40:48,380
As for their directing styles, Team BADA and Koo Young...

2660
01:40:48,380 --> 01:40:50,950
was like a military.

2661
01:40:51,650 --> 01:40:54,550
For Team NaiN and BABYZOO, I enjoyed dancing.

2662
01:40:54,550 --> 01:40:55,720
It's fun.

2663
01:40:55,720 --> 01:40:56,720
It's fun.

2664
01:40:56,720 --> 01:40:59,830
The artist himself said he enjoyed ours.

2665
01:40:59,830 --> 01:41:02,560
Since he's the one deciding at the end of the day,

2666
01:41:02,560 --> 01:41:04,860
I'm hoping for a good result.

2667
01:41:04,860 --> 01:41:08,400
Team BADA and Koo Young had a lot of details...

2668
01:41:08,400 --> 01:41:10,900
and gestures,

2669
01:41:10,900 --> 01:41:12,200
so he didn't enjoy it.

2670
01:41:12,240 --> 01:41:15,370
When I was dancing, I had to keep thinking about the details.

2671
01:41:15,370 --> 01:41:16,610
So it wasn't fun.

2672
01:41:17,210 --> 01:41:19,040
These small things...

2673
01:41:19,040 --> 01:41:20,210
could decide...

2674
01:41:20,210 --> 01:41:22,480
the result of Koo Young and my team.

2675
01:41:22,480 --> 01:41:24,550
It's true that I was quite worried...

2676
01:41:24,550 --> 01:41:26,920
when I heard that.

2677
01:41:26,920 --> 01:41:29,790
But every time BADA points something out,

2678
01:41:29,790 --> 01:41:31,890
the quality of the performance clearly improves.

2679
01:41:31,890 --> 01:41:33,160
Looking at the end result alone,

2680
01:41:33,160 --> 01:41:35,130
ours was much better.

2681
01:41:35,130 --> 01:41:38,000
TAEYONG wouldn't have heard it because he was wearing the in-ear,

2682
01:41:38,000 --> 01:41:40,670
but the fans cheered so loudly.

2683
01:41:40,770 --> 01:41:42,070
(During the filming of Team BADA and Back Koo Young)

2684
01:41:42,070 --> 01:41:44,670
Even for the finger flick, they all cheered.

2685
01:41:44,670 --> 01:41:46,040
(The fans followed the finger flick, the signature dance,)

2686
01:41:46,040 --> 01:41:47,510
(and "Wacka Wak's" signal.)

2687
01:41:47,510 --> 01:41:49,740
For the outro as well, they cheered really loudly.

2688
01:41:50,340 --> 01:41:51,910
TAEYONG's fans...

2689
01:41:51,910 --> 01:41:53,650
were really sharing...

2690
01:41:53,650 --> 01:41:56,010
the energy from his performance.

2691
01:41:56,080 --> 01:41:58,620
I think they felt a thrill.

2692
01:41:58,620 --> 01:42:01,090
When I watched the opposing team's camerawork,

2693
01:42:01,090 --> 01:42:03,720
I found that a lot of it didn't show TAEYONG clearly.

2694
01:42:04,420 --> 01:42:07,430
He was overshadowed by the lyrics on the walls,

2695
01:42:07,460 --> 01:42:09,500
the dancers stood out more,

2696
01:42:10,000 --> 01:42:11,260
or he was too far.

2697
01:42:11,800 --> 01:42:14,270
I want to see them lose their momentum.

2698
01:42:14,270 --> 01:42:15,730
Those with more tenure.

2699
01:42:15,800 --> 01:42:16,870
I'm very sure...

2700
01:42:16,870 --> 01:42:18,440
that I'll win. I'm 100 percent sure.

2701
01:42:18,440 --> 01:42:20,410
If I lose this round,

2702
01:42:20,610 --> 01:42:22,040
I'll leave the show.

2703
01:42:22,540 --> 01:42:25,440
(Goodbye, Kasper.)

2704
01:42:25,440 --> 01:42:28,610
I heard they were confident they'd win.

2705
01:42:28,650 --> 01:42:30,250
But we'll win...

2706
01:42:30,250 --> 01:42:31,550
by a landslide.

2707
01:42:31,550 --> 01:42:33,020
"What suits me..."

2708
01:42:33,020 --> 01:42:34,250
"and this song?"

2709
01:42:34,490 --> 01:42:35,690
I think that's what she'll consider.

2710
01:42:36,790 --> 01:42:38,690
This siren torments me so much.

2711
01:42:38,690 --> 01:42:40,360
I can't get used to it at all.

2712
01:42:40,360 --> 01:42:41,390
(He can't get used to it, but his body reacts fast.)

2713
01:42:41,390 --> 01:42:43,760
I hope I don't come back crying.

2714
01:42:44,630 --> 01:42:46,530
I'm very ambitious about this performance.

2715
01:42:46,530 --> 01:42:48,500
I'm sure we can win.

2716
01:42:48,500 --> 01:42:50,570
It's a given that we'll win this round.

2717
01:42:50,570 --> 01:42:51,870
But I want to have a landslide victory.

2718
01:42:51,870 --> 01:42:53,840
I have no regrets,

2719
01:42:53,840 --> 01:42:54,870
but I must win.

2720
01:42:54,870 --> 01:42:56,740
I think we'll win.

2721
01:42:56,880 --> 01:42:59,680
(The Directors' Square is filled with tension.)

2722
01:42:59,810 --> 01:43:01,480
(At that moment, someone walks up to the stage?)

2723
01:43:01,480 --> 01:43:02,980
(Surprised)

2724
01:43:03,220 --> 01:43:05,420
(The choreographers clap to welcome the person.)

2725
01:43:05,420 --> 01:43:07,320
- Hello. - Hello.

2726
01:43:08,020 --> 01:43:09,320
It's Goliath.

2727
01:43:09,320 --> 01:43:10,420
Hello.

2728
01:43:11,320 --> 01:43:12,690
(David's 90-degree bow)

2729
01:43:13,430 --> 01:43:14,790
Hello, everyone.

2730
01:43:14,790 --> 01:43:17,130
Debuting as a special MC today,

2731
01:43:17,130 --> 01:43:18,700
I'm Lip J. Nice to meet you.

2732
01:43:18,960 --> 01:43:20,270
(Welcoming her fiercely)

2733
01:43:20,270 --> 01:43:21,930
Lip J.

2734
01:43:21,930 --> 01:43:24,200
For this Solo Artist Direct Mission,

2735
01:43:24,270 --> 01:43:26,200
two choreographers became a team...

2736
01:43:26,200 --> 01:43:28,240
to develop...

2737
01:43:28,240 --> 01:43:29,580
and direct...

2738
01:43:29,580 --> 01:43:31,480
a solo artist's performance.

2739
01:43:31,680 --> 01:43:32,780
And today,

2740
01:43:32,780 --> 01:43:34,110
based on the artists' decision,

2741
01:43:34,110 --> 01:43:36,180
two teams' fates...

2742
01:43:36,180 --> 01:43:37,250
will be decided.

2743
01:43:37,250 --> 01:43:38,850
There's no way...

2744
01:43:38,850 --> 01:43:39,850
Simeez and INGYOO will fail.

2745
01:43:39,850 --> 01:43:41,920
I think BAILEY will choose my team.

2746
01:43:41,920 --> 01:43:43,890
The teams chosen by the artists...

2747
01:43:43,890 --> 01:43:45,720
will advance to the next mission.

2748
01:43:45,720 --> 01:43:47,560
The teams which were not chosen...

2749
01:43:47,630 --> 01:43:49,860
will head to Last Stage.

2750
01:43:50,230 --> 01:43:52,600
This is even crueler than the elimination battle.

2751
01:43:54,670 --> 01:43:56,300
I'm not going to Last Stage no matter what.

2752
01:43:56,340 --> 01:43:58,800
Which teams are chosen by the artists?

2753
01:43:58,800 --> 01:44:01,810
Which choreographers will head to Last Stage?

2754
01:44:01,840 --> 01:44:04,140
I'll announce the final results...

2755
01:44:04,240 --> 01:44:06,410
of the Solo Artist Direct Mission.

2756
01:44:08,180 --> 01:44:09,780
Oh, my gosh!

2757
01:44:09,820 --> 01:44:11,780
- You look stunning! - You too. Oh, my gosh.

2758
01:44:11,850 --> 01:44:13,320
It's been way too long.

2759
01:44:13,690 --> 01:44:16,290
(Judge, Sienna Lalau)

2760
01:44:18,220 --> 01:44:19,520
(A world-class choreographer, Sienna Lalau,)

2761
01:44:19,520 --> 01:44:20,830
(who made her name known as the choreographer of "ON" by BTS)

2762
01:44:20,830 --> 01:44:23,900
(Sienna, BAILEY)

2763
01:44:23,900 --> 01:44:26,970
(Two of them have been best friends for a long time.)

2764
01:44:27,070 --> 01:44:28,270
Okay, long story short,

2765
01:44:28,270 --> 01:44:29,270
I have a song,

2766
01:44:29,270 --> 01:44:31,770
and I was working on it for a long time.

2767
01:44:31,770 --> 01:44:34,370
A song that I knew I wanted to push to have performance with.

2768
01:44:34,710 --> 01:44:35,840
It got into two teams.

2769
01:44:35,840 --> 01:44:37,610
- Completely different styles. - Right.

2770
01:44:37,780 --> 01:44:42,150
I thought about what could bring out her strength the most.

2771
01:44:42,150 --> 01:44:43,680
I got a tailored outfit for her.

2772
01:44:44,580 --> 01:44:47,490
A female solo artist wants to stand out.

2773
01:44:47,490 --> 01:44:49,620
I emphasized that.

2774
01:44:50,020 --> 01:44:51,460
I'm going to be completely honest.

2775
01:44:51,460 --> 01:44:52,890
I really have no idea.

2776
01:44:53,130 --> 01:44:54,790
- So I need your help. - Okay.

2777
01:44:54,790 --> 01:44:56,290
I think what I'm excited to see...

2778
01:44:56,290 --> 01:44:58,200
is how both groups of choreographers...

2779
01:44:58,200 --> 01:45:01,300
bring out those different sides of you.

2780
01:45:02,030 --> 01:45:03,470
This isn't easy.

2781
01:45:03,770 --> 01:45:06,140
When I first saw the choreography draft,

2782
01:45:06,140 --> 01:45:08,610
I had a team in mind.

2783
01:45:08,670 --> 01:45:10,510
Actually, I prefer Team NaiN and BABYZOO.

2784
01:45:10,510 --> 01:45:12,410
I thought they were better...

2785
01:45:12,410 --> 01:45:16,280
because it had more aspects for me to show myself.

2786
01:45:16,850 --> 01:45:18,880
(Before, TAEYONG chose Team NaiN and BABYZOO.)

2787
01:45:19,020 --> 01:45:21,650
My mind had changed during the practice,

2788
01:45:21,650 --> 01:45:23,460
and by filming the performances,

2789
01:45:23,460 --> 01:45:25,860
I said I wanted to see how the fans would respond.

2790
01:45:25,890 --> 01:45:28,460
They cheered really loudly for both.

2791
01:45:30,400 --> 01:45:32,200
They liked both.

2792
01:45:32,200 --> 01:45:34,830
So my mind kept changing.

2793
01:45:34,870 --> 01:45:35,970
It's hard to choose.

2794
01:45:35,970 --> 01:45:37,100
(Which performance stole the artists' hearts?)

2795
01:45:37,440 --> 01:45:40,170
First, the matchup for TAEYONG's track.

2796
01:45:40,170 --> 01:45:42,170
Choreographers NaiN and BABYZOO...

2797
01:45:42,170 --> 01:45:44,510
versus Choreographers BADA and Back Koo Young.

2798
01:45:44,510 --> 01:45:45,710
I'll announce the result.

2799
01:45:45,710 --> 01:45:47,450
(Solo Artist Direct Mission: TAEYONG)

2800
01:45:47,450 --> 01:45:48,450
(My gosh)

2801
01:45:48,580 --> 01:45:49,650
(Nervous)

2802
01:45:49,650 --> 01:45:50,820
My heart is pounding.

2803
01:45:51,380 --> 01:45:52,480
(Unconcerned)

2804
01:45:52,550 --> 01:45:54,520
BABYZOO isn't moving at all.

2805
01:45:54,620 --> 01:45:56,820
I think it's a battle...

2806
01:45:56,820 --> 01:45:59,760
about who spoke to the artist more.

2807
01:45:59,760 --> 01:46:02,690
I personally felt very pressured.

2808
01:46:03,030 --> 01:46:04,760
My cube is moving.

2809
01:46:04,760 --> 01:46:05,860
I'm planning it for the Last Stage now.

2810
01:46:06,030 --> 01:46:07,500
If I lose here,

2811
01:46:07,500 --> 01:46:09,330
I'll end up in Last Stage straight away.

2812
01:46:09,330 --> 01:46:11,040
So I was very nervous.

2813
01:46:11,170 --> 01:46:14,240
As for the results of each section win,

2814
01:46:15,070 --> 01:46:18,810
Team BADA and Back Koo Young had more sections chosen.

2815
01:46:18,810 --> 01:46:22,150
However, the team TAEYONG chose for the overall choreography...

2816
01:46:22,310 --> 01:46:24,850
was Team NaiN and BABYZOO.

2817
01:46:25,180 --> 01:46:27,250
Even if we were chosen for the interim decision,

2818
01:46:27,250 --> 01:46:29,150
we were selected less...

2819
01:46:29,150 --> 01:46:31,420
when it came to the sections.

2820
01:46:31,420 --> 01:46:34,890
We tried to pinpoint the feedback...

2821
01:46:34,890 --> 01:46:36,860
he gave for each section.

2822
01:46:36,860 --> 01:46:38,000
"Let's make a stage for TAEYONG..."

2823
01:46:38,000 --> 01:46:41,430
"which is cooler than the first draft."

2824
01:46:41,430 --> 01:46:43,840
That was the goal of our directing.

2825
01:46:44,100 --> 01:46:46,270
Especially, since both teams...

2826
01:46:46,270 --> 01:46:49,340
had choreographers who've worked with TAEYONG before,

2827
01:46:49,340 --> 01:46:51,910
the match was conducted based on deep understanding...

2828
01:46:51,910 --> 01:46:53,510
of TAEYONG.

2829
01:46:53,580 --> 01:46:54,780
I think...

2830
01:46:54,910 --> 01:46:58,620
we interpreted it to match TAEYONG's character better.

2831
01:46:58,780 --> 01:46:59,990
I think we have...

2832
01:46:59,990 --> 01:47:01,550
a big edge over them.

2833
01:47:01,690 --> 01:47:05,420
We considered what TAEYONG could express best,

2834
01:47:05,420 --> 01:47:07,430
and taking a step higher,

2835
01:47:07,430 --> 01:47:09,490
we tried to make a performance...

2836
01:47:09,490 --> 01:47:11,900
where TAEYONG and the audience became one.

2837
01:47:12,260 --> 01:47:14,500
Our performance had...

2838
01:47:14,500 --> 01:47:15,570
way more impact.

2839
01:47:16,100 --> 01:47:17,300
This is the evaluation sheet.

2840
01:47:17,970 --> 01:47:19,140
I'm looking forward to it.

2841
01:47:19,140 --> 01:47:20,170
(The evaluation was done based on the evaluation sheet.)

2842
01:47:20,270 --> 01:47:22,710
As for the dancing itself,

2843
01:47:22,710 --> 01:47:26,510
Team NaiN and BABYZOO had various movements...

2844
01:47:26,510 --> 01:47:29,710
and trendy movements.

2845
01:47:29,820 --> 01:47:31,780
When I dance myself,

2846
01:47:31,780 --> 01:47:33,490
Team NaiN and BABYZOO's is more enjoyable.

2847
01:47:33,490 --> 01:47:34,620
It really has a lot of dance moves.

2848
01:47:34,620 --> 01:47:36,120
It really has a lot of dance moves.

2849
01:47:36,190 --> 01:47:37,790
Team BADA and Back Koo Young...

2850
01:47:37,790 --> 01:47:39,760
put more emphasis on the overall picture, I feel.

2851
01:47:39,760 --> 01:47:42,160
It's easier for the audience...

2852
01:47:42,160 --> 01:47:43,160
to understand.

2853
01:47:43,160 --> 01:47:45,060
Using speakerphones,

2854
01:47:45,060 --> 01:47:46,700
microphones,

2855
01:47:46,700 --> 01:47:49,170
and lightings,

2856
01:47:49,170 --> 01:47:52,270
they made it very clear what they were trying to express.

2857
01:47:52,270 --> 01:47:55,710
It's a lot easier and more direct for the audience.

2858
01:47:55,740 --> 01:47:56,980
It was bright,

2859
01:47:56,980 --> 01:47:58,180
and it felt like...

2860
01:47:58,410 --> 01:48:01,650
the song blended in better.

2861
01:48:01,980 --> 01:48:03,520
The intro was really cool too.

2862
01:48:03,580 --> 01:48:04,920
They were total opposites.

2863
01:48:07,020 --> 01:48:08,420
The impact at the start was amazing.

2864
01:48:08,420 --> 01:48:10,890
- That's right. - Starting with the eyes.

2865
01:48:11,190 --> 01:48:14,190
For Team NaiN and BABYZOO, it was like a resurrection of a king.

2866
01:48:14,360 --> 01:48:15,590
For Team BADA and Back Koo Young,

2867
01:48:15,590 --> 01:48:18,230
it felt more comical.

2868
01:48:18,260 --> 01:48:20,900
So the audience might find it...

2869
01:48:20,900 --> 01:48:23,440
more comfortable and fresher.

2870
01:48:24,300 --> 01:48:26,370
Which outro do you prefer?

2871
01:48:26,440 --> 01:48:28,740
For Team NaiN and BABYZOO,

2872
01:48:28,740 --> 01:48:30,510
we move forward,

2873
01:48:30,740 --> 01:48:32,480
and the ending is very short.

2874
01:48:32,480 --> 01:48:35,510
I dance hard all the way...

2875
01:48:35,650 --> 01:48:37,880
until the very end.

2876
01:48:37,880 --> 01:48:39,220
But for this team,

2877
01:48:39,220 --> 01:48:42,450
it kind of tells the audience that we're going to end it now...

2878
01:48:42,450 --> 01:48:43,920
when I move to the side.

2879
01:48:44,160 --> 01:48:45,560
Is that why...

2880
01:48:45,560 --> 01:48:46,730
it feels...

2881
01:48:46,730 --> 01:48:47,860
- a lot more relaxed overall? - I think...

2882
01:48:47,860 --> 01:48:49,530
As for the dancing of the outro itself,

2883
01:48:49,530 --> 01:48:52,730
Team NaiN and BABYZOO feels fuller and funnier.

2884
01:48:52,730 --> 01:48:55,130
I liked it because it was full.

2885
01:48:55,130 --> 01:48:56,170
(Team NaiN and BABYZOO has the upper hand for the outro.)

2886
01:48:56,170 --> 01:48:57,970
The signature killing point...

2887
01:48:57,970 --> 01:48:59,700
is so hard to pick as well.

2888
01:49:00,340 --> 01:49:04,580
When I was dancing that move,

2889
01:49:04,580 --> 01:49:06,310
it felt like the phrase "Wacka Wak..."

2890
01:49:06,310 --> 01:49:09,920
was expressed perfectly, so I really liked it.

2891
01:49:10,020 --> 01:49:11,120
But...

2892
01:49:11,120 --> 01:49:14,390
I don't know if it's because Koo Young said it repeatedly,

2893
01:49:14,390 --> 01:49:17,120
but the finger flick keeps invading my mind.

2894
01:49:17,220 --> 01:49:19,560
When I think about the chorus,

2895
01:49:20,060 --> 01:49:21,430
all I can think about is the finger flick.

2896
01:49:21,430 --> 01:49:22,560
This is crazy.

2897
01:49:22,560 --> 01:49:23,660
It's hard to decide.

2898
01:49:24,430 --> 01:49:25,800
When I had the choreography lessons,

2899
01:49:25,800 --> 01:49:27,430
for Team NaiN and BABYZOO...

2900
01:49:27,430 --> 01:49:30,370
Is there a specific direction you'd like us to revise?

2901
01:49:30,700 --> 01:49:32,900
They kept sharing their opinions,

2902
01:49:32,900 --> 01:49:34,070
and I told them my own as well.

2903
01:49:34,070 --> 01:49:36,210
And they were reflected immediately.

2904
01:49:36,410 --> 01:49:39,310
In terms of feedback reflection and performance improvement,

2905
01:49:39,310 --> 01:49:42,010
Team NaiN and BABYZOO definitely was better.

2906
01:49:42,080 --> 01:49:44,250
Team BADA and Back Koo Young...

2907
01:49:44,250 --> 01:49:45,780
knows me very well,

2908
01:49:45,780 --> 01:49:47,820
so it was easier to learn,

2909
01:49:47,820 --> 01:49:50,190
and I had more time...

2910
01:49:50,190 --> 01:49:52,190
to add my own vibe to it.

2911
01:49:52,190 --> 01:49:54,530
In terms of choreography teaching and communication skills,

2912
01:49:54,530 --> 01:49:57,300
I'll choose Team BADA and Back Koo Young.

2913
01:49:57,860 --> 01:49:59,930
But honestly, until yesterday,

2914
01:49:59,930 --> 01:50:01,930
I was going to choose this team.

2915
01:50:01,930 --> 01:50:05,270
At the end of the performance,

2916
01:50:05,270 --> 01:50:06,340
I changed my mind.

2917
01:50:07,710 --> 01:50:09,110
I'm nervous,

2918
01:50:09,110 --> 01:50:10,940
but at the same time, I'm confident.

2919
01:50:10,940 --> 01:50:13,480
I'm having a lot of mixed feelings.

2920
01:50:13,910 --> 01:50:16,980
Based on the end result alone, we have a better chance of winning.

2921
01:50:17,380 --> 01:50:20,250
As someone who's seen TAEYONG for a long time,

2922
01:50:20,250 --> 01:50:23,250
I could tell from his performance...

2923
01:50:23,250 --> 01:50:24,860
that he preferred...

2924
01:50:24,860 --> 01:50:25,960
Team NaiN and BABYZOO's choreography.

2925
01:50:25,960 --> 01:50:27,330
I could feel it clearly.

2926
01:50:27,460 --> 01:50:28,760
I think TAEYONG would choose...

2927
01:50:28,760 --> 01:50:30,800
Team BADA and Back Koo Young.

2928
01:50:30,900 --> 01:50:32,800
The artist stood out more.

2929
01:50:32,900 --> 01:50:35,100
Let's check the result now.

2930
01:50:35,900 --> 01:50:39,470
Thank you to both teams for making an incredible performance.

2931
01:50:39,670 --> 01:50:43,240
I got to dance with those who love dancing.

2932
01:50:43,240 --> 01:50:44,710
I had so much fun,

2933
01:50:44,710 --> 01:50:47,650
and it got me to love dancing once again.

2934
01:50:48,010 --> 01:50:50,420
Even with the same song and the same artist,

2935
01:50:50,480 --> 01:50:53,920
you interpreted it differently, which was very impressive.

2936
01:50:54,520 --> 01:50:57,620
I couldn't make up my mind...

2937
01:50:57,620 --> 01:50:59,220
until the very last moment of the performance.

2938
01:50:59,560 --> 01:51:02,290
(Nervous)

2939
01:51:02,590 --> 01:51:05,130
Both teams have come up with high quality works.

2940
01:51:05,260 --> 01:51:06,930
My decision was based on the focus of...

2941
01:51:06,930 --> 01:51:10,500
choosing a performance that would make me stand out...

2942
01:51:10,500 --> 01:51:12,670
when I got up on the stage myself.

2943
01:51:13,510 --> 01:51:15,510
The dancers' outfits have been toned down.

2944
01:51:15,510 --> 01:51:16,780
They're wearing masks as well.

2945
01:51:16,780 --> 01:51:20,410
I designed it so that the artist would stand out more.

2946
01:51:20,480 --> 01:51:22,480
We must win. Please!

2947
01:51:22,750 --> 01:51:24,180
Our concept...

2948
01:51:24,180 --> 01:51:28,020
was for TAEYONG to make a strong impact as an artist.

2949
01:51:28,020 --> 01:51:30,520
The focus was on TAEYONG.

2950
01:51:30,790 --> 01:51:32,420
We definitely have the advantage.

2951
01:51:33,760 --> 01:51:35,330
The Solo Artist Direct Mission.

2952
01:51:35,890 --> 01:51:39,130
The directors I will work with...

2953
01:51:41,630 --> 01:51:43,800
are choreographers BADA and Back Koo Young.

2954
01:51:43,800 --> 01:51:45,600
(Artist TAEYONG's choice: BADA and Back Koo Young)

2955
01:51:46,070 --> 01:51:47,370
(BADA and Back Koo Young)

2956
01:51:47,710 --> 01:51:49,010
(Letting out a sigh)

2957
01:51:49,010 --> 01:51:50,040
We did well.

2958
01:51:50,510 --> 01:51:52,080
It felt great.

2959
01:51:52,280 --> 01:51:54,050
I got goosebumps all over.

2960
01:51:54,250 --> 01:51:56,680
I felt a sense of relief.

2961
01:51:59,280 --> 01:52:01,150
Great work, BADA.

2962
01:52:04,090 --> 01:52:05,260
No way.

2963
01:52:05,620 --> 01:52:06,860
It was a big shock.

2964
01:52:06,860 --> 01:52:08,590
It was the biggest shock I went through recently.

2965
01:52:10,430 --> 01:52:12,360
This isn't TAEYONG's mood.

2966
01:52:12,830 --> 01:52:14,700
"Ours will get chosen."

2967
01:52:14,700 --> 01:52:16,170
I was certain about it.

2968
01:52:16,430 --> 01:52:17,740
It was hard to understand.

2969
01:52:18,040 --> 01:52:19,440
To be honest,

2970
01:52:19,740 --> 01:52:21,070
I would've made...

2971
01:52:21,070 --> 01:52:23,140
a different decision yesterday.

2972
01:52:23,140 --> 01:52:26,980
I love NaiN and BABYZOO's choreography.

2973
01:52:27,080 --> 01:52:30,650
I was certain to the point that...

2974
01:52:30,650 --> 01:52:31,820
I had already made up my mind.

2975
01:52:31,880 --> 01:52:33,720
As directors, I believe BADA and Back Koo Young...

2976
01:52:33,720 --> 01:52:36,120
created this energy within the stage...

2977
01:52:36,520 --> 01:52:39,160
and they were able to fill the stage...

2978
01:52:39,160 --> 01:52:40,730
with something unique.

2979
01:52:41,060 --> 01:52:43,730
That made the performance feel more complete.

2980
01:52:43,730 --> 01:52:47,530
It became a performance I was able to enjoy with the fans.

2981
01:52:47,770 --> 01:52:49,130
As I mentioned at the start,

2982
01:52:49,130 --> 01:52:52,100
the goal of this song was to feel energized...

2983
01:52:52,100 --> 01:52:55,770
while dreaming of being in the top tier.

2984
01:52:56,170 --> 01:52:58,780
The performance that suited that goal...

2985
01:52:58,980 --> 01:53:01,810
was made by BADA and Back Koo Young.

2986
01:53:02,750 --> 01:53:05,980
The energy we received from "Wacka Wak..."

2987
01:53:05,980 --> 01:53:07,320
was created into a performance.

2988
01:53:07,320 --> 01:53:11,190
This energy was delivered to TAEYONG.

2989
01:53:12,190 --> 01:53:16,090
He emphasized the bright energy and connection with the fans.

2990
01:53:16,090 --> 01:53:19,200
We might've gone in the wrong direction.

2991
01:53:19,560 --> 01:53:22,130
The moments that we loved...

2992
01:53:22,130 --> 01:53:23,970
ended up failing.

2993
01:53:23,970 --> 01:53:25,470
That broke my heart.

2994
01:53:26,240 --> 01:53:29,570
As a result, choreographers NaiN and BABYZOO...

2995
01:53:29,640 --> 01:53:31,780
will head to the Last Stage.

2996
01:53:32,380 --> 01:53:34,780
(NaiN and BABYZOO confirmed for Last Stage: 24H.)

2997
01:53:35,250 --> 01:53:36,250
(Forced laughter)

2998
01:53:36,250 --> 01:53:37,280
That's harsh.

2999
01:53:37,880 --> 01:53:38,950
This is crazy.

3000
01:53:40,220 --> 01:53:42,320
There's nothing easy in life.

3001
01:53:43,250 --> 01:53:45,060
Great work. We did a great job.

3002
01:53:45,320 --> 01:53:46,320
We did a great job.

3003
01:53:47,890 --> 01:53:49,490
I hoped that this wouldn't happen.

3004
01:53:49,690 --> 01:53:50,960
It's heartbreaking.

3005
01:53:51,830 --> 01:53:53,260
I was on the same team as NaiN.

3006
01:53:53,260 --> 01:53:56,570
We had to compete against each other on the Last Stage.

3007
01:53:56,570 --> 01:53:57,970
That broke my heart even more.

3008
01:53:58,340 --> 01:53:59,500
I went through a reality check.

3009
01:53:59,500 --> 01:54:01,310
I tried to control my mind,

3010
01:54:01,310 --> 01:54:02,870
but it wasn't easy.

3011
01:54:02,870 --> 01:54:04,740
I went through many different emotions.

3012
01:54:06,610 --> 01:54:08,850
Next is the matchup for artist BAILEY.

3013
01:54:09,950 --> 01:54:10,980
The result will be announced for the matchup between...

3014
01:54:10,980 --> 01:54:12,020
choreographers JEONG MIN JUN and Kasper...

3015
01:54:12,020 --> 01:54:15,520
against choreographers Simeez and INGYOO.

3016
01:54:16,120 --> 01:54:17,520
I really want to avoid going to the Last Stage...

3017
01:54:17,520 --> 01:54:19,460
and I want to achieve a perfect victory.

3018
01:54:19,820 --> 01:54:21,230
It's a battle based on being chosen.

3019
01:54:21,530 --> 01:54:24,760
The new challenge of the solo artist and the needs of that artist.

3020
01:54:24,960 --> 01:54:27,300
It will be based on how well we did with those things.

3021
01:54:27,670 --> 01:54:29,030
I had a sense of certainty.

3022
01:54:29,470 --> 01:54:31,570
BAILEY liked our choreography.

3023
01:54:31,740 --> 01:54:33,640
The one performing on stage...

3024
01:54:33,640 --> 01:54:35,610
will know whether she stands out or not.

3025
01:54:35,810 --> 01:54:37,480
Wouldn't she base her decision on those things?

3026
01:54:38,110 --> 01:54:40,310
And I genuinely do want to see what they could come up with.

3027
01:54:40,310 --> 01:54:41,450
I think what I'm excited about...

3028
01:54:41,450 --> 01:54:43,680
You are not only a dancer but also a performer.

3029
01:54:43,680 --> 01:54:47,920
So it's based on how both groups of choreographers bring out...

3030
01:54:48,250 --> 01:54:49,690
those different sides of you.

3031
01:54:49,690 --> 01:54:51,860
Honestly, if anybody mixed the two...

3032
01:54:53,060 --> 01:54:54,690
Chef's kiss. I can't even wait.

3033
01:54:55,330 --> 01:54:56,530
(Full of expectation)

3034
01:54:56,790 --> 01:54:59,360
In the result of each section win announced earlier...

3035
01:54:59,830 --> 01:55:01,870
Only the verse and pre-chorus were chosen...

3036
01:55:01,870 --> 01:55:03,270
and that was something to worry about.

3037
01:55:03,770 --> 01:55:05,040
(Simeez and INGYOO were chosen by the artist.)

3038
01:55:05,240 --> 01:55:06,840
"Nice! It worked." This was what it felt like.

3039
01:55:06,840 --> 01:55:07,840
Okay!

3040
01:55:08,170 --> 01:55:09,670
What was a relief...

3041
01:55:09,740 --> 01:55:12,610
was that the scenes we considered most important in our concept...

3042
01:55:12,610 --> 01:55:15,510
were the intro, chorus, and outro.

3043
01:55:15,510 --> 01:55:19,520
We believe that the frame and concept worked for her.

3044
01:55:19,650 --> 01:55:22,850
We thought about what we could add with open hearts...

3045
01:55:22,850 --> 01:55:25,420
based on her needs.

3046
01:55:25,560 --> 01:55:27,790
We focused on developing what we had.

3047
01:55:27,930 --> 01:55:28,990
I'm confident.

3048
01:55:28,990 --> 01:55:32,800
It's up to BAILEY to decide which weapon is better for her.

3049
01:55:32,800 --> 01:55:34,830
Directing is about...

3050
01:55:34,830 --> 01:55:36,400
seeing the bigger picture from the back...

3051
01:55:36,400 --> 01:55:39,840
and making the artist shine.

3052
01:55:39,970 --> 01:55:41,710
When it comes to those things,

3053
01:55:41,710 --> 01:55:44,040
I'm certain that nobody can do better than I do.

3054
01:55:44,380 --> 01:55:45,910
- What is he saying? - I'm not sure about that.

3055
01:55:46,310 --> 01:55:49,110
I felt even more certain after seeing today's performance.

3056
01:55:50,210 --> 01:55:52,250
- Completely different styles. - Right.

3057
01:55:52,250 --> 01:55:53,950
It's like black and white.

3058
01:55:54,320 --> 01:55:56,990
I definitely think INGYOO and Simeez...

3059
01:55:56,990 --> 01:55:59,520
did it in the eye of an artist.

3060
01:55:59,660 --> 01:56:01,130
The gestures that she's doing...

3061
01:56:01,130 --> 01:56:03,900
or the way she gives a performance of the facial.

3062
01:56:03,900 --> 01:56:07,430
She's able to freely express herself in that way.

3063
01:56:07,430 --> 01:56:09,630
But I could also see the difference.

3064
01:56:09,770 --> 01:56:13,300
Kasper and MIN JUN are so technical.

3065
01:56:13,300 --> 01:56:15,740
They really studied you down to a T.

3066
01:56:15,740 --> 01:56:19,980
They were able to really find all of those mannerisms,

3067
01:56:19,980 --> 01:56:22,110
and choreograph it to your style.

3068
01:56:22,310 --> 01:56:24,420
That's the thing. I think, for both teams...

3069
01:56:24,420 --> 01:56:26,720
- Almost everything is in the high. - Yes.

3070
01:56:26,720 --> 01:56:28,750
But in such different ways.

3071
01:56:28,990 --> 01:56:32,120
That intro. Kasper and MIN JUN.

3072
01:56:32,220 --> 01:56:33,220
My gosh.

3073
01:56:33,220 --> 01:56:34,960
Already starting off with a bang!

3074
01:56:34,960 --> 01:56:37,560
I was sold already. I was sold from the very beginning.

3075
01:56:37,560 --> 01:56:39,500
Because nobody starts like that...

3076
01:56:39,500 --> 01:56:40,700
except Bailey Sok.

3077
01:56:40,700 --> 01:56:42,930
What I love is that we can't expect it.

3078
01:56:43,230 --> 01:56:45,300
For INGYOO and Simeez,

3079
01:56:45,300 --> 01:56:48,240
I definitely liked the idea that they used with the fabric...

3080
01:56:48,240 --> 01:56:49,270
in the beginning.

3081
01:56:49,410 --> 01:56:53,680
I could see the concept playing out in between the song.

3082
01:56:53,750 --> 01:56:55,310
What do I remember from these videos?

3083
01:56:55,310 --> 01:56:56,310
I remember red.

3084
01:56:56,310 --> 01:56:57,820
Choreography and killing point.

3085
01:56:57,820 --> 01:57:01,190
I definitely feel like Kasper and MIN JUN...

3086
01:57:01,390 --> 01:57:03,960
did a really good job at knowing who BAILEY is.

3087
01:57:03,960 --> 01:57:05,790
The bullet.

3088
01:57:05,990 --> 01:57:08,790
The "can't kill me" catch into the groove after.

3089
01:57:09,430 --> 01:57:13,700
I feel like they really got your intricacies really well.

3090
01:57:13,700 --> 01:57:15,370
You are the queen of isolation...

3091
01:57:15,370 --> 01:57:18,500
and you have so much detail to your movement.

3092
01:57:18,500 --> 01:57:20,470
And it's always very intentional.

3093
01:57:20,470 --> 01:57:22,470
It felt like they did a really good job...

3094
01:57:22,470 --> 01:57:25,440
at bringing that side out of you even more.

3095
01:57:25,580 --> 01:57:27,850
INGYOO and Simeez's style is...

3096
01:57:27,850 --> 01:57:30,950
BAILEY getting into that lift and then jumping on...

3097
01:57:30,950 --> 01:57:32,850
whoever that dancer was.

3098
01:57:32,850 --> 01:57:35,020
Yes! Put him to the ground!

3099
01:57:35,020 --> 01:57:36,020
(Laughing)

3100
01:57:36,020 --> 01:57:37,160
- Yes! - Yes!

3101
01:57:38,090 --> 01:57:40,560
You crazy girl! Gosh!

3102
01:57:40,560 --> 01:57:44,130
Honestly, lighting is such an important part of a performance.

3103
01:57:44,130 --> 01:57:47,530
Kasper. The way you were highlighted with different spotlights...

3104
01:57:47,530 --> 01:57:50,400
made the biggest difference in the tone in a move like this.

3105
01:57:50,400 --> 01:57:52,940
I think they both have really great strengths...

3106
01:57:52,940 --> 01:57:54,770
and really hard challenges at the same time.

3107
01:57:54,770 --> 01:57:57,040
- It's tough. - Gosh, it's so interesting.

3108
01:57:57,040 --> 01:57:59,680
(BAILEY struggles to make decision.)

3109
01:57:59,680 --> 01:58:01,780
With different interpretations and directing,

3110
01:58:01,950 --> 01:58:04,450
these two teams completed BAILEY's performance.

3111
01:58:05,380 --> 01:58:10,320
Which team's directing did BAILEY choose?

3112
01:58:10,320 --> 01:58:11,490
(What choice will artist BAILEY make?)

3113
01:58:12,020 --> 01:58:16,230
I put together a tailor-made suit...

3114
01:58:16,230 --> 01:58:17,630
and sent it to BAILEY.

3115
01:58:17,760 --> 01:58:20,100
I was confident about the performance I made for her.

3116
01:58:20,100 --> 01:58:22,000
I was certain that she was going to choose mine.

3117
01:58:22,170 --> 01:58:23,600
I really want to win this time.

3118
01:58:23,600 --> 01:58:25,370
I can't go to the Last Stage now.

3119
01:58:25,370 --> 01:58:26,740
You guys should go.

3120
01:58:27,100 --> 01:58:29,910
When I monitored it on site,

3121
01:58:29,910 --> 01:58:33,880
Kasper and MIN JUN's performance had a greater impact.

3122
01:58:33,880 --> 01:58:36,010
I've worked with BAILEY before.

3123
01:58:36,010 --> 01:58:38,380
She's an artist who creates a synergy...

3124
01:58:38,720 --> 01:58:41,020
when things are stable on stage.

3125
01:58:41,190 --> 01:58:43,750
I think she will choose Kasper and MIN JUN based on that.

3126
01:58:43,750 --> 01:58:44,820
It's a tough one.

3127
01:58:44,820 --> 01:58:46,920
Can INGYOO and Simeez not be chosen?

3128
01:58:47,390 --> 01:58:48,630
We went for the right vibes.

3129
01:58:49,190 --> 01:58:51,830
I believe we put together a great performance.

3130
01:58:51,900 --> 01:58:53,870
It's a performance that reveals...

3131
01:58:53,870 --> 01:58:56,430
the birth of the Hydra Queen.

3132
01:58:57,130 --> 01:59:00,370
Won't INGYOO and Simeez have the advantage?

3133
01:59:00,640 --> 01:59:02,840
It can bring out a new charm...

3134
01:59:02,840 --> 01:59:05,310
that BAILEY has never revealed.

3135
01:59:05,310 --> 01:59:07,750
That new challenge was very impressive.

3136
01:59:08,310 --> 01:59:09,310
The result will be revealed now...

3137
01:59:09,610 --> 01:59:11,580
through the screen.

3138
01:59:12,650 --> 01:59:15,520
Truly. I mean this honestly from the bottom of my heart.

3139
01:59:15,890 --> 01:59:18,820
Both teams really created such high-level,

3140
01:59:18,820 --> 01:59:20,860
such incredible performances.

3141
01:59:20,860 --> 01:59:22,830
One team really brought out my strengths...

3142
01:59:22,830 --> 01:59:25,330
and my identity as a choreographer...

3143
01:59:25,330 --> 01:59:27,330
and as a dancer. My whole background of it.

3144
01:59:27,330 --> 01:59:31,700
Another team showed me a whole other side of myself...

3145
01:59:31,700 --> 01:59:34,040
that I didn't know really existed.

3146
01:59:34,340 --> 01:59:36,210
Thank you for making it so difficult for me.

3147
01:59:36,210 --> 01:59:39,040
So for the Solo Artist Direct Mission,

3148
01:59:39,140 --> 01:59:41,250
the final directors of the performance...

3149
01:59:41,250 --> 01:59:43,950
I'll be using for my official promotional activities are...

3150
01:59:44,320 --> 01:59:46,220
Please go to the Last Stage, INGYOO and Simeez.

3151
01:59:46,220 --> 01:59:47,550
We're bound to win.

3152
01:59:47,920 --> 01:59:50,660
I'll surely win. I just want to overwhelm them.

3153
01:59:50,660 --> 01:59:53,460
I'm sorry, but please go to the Last Stage, MIN JUN and Kasper.

3154
01:59:54,460 --> 01:59:57,060
(To be continued)

3155
01:59:57,060 --> 01:59:58,860
(Which team will be BAILEY's final choice?)

3156
01:59:59,130 --> 02:00:02,070
So for the Solo Artist Direct Mission,

3157
02:00:02,170 --> 02:00:04,000
the final directors of the performance...

3158
02:00:04,000 --> 02:00:07,100
I'll be using for my official promotional activities are...

3159
02:00:07,100 --> 02:00:09,040
Please go to the Last Stage, INGYOO and Simeez.

3160
02:00:09,040 --> 02:00:10,640
We're bound to win.

3161
02:00:10,880 --> 02:00:12,180
I'll surely win.

3162
02:00:12,180 --> 02:00:13,540
I just want to overwhelm them.

3163
02:00:13,540 --> 02:00:15,080
I'm sorry, but please...

3164
02:00:15,080 --> 02:00:16,150
go to the Last Stage, MIN JUN and Kasper.

3165
02:00:16,150 --> 02:00:19,650
(K-pop Solo Artist Direct Mission)

3166
02:00:19,950 --> 02:00:22,020
(Which team will be BAILEY's final choice?)

3167
02:00:22,250 --> 02:00:25,190
Choreographers INGYOO and Simeez.

3168
02:00:26,060 --> 02:00:29,930
(Team Simeez and INGYOO is the final winner.)

3169
02:00:30,260 --> 02:00:31,830
(Joy)

3170
02:00:31,830 --> 02:00:33,330
(Sorrow)

3171
02:00:33,970 --> 02:00:35,670
We won. We overcame.

3172
02:00:35,670 --> 02:00:37,230
(Applause of joy)

3173
02:00:37,230 --> 02:00:39,370
The sensation is incredibly pleasurable.

3174
02:00:39,740 --> 02:00:41,810
I kept refining it continuously, without missing...

3175
02:00:42,210 --> 02:00:43,910
a single day or even a few hours.

3176
02:00:43,910 --> 02:00:46,240
Right up until filming began.

3177
02:00:46,240 --> 02:00:47,650
I was deeply moved.

3178
02:00:47,880 --> 02:00:49,710
(BAILEY's choice, Simeez and INGYOO)

3179
02:00:49,850 --> 02:00:51,420
Congratulations.

3180
02:00:52,520 --> 02:00:53,520
(Glancing)

3181
02:00:55,690 --> 02:00:58,260
Am I dreaming? What's going on?

3182
02:00:58,260 --> 02:01:00,060
Why?

3183
02:01:00,190 --> 02:01:03,960
I hadn't even considered going to the last stage twice.

3184
02:01:03,960 --> 02:01:06,400
Why did BAILEY make that choice?

3185
02:01:06,400 --> 02:01:08,770
I was taken aback.

3186
02:01:09,200 --> 02:01:11,440
I think Kasper and MIN JUN's maybe brought out...

3187
02:01:11,440 --> 02:01:12,800
my strengths.

3188
02:01:13,000 --> 02:01:14,340
It was so me.

3189
02:01:14,340 --> 02:01:18,140
But INGYOO and Simeez had a different push in terms of...

3190
02:01:18,140 --> 02:01:19,910
"Who are you as an artist?"

3191
02:01:19,910 --> 02:01:21,910
Or "What kind of character do you want to bring?"

3192
02:01:21,910 --> 02:01:24,020
They opened like a whole another world in a different way.

3193
02:01:24,020 --> 02:01:26,720
So, in terms of putting a performance out there,

3194
02:01:26,720 --> 02:01:28,050
what's going to be entertaining...

3195
02:01:28,050 --> 02:01:30,550
in a lot of different ways might be an unexpected one.

3196
02:01:30,550 --> 02:01:31,620
And something that I want to...

3197
02:01:31,620 --> 02:01:33,660
push myself and challenge myself towards...

3198
02:01:33,660 --> 02:01:35,560
is a little bit of a new style.

3199
02:01:35,830 --> 02:01:37,700
My judgment was wrong.

3200
02:01:37,700 --> 02:01:40,400
I thought I knew BAILEY the best, but I didn't.

3201
02:01:40,400 --> 02:01:42,100
That was the biggest shock.

3202
02:01:42,300 --> 02:01:45,340
So, choreographers Kasper and JEONG MIN JUN...

3203
02:01:45,340 --> 02:01:47,540
will go to the Last Stage.

3204
02:01:48,070 --> 02:01:50,640
Please prepare for the Last Stage.

3205
02:01:51,010 --> 02:01:52,010
(Laughing)

3206
02:01:52,010 --> 02:01:54,850
(Disheartened)

3207
02:01:54,850 --> 02:01:56,680
(Glancing)

3208
02:01:58,950 --> 02:02:02,420
(Only silence reigns in the Directors' Lab.)

3209
02:02:02,990 --> 02:02:04,190
I'm furious.

3210
02:02:04,190 --> 02:02:05,960
This doesn't make sense.

3211
02:02:06,220 --> 02:02:07,760
It bothers me that...

3212
02:02:07,760 --> 02:02:11,330
MIN JUN is going to the Last Stage again this time.

3213
02:02:11,330 --> 02:02:13,800
That wasn't in my plans at all.

3214
02:02:13,800 --> 02:02:14,900
It was the same for me.

3215
02:02:14,900 --> 02:02:16,670
It was too harsh.

3216
02:02:16,670 --> 02:02:19,800
Hash and Renan, the first team from the Director's Cut,

3217
02:02:19,800 --> 02:02:21,740
also went to the Last Stage.

3218
02:02:21,740 --> 02:02:23,210
MIN JUN and I teamed up,

3219
02:02:23,210 --> 02:02:24,580
and we ended up going to the Last Stage.

3220
02:02:24,580 --> 02:02:27,310
The odds are against it, but I'm going again.

3221
02:02:27,310 --> 02:02:29,350
This feels like...

3222
02:02:29,350 --> 02:02:31,280
a major jinx to me.

3223
02:02:31,780 --> 02:02:34,820
The thought of having to prepare all over again is heartbreaking.

3224
02:02:34,820 --> 02:02:36,990
It feels like my heart is shattering.

3225
02:02:37,620 --> 02:02:40,930
The thought that I have to draw it out one more time...

3226
02:02:41,260 --> 02:02:42,760
It's really...

3227
02:02:43,230 --> 02:02:45,130
I'm not sure how to put it.

3228
02:02:45,130 --> 02:02:47,600
I have such mixed emotions.

3229
02:02:49,030 --> 02:02:50,030
At first, I told myself...

3230
02:02:50,030 --> 02:02:52,800
I should at least approach it with a bold mindset.

3231
02:02:52,970 --> 02:02:56,670
(He accepted the first "Last Stage" with composure.)

3232
02:02:56,810 --> 02:02:58,840
By the second time around, the thought of having...

3233
02:02:58,840 --> 02:03:00,750
a bold heart doesn't even cross my mind.

3234
02:03:00,750 --> 02:03:02,910
I've lost my mind.

3235
02:03:03,080 --> 02:03:04,120
(Laughing)

3236
02:03:04,120 --> 02:03:05,450
What should I do?

3237
02:03:05,450 --> 02:03:07,150
I'll survive, no matter what it takes.

3238
02:03:07,150 --> 02:03:08,820
I'll finish them off.

3239
02:03:09,390 --> 02:03:11,520
Choreographers JEONG MIN JUN, Kasper,

3240
02:03:11,520 --> 02:03:13,420
NaiN, and BABYZOO...

3241
02:03:13,420 --> 02:03:16,660
will go to the Last Stage 24H.

3242
02:03:16,860 --> 02:03:18,860
(Last Stage: 24H, the final survival showdown to determine...)

3243
02:03:18,860 --> 02:03:20,930
(which choreographer gets eliminated can be viewed on TVING.)

3244
02:03:21,970 --> 02:03:25,070
(SDF Stage Audience Event)

3245
02:03:25,070 --> 02:03:28,470
(Witness the Street World Fighter: Directors' War set...)

3246
02:03:28,470 --> 02:03:31,680
(and see the directors take the stage with your own eyes!)

3247
02:03:33,010 --> 02:03:34,180
(It's a nightmare.)

3248
02:03:34,180 --> 02:03:35,880
(It doesn't make sense.)

3249
02:03:36,250 --> 02:03:37,780
(Is this right?)

3250
02:03:37,780 --> 02:03:39,220
(What do they want?)

3251
02:03:39,550 --> 02:03:41,490
(It's infuriating to have to go...)

3252
02:03:41,490 --> 02:03:42,490
(to the Last Stage twice.)

3253
02:03:42,490 --> 02:03:44,220
(I felt sorry for MIN JUN.)

3254
02:03:44,220 --> 02:03:46,020
(It weighed on my mind...)

3255
02:03:46,260 --> 02:03:47,530
(because it felt like it was my fault.)

3256
02:03:47,730 --> 02:03:48,730
(You did well.)

3257
02:03:48,730 --> 02:03:50,190
(Patting)

3258
02:03:50,530 --> 02:03:51,530
(I'm sorry.)

3259
02:03:51,530 --> 02:03:52,530
(No.)

3260
02:03:52,530 --> 02:03:53,760
(Sighing)

3261
02:03:54,570 --> 02:03:57,130
(I really hope Kasper and I survive.)

3262
02:03:57,130 --> 02:03:58,170
(Last Stage?)

3263
02:03:58,170 --> 02:03:59,840
(It's messing with your head, isn't it?)

3264
02:03:59,840 --> 02:04:01,440
(I can't get my head straight.)

3265
02:04:03,370 --> 02:04:05,910
(Last Stage came as a huge shock.)

3266
02:04:06,680 --> 02:04:08,450
(Sighing)

3267
02:04:08,850 --> 02:04:11,680
(NaiN eventually sheds tears over the unexpected result.)

3268
02:04:11,680 --> 02:04:12,780
(I felt a little sorrier...)

3269
02:04:12,780 --> 02:04:14,490
(toward NaiN.)

3270
02:04:14,490 --> 02:04:16,020
(If I had done a little better,)

3271
02:04:16,020 --> 02:04:18,460
(this wouldn't have happened.)

3272
02:04:19,160 --> 02:04:21,190
(NaiN, you did so well.)

3273
02:04:21,190 --> 02:04:23,260
(You too.)

3274
02:04:23,830 --> 02:04:26,260
(They offer each other comfort after all the hard work.)

3275
02:04:26,260 --> 02:04:27,530
(We have no time...)

3276
02:04:27,530 --> 02:04:31,100
(to be swayed by emotions right now.)

3277
02:04:31,100 --> 02:04:32,740
(Let's just do it.)

3278
02:04:32,740 --> 02:04:34,740
(Let's wrap up the Last Stage and then unwind.)

3279
02:04:34,740 --> 02:04:36,240
(Positive thinking)

3280
02:04:36,240 --> 02:04:37,680
(We can...)

3281
02:04:37,680 --> 02:04:39,410
(show them another performance.)

3282
02:04:39,410 --> 02:04:41,610
(Isn't this a bit of a forced stroke of luck?)

3283
02:04:42,350 --> 02:04:43,350
(We will advance.)

3284
02:04:43,350 --> 02:04:44,880
(Yes! For sure!)

3285
02:04:45,420 --> 02:04:46,520
(Let's grit our teeth even harder...)

3286
02:04:46,520 --> 02:04:49,320
(and pour everything we have into this.)

3287
02:04:49,320 --> 02:04:50,650
(If you are ready to die, you will live.)

3288
02:04:50,650 --> 02:04:52,220
(If you cling to life, you will die.)

3289
02:04:52,220 --> 02:04:54,230
(I'm ready to die.)

3290
02:04:54,230 --> 02:04:56,260
(You are given...)

3291
02:04:56,260 --> 02:04:57,260
(20 cubes.)

3292
02:04:57,260 --> 02:04:58,260
(20 cubes?)

3293
02:04:58,260 --> 02:04:59,260
(I just used objects.)

3294
02:04:59,260 --> 02:05:00,560
(They're telling me to use them again.)

3295
02:05:00,700 --> 02:05:01,700
(I feel at a loss.)

3296
02:05:01,700 --> 02:05:04,000
(What were the production team thinking when they prepared this?)

3297
02:05:04,400 --> 02:05:05,400
(This is crazy.)

3298
02:05:05,400 --> 02:05:06,700
(What should I do?)

3299
02:05:06,700 --> 02:05:07,710
(It's making me go crazy.)

3300
02:05:07,710 --> 02:05:09,040
(I can't come up with the choreography.)

3301
02:05:09,040 --> 02:05:10,170
(I can't think of anything.)

3302
02:05:10,170 --> 02:05:11,180
(Gosh)

3303
02:05:11,180 --> 02:05:12,780
(I'll just go home.)

3304
02:05:12,780 --> 02:05:14,380
(There's nothing I can do with this!)

3305
02:05:14,380 --> 02:05:16,150
(The cube is the simplest geometric shape.)

3306
02:05:16,150 --> 02:05:17,580
(Stacked, it becomes a structure,)

3307
02:05:17,580 --> 02:05:19,080
(joined, a wall,)

3308
02:05:19,080 --> 02:05:21,250
(arranged, a space,)

3309
02:05:21,420 --> 02:05:22,650
(and when it meets dance,)

3310
02:05:22,650 --> 02:05:24,020
(it becomes a work of art.)

3311
02:05:24,020 --> 02:05:25,360
(In terms of utilizing the objects,)

3312
02:05:25,360 --> 02:05:27,260
(I have the greatest advantage since I have experience.)

3313
02:05:27,260 --> 02:05:28,860
(Everyone except me...)

3314
02:05:29,330 --> 02:05:30,460
(will be at a disadvantage.)

3315
02:05:30,460 --> 02:05:31,930
(I'm going to bring out my weapon,)

3316
02:05:31,930 --> 02:05:33,260
(the thing I excel at.)

3317
02:05:33,260 --> 02:05:35,130
(Equipped with BABYZOO's signature Waacking weapon)

3318
02:05:35,130 --> 02:05:36,430
(Then I'll have hope.)

3319
02:05:36,430 --> 02:05:39,700
(To blend into the dance as much as possible.)

3320
02:05:39,700 --> 02:05:41,440
(I don't want to use it simply.)

3321
02:05:41,440 --> 02:05:43,170
(I don't want to just stand there and dance.)

3322
02:05:43,470 --> 02:05:44,580
(Grunting)

3323
02:05:45,010 --> 02:05:46,240
(I think it'll work.)

3324
02:05:46,240 --> 02:05:47,710
(I wanted to be eliminated.)

3325
02:05:48,250 --> 02:05:49,250
(But I don't think I will.)

3326
02:05:49,510 --> 02:05:50,750
(I'll kill it.)

3327
02:05:50,750 --> 02:05:52,050
(It was a matter of life and death,)

3328
02:05:52,050 --> 02:05:53,920
(so I gritted my teeth and prepared for it.)

3329
02:05:53,920 --> 02:05:55,620
(I am confident I can survive.)

3330
02:05:56,120 --> 02:05:58,360
(1 of the 3 will die.)

3331
02:05:58,360 --> 02:05:59,390
(As long as it's not me, it's okay.)

3332
02:05:59,560 --> 02:06:02,530
(A battle for survival staked on the director's reputation)

3333
02:06:02,790 --> 02:06:04,190
(4 people who spent an intense 24 hours for survival)

3334
02:06:04,190 --> 02:06:05,660
(How are these people...)

3335
02:06:05,660 --> 02:06:06,700
(at risk of elimination?)

3336
02:06:06,960 --> 02:06:08,400
(It's so good.)

3337
02:06:08,400 --> 02:06:09,530
(It feels like the final stage.)

3338
02:06:09,530 --> 02:06:11,540
(Your skill in handling the cube...)

3339
02:06:11,540 --> 02:06:13,370
(was truly impressive.)

3340
02:06:13,500 --> 02:06:15,070
(Is today really your last dance?)

3341
02:06:15,070 --> 02:06:17,010
(This is it!)

3342
02:06:17,010 --> 02:06:19,810
(It's really dramatic.)

3343
02:06:19,810 --> 02:06:21,910
(MIN JUN is on his 2nd bullet.)

3344
02:06:21,910 --> 02:06:23,410
(He's a really scary kid.)

3345
02:06:23,410 --> 02:06:24,880
(Nice!)

3346
02:06:24,880 --> 02:06:26,780
(This is the cube we envisioned.)

3347
02:06:27,250 --> 02:06:28,690
(This is what we really wanted.)

3348
02:06:28,690 --> 02:06:30,790
(It makes no sense that this was done within 24 hours.)

3349
02:06:31,060 --> 02:06:33,660
(K-pop Solo Artist Direct Mission was a team competition.)

3350
02:06:33,660 --> 02:06:35,260
(You compete for survival...)

3351
02:06:35,260 --> 02:06:37,430
(against the very partner with whom...)

3352
02:06:37,430 --> 02:06:40,260
(you once dreamed of victory and prepared for the stage.)

3353
02:06:41,570 --> 02:06:43,200
(Who is the final director...)

3354
02:06:43,200 --> 02:06:45,640
(eliminated in the 2nd Last Stage: 24H?)

3355
02:06:49,370 --> 02:06:51,940
(Shocked)

3356
02:06:51,940 --> 02:06:53,410
(This doesn't make sense.)

3357
02:06:54,180 --> 02:06:55,950
(It was such a shame.)

3358
02:06:56,750 --> 02:06:58,920
(It feels like it ended just as I was getting used to it.)

3359
02:06:58,920 --> 02:07:00,120
(I have no regrets.)

3360
02:07:00,120 --> 02:07:02,920
(I couldn't do more than this.)
